    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN115-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 2 (5 marks) Aaron works part-time as a porter at a hotel. His timesheet for three shifts he worked in January this year is shown below. Day Start time Finish time Wednesday (Australia Day holiday) 6: 30 am 1: 00 pm Thursday 11: 45 am 7: 45 pm Friday 10: 15 am 7: 15 pm The hotel pays porters $20 per hour, except for (i) hours worked after 5 pm when time-and-a-half is paid; and (ii) all hours worked on a public holiday when double time is paid. Determine Aaron's pay for the three shifts he worked.",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN115-193-3 Question 2 (5 marks) Aaron works part-time as a porter at a hotel. His timesheet for three shifts he worked in January this year is shown below. Day Start time Finish time Wednesday (Australia Day holiday) 6: 30 am 1: 00 pm Thursday 11: 45 am 7: 45 pm Friday 10: 15 am 7: 15 pm The hotel pays porters $20 per hour, except for (i) hours worked after 5 pm when time-and-a-half is paid; and (ii) all hours worked on a public holiday when double time is paid. Determine Aaron's pay for the three shifts he worked. Solution Double time on Wed: 6h 30m Time-and-a-half hours (after 5 pm) on Thurs and Fri: 2h 45m + 2h 15m = 5h Normal hours (until 5 pm) on Thurs and Fri in hours and minutes: 5ℎ 15min + 6ℎ 45min = 12h Using bonus rates, time paid, in hours: 12 + (5 × 1.5) + (6.5 × 2) = 12 + 7.5 + 13 = 32.5 Aaron's pay for three shifts: 32.5 × 20 = $650 NB Alternative methods exist, such as pay per day resulting in Wed: $260, Thurs: $187.50, Fri: $202.50, totalling $650. Specific behaviours  indicates hours worked at normal rates  indicates hours worked at time-and-a-half  indicates hours worked at double time  correctly adjusts tim",
