    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN115-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar pentagons 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾 and 𝐾𝐾′𝐿𝐿′𝑀𝑀′𝑁𝑁′𝑂𝑂′. The lengths of some of the sides are shown in centimetres. (a) Show use of a scale factor to determine the length of side 𝐿𝐿𝐿𝐿 and the length of side 𝑂𝑂′𝐾𝐾′. (3 marks) The perimeter of 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾 is 130 cm. (b) Determine the length of side 𝑂𝑂′𝑁𝑁′. (2 marks) The area of 𝐾𝐾′𝐿𝐿′𝑀𝑀′𝑁𝑁′𝑂𝑂′ is 30 cm2. (c) Determine the area of 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN115-193-3 Question 6 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar pentagons 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾 and 𝐾𝐾′𝐿𝐿′𝑀𝑀′𝑁𝑁′𝑂𝑂′. The lengths of some of the sides are shown in centimetres. (a) Show use of a scale factor to determine the length of side 𝐿𝐿𝐿𝐿 and the length of side 𝑂𝑂′𝐾𝐾′. (3 marks) The perimeter of 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾 is 130 cm. (b) Determine the length of side 𝑂𝑂′𝑁𝑁′. (2 marks) The area of 𝐾𝐾′𝐿𝐿′𝑀𝑀′𝑁𝑁′𝑂𝑂′ is 30 cm2. (c) Determine the area of 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾. (2 marks) Solution Scale factor: 𝑁𝑁𝑁𝑁 𝑁𝑁′𝑀𝑀′ = 30 6 = 5 𝐿𝐿𝐿𝐿= 5 × 5 = 25 cm, 𝑂𝑂′𝐾𝐾′ = 20 ÷ 5 = 4 cm Specific behaviours  calculates scale factor (either 5 or 1 5 ൗ)  length of 𝐿𝐿𝐿𝐿  length of 𝑂𝑂′𝐾𝐾′ Solution 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾= 8 × 5 = 40 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 130 −(20 + 40 + 25 + 30) = 130 −115 = 15 𝑂𝑂′𝑁𝑁′ = 15 ÷ 5 = 3 cm 𝑃𝑃𝐾𝐾′𝐿𝐿′𝑀𝑀′𝑁𝑁′𝑂𝑂′ = 130 ÷ 5 = 26 𝑂𝑂′𝑁𝑁′ = 26 −(8 + 5 + 6 + 4) = 26 −23 = 3 cm Specific behaviours  uses scale factor to obtain 𝐾𝐾𝐾𝐾 or small pentagon perimeter  correct side length Solution Area scale factor is 5 × 5 = 25 Area = 30 × 25 = 750 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct area scale factor  uses area scale factor to obtain area",
