    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN115-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (8 marks) The sketch diagram (not drawn to scale) shows a plot of land bounded by six straight sides. The length of each side is shown in metres. (a) A fence that costs $30 per metre is to be erected around the perimeter of plot. Determine the total cost of fencing. (3 marks) (b) Once the fence is in place, the plot is to be treated with weedkiller at a rate of 10 mL per square metre. The weedkiller is sold in 3 litre containers. Determine, with justification, the number of containers of weedkiller required. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN115-193-3 Question 7 (8 marks) The sketch diagram (not drawn to scale) shows a plot of land bounded by six straight sides. The length of each side is shown in metres. (a) A fence that costs $30 per metre is to be erected around the perimeter of plot. Determine the total cost of fencing. (3 marks) (b) Once the fence is in place, the plot is to be treated with weedkiller at a rate of 10 mL per square metre. The weedkiller is sold in 3 litre containers. Determine, with justification, the number of containers of weedkiller required. (5 marks) Solution 𝑃𝑃= 50 + 41 + 39 + 20 + 20 + 20 = 190 m 𝐶𝐶= 190 × 30 = $5700 Specific behaviours  indicates correct calculation for perimeter  indicates correct calculation for total cost  correct total cost Solution Rectangle: 𝐴𝐴𝑅𝑅= 50 × 40 = 2000 Square: 𝐴𝐴𝑆𝑆= 20 × 20 = 400 Triangle: 𝐴𝐴𝑇𝑇= 1 2 × 9 × 40 = 180 Total area: 𝐴𝐴= 2000 −400 + 180 = 1780 m2 Litres of weedkiller: 1780 × 0.01 = 17.8 L and so 6 containers will be required as 6x3=18 >17.8 Specific behaviours  correctly partitions plot into suitable composite areas  calculates all composite areas correctly  calculates total area  calc",
