    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN115-193-4 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has twelve questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 8 (6 marks) The diagram, not to scale, shows a right triangular prism with a length of 9.0 cm. The lengths of some of the edges are shown on the diagram in centimetres. (a) Determine the height ℎ of the right triangle. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (4 marks) Solution ℎ2 = 7.32 −4.82 = 30.25 ℎ= 5.5 cm Specific behaviours  shows correct use of Pythagoras' Theorem  correct height Solution Area of triangular end: 𝐴𝐴1 = 1 2 × 4.8 × 5.5 = 13.2 cm2 Area of rectangles: 𝐴𝐴2 = 9.0 × (4.8 + 5.5 + 7.3) = 9 × 17.6 = 158.4 cm2 Total surface area: 𝐴𝐴= 2 × 13.2 + 158.4 = 184.8 cm2 Specific behaviours  calculates area of one triangle  calculates area of at least one rectangle  indicates sum of all five faces  correct total surface area",
