    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN115-193-4 Question 12 (8 marks) A sketch plan of a twin bedroom is shown, not drawn to scale. The internal and external dimensions of the room are shown on the sketch in millimetres. (a) State the internal length and width of the room in metres. (2 marks) The floor of the interior of the room is to be carpeted using a 10 m long roll of carpet that is 1.8 m wide. No more than four cuts can be made to the carpet. (b) Sketch a diagram to show how the carpet could be laid on the floor, showing the dimensions of each piece of carpet cut from the roll. (3 marks) (c) After the floor has been carpeted, some of the roll is left over. Determine what percentage of the area of the roll is left over. (3 marks) Solution 𝑙𝑙= 4.5 m, 𝑤𝑤= 3.4 m Specific behaviours  uses correct dimensions (𝑙𝑙 and 𝑤𝑤 interchangeable)  writes dimensions in metres Solution Area of roll: 𝐴𝐴𝑅𝑅= 10 × 1.8 = 18.0 m2 Area of floor: 𝐴𝐴𝐹𝐹= 4.5 × 3.4 = 15.3 m2 Area left over: 𝐴𝐴= 18.0 −15.3 = 2.7 m2 Percentage left over: 2.7 ÷ 18 = 15% Specific behaviours  areas of floor and roll  shows correct calculation for percentage  evaluates percentage (correct to nearest whol",
