    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN115-193-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (8 marks) The diagram (not to scale) shows a fabric panel used in the construction of a kite. The panel consists of a 230° sector of a circle with centre 𝑂𝑂 and radius 50 cm, and quadrilateral 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 in which 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 108 cm. (a) Calculate the area of the sector. (2 marks) (b) Hence determine the total area of the fabric panel. (3 marks) (c) The panel is to be edged with tape. Calculate the length of tape required. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN115-193-4 Question 15 (8 marks) The diagram (not to scale) shows a fabric panel used in the construction of a kite. The panel consists of a 230° sector of a circle with centre 𝑂𝑂 and radius 50 cm, and quadrilateral 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 in which 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 108 cm. (a) Calculate the area of the sector. (2 marks) (b) Hence determine the total area of the fabric panel. (3 marks) (c) The panel is to be edged with tape. Calculate the length of tape required. (3 marks) Solution Perimeter of sector, 𝑃𝑃: 𝑃𝑃= 230 360 × 2 × 𝜋𝜋× 50 = 200.71 cm Total length of tape, 𝐿𝐿: 𝐿𝐿= 200.71 + 2 × 108 = 416.71 cm Specific behaviours  indicates correct method for sector perimeter  calculates sector perimeter  calculates total length of tape Solution Quadrilateral can be split into two right triangles. Area of a triangle: 𝐴𝐴= 1 2 × 50 × 108 = 2700 cm2 Hence total area is sector plus two triangles: 𝐴𝐴= 5017.82 + 2 × 2700 = 10 417. 82 cm2 Specific behaviours  splits quadrilateral into two right-triangles  area of one right-triangle  calculates total area Solution 𝐴𝐴= 230 360 × 𝜋𝜋× 502 = 5017.82 cm2 (𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 5018 cm2) Specific behaviours  uses appr",
