    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN115-193-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 18 (9 marks) A woodturner takes a solid cylindrical wooden pole of length 66 cm and radius 8 cm and uses a machine to reduce the radius of the middle third of the pole by 30%, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). (a) Explaining your method, calculate the volume of wood removed by the machine. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN115-193-4 Question 18 (9 marks) A woodturner takes a solid cylindrical wooden pole of length 66 cm and radius 8 cm and uses a machine to reduce the radius of the middle third of the pole by 30%, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). (a) Explaining your method, calculate the volume of wood removed by the machine. (4 marks) Solution Volume removed will be difference in volume of middle section of pole as a cylinder with height of 66 ÷ 3 = 22 cm and initial radius of 8 cm and final radius of 8 × 0.7 = 5.6 cm. 𝑉𝑉1 = 𝜋𝜋× 82 × 22 = 4423 cm3 𝑉𝑉2 = 𝜋𝜋× 5.62 × 22 = 2167 cm3 Hence volume removed is 4423 −2167 = 2256 cm3. Specific behaviours  explanation of method or describes each step  correctly calculates volume of original cylinder 𝑉𝑉1  correctly calculates volume of final cylinder 𝑉𝑉2  correctly calculates volume removed",
