    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN115-193-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (b) Explaining your method, determine the total surface area of the remaining object. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN115-193-4 (b) Explaining your method, determine the total surface area of the remaining object. (5 marks) Solution TSA of one large end cylinder: 𝐴𝐴1 = 2𝜋𝜋× 82 + 2𝜋𝜋× 8 × 22 = 402.1 + 1105.84 = 1508 cm2 Area of curved surface of small middle cylinder: 𝐴𝐴2 = 2𝜋𝜋× 5.6 × 22 = 774 cm2 Area of one circular end of small middle cylinder: 𝐴𝐴3 = 𝜋𝜋× 5.62 = 98.5 cm2 TSA of remaining object: 𝐴𝐴= 2𝐴𝐴1 + 𝐴𝐴2 −2𝐴𝐴3 = 3016 + 774 −197 = 3593 cm2 OR TSA of two large cylinders: 𝐴𝐴1 = 2𝜋𝜋× 82 + (2𝜋𝜋× 8 × 22) × 2 = 402.1 + 2211.68 = 2613.78 cm2 Area of curved surface of small middle cylinder: 𝐴𝐴2 = 2𝜋𝜋× 5.6 × 22 = 774 cm2 Area of two ‘donuts’ joining small and large cylinder: 𝐴𝐴3 = (𝜋𝜋× 82 −𝜋𝜋× 5.62) × 2 = 205.08 cm2 TSA of remaining object: 𝐴𝐴= 𝐴𝐴1 + 𝐴𝐴2 + 𝐴𝐴3 = 2614 + 774 −205 = 3593 cm2 Many possible methods. Specific behaviours  explanation of method or describes each step  correctly calculates TSA of larger cylinder 𝐴𝐴1  correctly calculates curved surface of smaller cylinder 𝐴𝐴2  correctly calculates area of smaller cylinder ends 𝐴𝐴3  correct TSA of object",
