    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN115-193-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (9 marks) When a person needs to save an amount of 𝐴𝐴 dollars by making 𝑁𝑁 monthly deposits into an account with an interest at a rate of 𝑅𝑅% p.a. compounded monthly, then the deposit that they must make each month, 𝐷𝐷 dollars, is given by the formula 𝐷𝐷= 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 𝑘𝑘 , where 𝑖𝑖= 𝑅𝑅 1200 and 𝑘𝑘= (1 + 𝑖𝑖)𝑁𝑁−1. (a) Lydia will make monthly deposits into a savings account with an interest rate of 6.96% p.a. compounded monthly and wants to save $18 000 to buy a used car in two years' time. (i) How many monthly deposits will she make in two years? (1 mark) (ii) Determine the amount that she must deposit each month. Hint: Do not round the value of 𝑘𝑘 in your calculations. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN115-193-4 Question 19 (9 marks) When a person needs to save an amount of 𝐴𝐴 dollars by making 𝑁𝑁 monthly deposits into an account with an interest at a rate of 𝑅𝑅% p.a. compounded monthly, then the deposit that they must make each month, 𝐷𝐷 dollars, is given by the formula 𝐷𝐷= 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 𝑘𝑘 , where 𝑖𝑖= 𝑅𝑅 1200 and 𝑘𝑘= (1 + 𝑖𝑖)𝑁𝑁−1. (a) Lydia will make monthly deposits into a savings account with an interest rate of 6.96% p.a. compounded monthly and wants to save $18 000 to buy a used car in two years' time. (i) How many monthly deposits will she make in two years? (1 mark) (ii) Determine the amount that she must deposit each month. Hint: Do not round the value of 𝑘𝑘 in your calculations. (4 marks) Solution 𝑖𝑖= 6.96 1200 = 0.0058, 𝑘𝑘= (1 + 0.0058)24 −1 = 0.14889 𝐷𝐷= 18 000 × 0.0058 0.14889 = 701.18 Hence the monthly deposit is $701.18. Specific behaviours  calculates value of 𝑖𝑖  calculates value of 𝑘𝑘  indicates expression for 𝐷𝐷  correctly evaluates 𝐷𝐷 Solution 𝑁𝑁= 12 × 2 = 24 deposits Specific behaviours  correct number",
