    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.3 · Shape and measurement",
    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 8 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 6 (8 marks) (a) I think of a number, triple it, then subtract the result from 20. The result is 8 more than the number I first thought of. By writing an equation and solving it, determine the number. (2 marks) (b) The length of a rectangle is 3cm more than double its width. The rectangle’s perimeter is 66cm. By first writing an equation and solving it to find the rectangle’s width, determine the area of the rectangle. (3 marks) (c) June is 42 years older than Tim. In ten years time their ages will be such that June will be twice as old as Tim. By writing an equation and solving it, determine how old June is now. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN245-093-2 Question 6 (6 marks) (a) I think of a number, triple it, then subtract the result from 20. The result is 8 more than the number I first thought of. By writing an equation and solving it, determine the number. (2 marks) (b) The length of a rectangle is 3cm more than double its width. The rectangle’s perimeter is 66cm. By first writing an equation and solving it to find the rectangle’s width, determine the area of the rectangle. (3 marks) (c) June is 42 years older than Tim. In ten years time their ages will be such that June will be twice as old as Tim. By writing an equation and solving it, determine how old June is now. (3 marks) Solution 20 −3𝑥= 𝑥+ 8 OR 20 −3𝑥−8 = 𝑥 𝑥= 3 Specific behaviours ✓ writes correct equation ✓ solves equation correctly Solution 2𝑥+ 2(2𝑥+ 3) = 66 𝑥= 10 Width =10, therefore length=23, so area is 230cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ writes correct equation ✓ solves equation correctly ✓ determines area Solution 2(𝑥+ 10) = 𝑥+ 42 + 10 𝑥= 32 Tim is currently 32, therefore June is currently 74. Specific behaviours ✓ writes correct equation ✓ solves equation correctly ✓ determines June’s current age",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-kennedy-2017-yr11-apps-u1-s1-e1169c2413-p008-question-440330bb9e.jpg",
