    "pageNumber": 9,
    "topicId": "a13",
    "topicCode": "1.3",
    "topicName": "Shape and measurement",
    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.3 · Shape and measurement",
    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions Question 7 (8 marks) (a) Write the scale 5 mm : 30 cm as a ratio in simplest form and without units. (2 marks) (b) Three similar triangles are shown below, although they are not drawn to the same scale. Some of the side lengths, in centimetres, are shown. Determine the lengths 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑. (4 marks) (c) A student used a map drawn to a scale of 1: 10 000 to plan a walk. The length of the walk on the map was 5.5 cm. State, with reasoning, whether the length of the walk was more than a kilometre. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN245-093-2 Question 7 (8 marks) (a) Write the scale 5 mm : 30 cm as a ratio in simplest form and without units. (2 marks) (b) Three similar triangles are shown below, although they are not drawn to the same scale. Some of the side lengths, in centimetres, are shown. Determine the lengths 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑. (4 marks) (c) A student used a map drawn to a scale of 1: 10 000 to plan a walk. The length of the walk on the map was 5.5 cm. State, with reasoning, whether the length of the walk was more than a kilometre. (2 marks) Solution No, walk was less than 1 km. 5.5×10000 100 = 550 m Specific behaviours ✓ states less ✓ states walk is 550 m long. Solution 5 mm : 300 mm = 1 ∶60 Specific behaviours ✓ converts measurements to same unit ✓ simplifies ratio Solution Lengths of LH triangle are 12 3 = 4 × middle triangle and 24 12 = 2 × RH triangle. 𝑎= 4 × 4 = 16 cm, 𝑏= 24 4 = 6 cm, 𝑐= 12 2 = 6 cm and 𝑑= 16 2 = 8 cm. Specific behaviours ✓ uses ratio of lengths of LH and middle triangles ✓ determines 𝑎 and 𝑏 ✓ uses ratios of lengths of RH and another triangle ✓",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-kennedy-2017-yr11-apps-u1-s1-e1169c2413-p009-question-c43eacb75b.jpg",
