    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-3 Question 9 (7 marks) The diagram below shows the dimensions of a paved area (shaded) that is adjacent to a circular pool of radius 4 m. (a) Determine the length of the perimeter of the paved area. (3 marks) (b) Determine the area of the paving. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-4 Question 9 (7 marks) The diagram below shows the dimensions of a paved area (shaded) that is adjacent to a circular pool of radius 4 m. (a) Determine the length of the perimeter of the paved area. (3 marks) (b) Determine the area of the paving. (4 marks) Solution Rectangles: 5 × 10 + 6 × 7 = 50 + 42 = 92 Quadrant: 𝜋× 42 ÷ 4 = 12.57 Area: 92 −12.57 = 79.43 m2 Specific behaviours ✓ splits into composite rectangles ✓ calculates area of rectangles ✓ calculates area of quadrant ✓calculates area of surface Solution Missing lengths: 12 −5 −4 = 3 m and 10 −4 −4 = 2 m Quadrant: 2 × 𝜋× 4 ÷ 4 = 25.13 ÷ 4 = 6.28 Perimeter: 6.28 + 2 + 12 + 10 + 5 + 4 + 3 = 42.28 m Specific behaviours ✓ determines missing lengths ✓ determines quadrant length ✓ determines perimeter",
