    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-093-3 Question 10 (6 marks) A tradesman uses the spreadsheet below to quote customers the price of a job ($𝑃), depending on the number of days the job will take (𝐷) and how many labourers (𝐿) will be required. The prices all include GST at 10%. The formula used in the spreadsheet is 𝑃= 220𝐷+ 85𝐿+ 150. Job prices ($𝑃) Length of job in days (𝐷) 1 2 3 4 Number of labourers (𝐿) 1 455 675 𝐴 1115 2 540 760 980 1200 3 625 𝐵 1065 1285 (a) For a job lasting four days and requiring three labourers: (i) state the price the tradesman will quote. (1 mark) (ii) calculate how much GST is included in the quote. (1 mark) (b) Determine the values of 𝐴 and 𝐵 in the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) The tradesman quoted a price of $1 895 for a job lasting 6 days. Determine the number of labourers required for this job. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-093-4 Question 10 (6 marks) A tradesman uses the spreadsheet below to quote customers the price of a job ($𝑃), depending on the number of days the job will take (𝐷) and how many labourers (𝐿) will be required. The prices all include GST at 10%. The formula used in the spreadsheet is 𝑃= 220𝐷+ 85𝐿+ 150. Job prices ($𝑃) Length of job in days (𝐷) 1 2 3 4 Number of labourers (𝐿) 1 455 675 𝐴 1115 2 540 760 980 1200 3 625 𝐵 1065 1285 (a) For a job lasting four days and requiring three labourers: (i) state the price the tradesman will quote. (1 mark) (ii) calculate how much GST is included in the quote. (1 mark) (b) Determine the values of 𝐴 and 𝐵 in the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) The tradesman quoted a price of $1 895 for a job lasting 6 days. Determine the number of labourers required for this job. (2 marks) Solution $1285 Specific behaviours ✓ states price Solution 1285 ÷ 11 = $116.82 Specific behaviours ✓calculates GST Solution 1895 = 220 × 6 + 85 × 𝐿+ 150 𝐿= 5 labourers Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes ✓ states number of labourers Solution 𝐴= 220 × 3 + 85 × 1 + 150 = $895 𝐵= 220 × 2 + 85 × 3 + 150 = $845 Specific behaviours",
