    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-093-3 (b) An 18-year-old person who lives independently qualifies for this pension and is also paid $17.75 an hour for 20 hours work each week. Determine the fortnightly sum of earnings and pension for this person. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-093-4 (b) An 18-year-old person who lives independently qualifies for this pension and is also paid $17.75 an hour for 20 hours work each week. Determine the fortnightly sum of earnings and pension for this person. (4 marks) Solution Fortnightly pension: $562.20 Fortnightly earnings: 2 × 20 × 17.75 = $710 Deduction: (710 −164) × 0.5 = 546 × 0.5 = $273 Sum: 562.20 + 710 −273 = $999.20 Specific behaviours ✓ correct pension rate ✓ correct fortnightly earnings ✓ correct deduction ✓ t t",
