    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-3 Question 12 (8 marks) A playground has the shape of quadrilateral 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 shown below, where the lengths of 𝐴𝐵, 𝐵𝐶 and 𝐶𝐷 are 36 m, 77 m and 13 m respectively. Angles 𝐵 and 𝐷 are both 90°. (a) Determine the lengths of (i) diagonal 𝐴𝐶. (2 marks) (ii) side 𝐴𝐷. (2 marks) A square playground 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 has the same area as the playground 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (b) Determine the area of playground 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (2 marks) (c) Determine the perimeter of the square playground 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-4 Question 12 (8 marks) A playground has the shape of quadrilateral 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 shown below, where the lengths of 𝐴𝐵, 𝐵𝐶 and 𝐶𝐷 are 36 m, 77 m and 13 m respectively. Angles 𝐵 and 𝐷 are both 90°. (a) Determine the lengths of (i) diagonal 𝐴𝐶. (2 marks) (ii) side 𝐴𝐷. (2 marks) A square playground 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 has the same area as the playground 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (b) Determine the area of playground 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (2 marks) (c) Determine the perimeter of the square playground 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (2 marks) Solution 𝐿= √1932 = 43.95 m 𝑃= 4 × 43.95 = 175.8 ≈176 m Specific behaviours ✓ determines side of square ✓ calculates perimeter (any value that rounds to 176) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐵𝐶= 1 2 × 36 × 77 = 1386 𝐴𝐴𝐶𝐷= 1 2 × 13 × 84 = 546 𝐴= 1386 + 546 = 1932 m2 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates areas of right triangles ✓ calculates total area Solution √852 −132 = √7056 = 84 m Specific behaviours ✓ uses Pythagoras' theorem ✓ determines length Solution √362 + 772 = √7225 = 85 m Specific behaviours ✓ uses Pythagoras' theorem ✓ determines length",
