    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-3 Question 14 (9 marks) The table below shows the budget used by a young person for running their medium-sized car last year. Item Average Weekly Amount Depreciation $72.50 Loan Repayment $55.25 Registration $7.75 Insurance $23.40 Fuel $18.30 Tyres $2.65 Servicing $21.90 (a) Determine the (i) weekly total of these amounts. (1 mark) (ii) the average monthly amount required to run the car, assuming there were exactly 52 weeks last year. (2 marks) For this year, the young person expects the average weekly amount for depreciation to fall by 10%, the loan repayment to remain unchanged and all other amounts to increase by 5%. (b) Determine the new average weekly amounts for (i) depreciation. (1 mark) (ii) insurance. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-4 Question 14 (9 marks) The table below shows the budget used by a young person for running their medium-sized car last year. Item Average Weekly Amount Depreciation $72.50 Loan Repayment $55.25 Registration $7.75 Insurance $23.40 Fuel $18.30 Tyres $2.65 Servicing $21.90 (a) Determine the (i) weekly total of these amounts. (1 mark) (ii) the average monthly amount required to run the car, assuming there were exactly 52 weeks last year. (2 marks) For this year, the young person expects the average weekly amount for depreciation to fall by 10%, the loan repayment to remain unchanged and all other amounts to increase by 5%. (b) Determine the new average weekly amounts for (i) depreciation. (1 mark) (ii) insurance. (1 mark) Solution 72.50 × 0.90 = 65.25 Specific behaviours ✓ decreases by 10% Solution 23.40 × 1.05 = $24.57 Specific behaviours ✓ increases by 5% Solution 201.75 × 52 = $10491 10491 ÷ 12 = $874.25 Specific behaviours ✓ converts to annual amount ✓ converts to monthly amount Solution Total is $201.75 Specific behaviours ✓ sums amounts",
