    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-3 Question 20 (10 marks) A triangular prism 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸𝐹 has a square base 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 of side 36 cm, two triangular ends and two sloping rectangular faces measuring 36 cm by 30 cm, as shown in the diagram below. 𝐺 and 𝐻 are the midpoints of sides 𝐴𝐷 and 𝐵𝐶 respectively. (a) Calculate the length of the diagonal 𝐹𝐷 in rectangle 𝐶𝐷𝐸𝐹. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length 𝐸𝐺. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the area of triangle 𝐴𝐸𝐷. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-093-4 Question 20 (10 marks) A triangular prism 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸𝐹 has a square base 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 of side 36 cm, two triangular ends and two sloping rectangular faces measuring 36 cm by 30 cm, as shown in the diagram below. 𝐺 and 𝐻 are the midpoints of sides 𝐴𝐷 and 𝐵𝐶 respectively. (a) Calculate the length of the diagonal 𝐹𝐷 in rectangle 𝐶𝐷𝐸𝐹. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length 𝐸𝐺. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the area of triangle 𝐴𝐸𝐷. (2 marks) Solution 0.5 × 36 × 24 = 432 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ uses half base times height (or Herons rule) ✓ calculates area Solution √302 −182 = 24 cm Specific behaviours ✓ uses Pythagoras' theorem, halving 𝐴𝐷 ✓ calculates length Solution √362 + 302 ≈46.9 cm Specific behaviours ✓ uses Pythagoras' theorem ✓ calculates length",
