    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.1 · Consumer arithmetic",
    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-1 Question 5 (6 marks) Hockey teams A and B had each played 21 games in a league. Team A had won 11, lost 4 and drawn the remainder of its games. In total, the two teams had won 21 and drawn 14 games. (a) Show this information in a 2 × 3 matrix 𝐻, with columns ordered win, lose, draw and rows ordered team A and team B. (2 marks) (b) Each team gains 3 points for a win, 1 point for a draw and no points for a loss. Show this information in matrix 𝑃 that can be multiplied by matrix 𝐻. (1 mark) (c) Calculate 𝐻× 𝑃 and state which team is leading the other in the league. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-2 Question 5 (6 marks) Hockey teams A and B had each played 21 games in a league. Team A had won 11, lost 4 and drawn the remainder of its games. In total, the two teams had won 21 and drawn 14 games. (a) Show this information in a 2 × 3 matrix 𝐻, with columns ordered win, lose, draw and rows ordered team A and team B. (2 marks) (b) Each team gains 3 points for a win, 1 point for a draw and no points for a loss. Show this information in matrix 𝑃 that can be multiplied by matrix 𝐻. (1 mark) (c) Calculate 𝐻× 𝑃 and state which team is leading the other in the league. (3 marks) Solution 𝐻= [11 4 6 10 3 8] Specific behaviours ✓ one row correct ✓ correct matrix Solution 𝑃= [ 3 0 1 ] Specific behaviours ✓ correct matrix Solution [11 4 6 10 3 8] × [ 3 0 1 ] = [39 38] Team A is leading team B. Specific behaviours ✓ obtains a 2 × 1 product ✓ correct product ✓ correct interpretation",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-waep-2019-yr11-apps-u1-s1-3a41e9deb8-p007-question-48ede71f27.jpg",
