    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-3 Question 10 (7 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑓 given that 𝑓= 1 𝑑 and 𝑑= 1 𝑑1 + 1 𝑑2 when 𝑑1 = 0.52 and 𝑑2 = 2.86. (2 marks) (b) The future value, 𝐹, of an annuity can be calculated using the formula below. 𝐹= 𝐶 𝑟((1 + 𝑟 𝑛) 𝑛𝑡 −1) Consider an annuity with values 𝐶= $2 500, 𝑟= 0.035, 𝑛= 4 and 𝑡= 5. (i) Calculate the future value, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (3 marks) (ii) Calculate the change in 𝐹 when the value of 𝑛 is changed from 4 to 12. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-4 Question 10 (7 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑓 given that 𝑓= 1 𝑑 and 𝑑= 1 𝑑1 + 1 𝑑2 when 𝑑1 = 0.52 and 𝑑2 = 2.86. (2 marks) (b) The future value, 𝐹, of an annuity can be calculated using the formula below. 𝐹= 𝐶 𝑟((1 + 𝑟 𝑛) 𝑛𝑡 −1) Consider an annuity with values 𝐶= $2 500, 𝑟= 0.035, 𝑛= 4 and 𝑡= 5. (i) Calculate the future value, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (3 marks) (ii) Calculate the change in 𝐹 when the value of 𝑛 is changed from 4 to 12. (2 marks) Solution 𝐹= 2500 0.035 ((1 + 0.035 4 ) 4×5 −1) 𝐹= 13595.70 𝐹≈$13 596 (nearest $) Specific behaviours ✓ evidence of correct substitution ✓ calculates 𝐹 ✓ value to nearest dollar Solution 𝑑= 1 0.52 + 1 2.86 = 25 11 = 2. 27 ̅̅̅̅ 𝑓= 1 ÷ 25 11 = 0.44 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value of 𝑑 ✓ correct answer Solution 𝐹≈$13 639 (nearest $) Increase of 13 639 −13 596 = $43 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates 𝐹 ✓ correct increase",
