    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-3 Question 12 (6 marks) A researcher at a weather station uses the following formula to calculate 𝐴, the absolute humidity of the air, where 𝐻 is the relative humidity and 𝑇 is the air temperature. 𝐴= 12.7 × 𝐻× (1.07)𝑇 𝑇+ 273 (a) Calculate 𝐴 when 𝐻= 55 and 𝑇= 30. (2 marks) The formula for 𝐴 was used to create the spreadsheet below for various values of 𝐻 and 𝑇. (b) Calculate the value of the entries 𝑃 and 𝑄 shown in the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) One of the entries in the spreadsheet is incorrect. State the value of 𝑇 and the value of 𝐻 for the cell in which the incorrect value lies and calculate the correct value of 𝐴. (2 marks) 𝐴 𝐻 40 50 60 70 80 𝑇 −10 0.98 1.23 1.47 1.72 𝑃 0 1.86 2.33 2.79 3.75 3.72 10 3.53 4.41 5.30 6.18 7.06 20 𝑄 8.39 10.06 11.74 13.42",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-4 Question 12 (6 marks) A researcher at a weather station uses the following formula to calculate 𝐴, the absolute humidity of the air, where 𝐻 is the relative humidity and 𝑇 is the air temperature. 𝐴= 12.7 × 𝐻× (1.07)𝑇 𝑇+ 273 (a) Calculate 𝐴 when 𝐻= 55 and 𝑇= 30. (2 marks) The formula for 𝐴 was used to create the spreadsheet below for various values of 𝐻 and 𝑇. (b) Calculate the value of the entries 𝑃 and 𝑄 shown in the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) One of the entries in the spreadsheet is incorrect. State the value of 𝑇 and the value of 𝐻 for the cell in which the incorrect value lies and calculate the correct value of 𝐴. (2 marks) 𝐴 𝐻 40 50 60 70 80 𝑇 −10 0.98 1.23 1.47 1.72 𝑃 0 1.86 2.33 2.79 3.75 3.72 10 3.53 4.41 5.30 6.18 7.06 20 𝑄 8.39 10.06 11.74 13.42 Solution 𝐴= 12.7 × 55 × (1.07)30 30 + 273 = 17.55 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly ✓ correct value Solution 𝑇= 0, 𝐻= 70 𝐴= 3.26 Specific behaviours ✓ correct values of 𝑇 and 𝐻 ✓ correct value of 𝐴 Solution 𝑃= 1.96 𝑄= 6.71 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑃 ✓ value of 𝑄",
