    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-3 Question 13 (6 marks) A bakery sells a specialty cake in the shape of a square-based pyramid. The sides of the square are all 32 cm and the vertex of the pyramid, 𝑉, lies 21 cm directly above the centre of the square base, 𝐶. The mid-point of one of the sides of the square is 𝑀. (a) Determine the volume of the cake. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the length 𝑉𝑀. (2 marks) (c) The four triangular faces are iced at a cost of 1.4 cents per square cm. Determine the cost of icing the cake, in dollars and cents. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-4 Question 13 (6 marks) A bakery sells a specialty cake in the shape of a square-based pyramid. The sides of the square are all 32 cm and the vertex of the pyramid, 𝑉, lies 21 cm directly above the centre of the square base, 𝐶. The mid-point of one of the sides of the square is 𝑀. (a) Determine the volume of the cake. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the length 𝑉𝑀. (2 marks) (c) The four triangular faces are iced at a cost of 1.4 cents per square cm. Determine the cost of icing the cake, in dollars and cents. (2 marks) Solution 𝑀𝐶= 32 ÷ 2 = 16 𝑉𝑀= √212 + 162 = 26.4 cm Specific behaviours ✓ indicates lengths 𝑀𝐶 and 𝑉𝐶 ✓ correct distance Solution 𝐴= 4 × 1 2 × 32 × 26.4 = 1689.6 𝐶= 1689.6 × 0.014 = $23.65 Specific behaviours ✓ correct TSA ✓ correct cost Solution 𝑉= 1 3(32 × 32) × 21 = 7 168 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates area of base ✓ correct volume",
