    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-3 Question 17 (12 marks) A spreadsheet to track a monthly car budget is shown below, with all amounts in dollars. The figures for months 1, 2 and 3 show the actual expenditure for each item. Item Monthly Budget Month 1 Month 2 Month 3 3-Month Total Loan payment 405 405 405 405 1215 Insurance 225 225 225 225 𝑅 Maintenance 108 0 458 45 503 Fuel 162 215 174 𝑄 582 Total 𝑃 845 1262 868 𝑆 (a) Determine the values of 𝑃, 𝑄, 𝑅 and 𝑆 in the spreadsheet. (3 marks) (b) A motoring organisation recommends allocating no more than 15% of a person's monthly income to running a car. Would a person on a salary of $67 500 pa and using the total monthly budget figure above meet this target? Justify your answer. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-133-4 Question 17 (12 marks) A spreadsheet to track a monthly car budget is shown below, with all amounts in dollars. The figures for months 1, 2 and 3 show the actual expenditure for each item. Item Monthly Budget Month 1 Month 2 Month 3 3-Month Total Loan payment 405 405 405 405 1215 Insurance 225 225 225 225 𝑅 Maintenance 108 0 458 45 503 Fuel 162 215 174 𝑄 582 Total 𝑃 845 1262 858 𝑆 (a) Determine the values of 𝑃, 𝑄, 𝑅 and 𝑆 in the spreadsheet. (3 marks) (b) A motoring organisation recommends allocating no more than 15% of a person's monthly income to running a car. Would a person on a salary of $67 500 pa and using the total monthly budget figure above meet this target? Justify your answer. (3 marks) Solution 𝑃= 900 𝑄= 582 −(215 + 174) = 193 𝑅= 3 × 225 = 675 𝑆= 2 975 Specific behaviours ✓ one correct value ✓ at least 3 correct values ✓ all correct values Solution 67500 ÷ 12 = 5625 Target: 5625 × 0.15 = $843.75 Since the budget total is $900 but the recommended maximum is only $843.75, they do not meet the target. Specific behaviours ✓ calculates monthly salary ✓ calculates correct percentage ✓ explains why they do no",
