    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-3 (c) Over the three months shown, the total actual expenditure for two items exceeded their budgeted figures. (i) Which items were these? (1 mark) (ii) Determine which of these two items exceeded their budgeted figure by the largest percentage. (3 marks) (d) The monthly budget figure for insurance includes a 10% tax. Determine the cost of the insurance without this tax. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-4 (c) Over the three months shown, the total actual expenditure for two items exceeded their budgeted figures. (i) Which items were these? (1 mark) (ii) Determine which of these two items exceeded their budgeted figure by the largest percentage. (3 marks) (d) The monthly budget figure for insurance includes a 10% tax. Determine the cost of the insurance without this tax. (2 marks) Solution Maintenance: 503 −3(108) = 503 −324 = 179 179 324 × 100 = 55% Fuel: 582 −3(162) = 582 −486 = 96 96 486 × 100 = 20% Maintenance exceeded by the largest percentage. Specific behaviours ✓ % figure for maintenance ✓ % figure for fuel ✓ states correct item Solution 225 ÷ 1.10 = $204.55 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates appropriate method ✓ correct cost, to nearest cent Solution Maintenance and fuel Specific behaviours ✓ correct items",
