    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-3 Question 19 (8 marks) A right-triangular prism has dimensions shown in the diagram below. (a) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) (b) An eighth-size model is made of the prism, i.e. using a scale of 1: 8. Calculate the total surface area of this model. (2 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the original prism. (1 mark) (d) Another scale model is made of the prism, so that the dimensions of the sloping face are now 3.6 cm by 4 cm. Calculate the volume of this scale model. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN245-133-4 Question 19 (8 marks) A right-triangular prism has dimensions shown in the diagram below. (a) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) (b) An eighth-size model is made of the prism, i.e. using a scale of 1: 8. Calculate the total surface area of this model. (2 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the original prism. (1 mark) (d) Another scale model is made of the prism, so that the dimensions of the sloping face are now 3.6 cm by 4 cm. Calculate the volume of this scale model. (2 marks) Solution Volume: 1 2 × 16 × 12 × 18 = 1 728 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ correct volume Solution Area scale factor: ( 1 8) 2 = 1 64 Area: 1056 × 1 64 = 16.5 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates area scale factor ✓ correct area Solution Triangular ends: 2 × 1 2 × 16 × 12 = 192 Rectangles: 18 × (12 + 16 + 20) = 864 TSA: 192 + 864 = 1 056 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates area of triangle ✓ indicates area of rectangle ✓ correct TSA Solution Scale factor: 4 20 = 1 5. Volume sf ( 1 5) 3 = 1 125 Volume: 1728 × 1 125 = 13.824 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates scale factor for length and volume ✓ correct volume",
