    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.3 · Shape and measurement",
    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN245-133-3 Question 21 (8 marks) The washer shown below is made of plastic and has an internal radius of 9 mm, an external radius of 23 mm and is 4 mm thick. (a) The plastic used to make the washers costs 75 cents per litre. Given that one litre is 1 000 cubic centimetres, determine the cost of making 5 000 of the washers. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the total surface area of one washer, giving your answer in mm2. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN245-133-4 Question 21 (8 marks) The washer shown below is made of plastic and has an internal radius of 9 mm, an external radius of 23 mm and is 4 mm thick. (a) The plastic used to make the washers costs 75 cents per litre. Given that one litre is 1 000 cubic centimetres, determine the cost of making 5 000 of the washers. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the total surface area of one washer, giving your answer in mm2. (4 marks) Solution Outer volume: 𝜋× 2.32 × 0.4 = 6.648 Inner volume: 𝜋× 0.92 × 0.4 = 1.018 Total volume: (6.648 −1.018) × 5000 = 5.63 × 5000 = 28150 Cost: 28150 ÷ 1000 × 0.75 = $21.11 Specific behaviours ✓ outer volume ✓ inner volume ✓ volume of all washers ✓ correct cost Solution Outer cylinder: 𝐴1 = 2𝜋(23)2 + 2𝜋(23)(4) = 3902 Inner circles: 𝐴2 = 2𝜋(9)2 = 509 Inner walls: 𝐴3 = 2𝜋(9)(4) = 226 TSA: 𝐴= 3902 −509 + 226 = 3 619 mm2 Specific behaviours ✓ outer cylinder ✓ inner circles ✓ inner walls ✓ correct TSA",
