    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-093-1 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (51 Marks) This section has seven (7) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 50 Indian rupees. (a) How many Indian rupees can be bought for 30 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (b) Determine how many Australian dollars are required to buy 50 000 rupees. (1 mark) (c) A tourist going to India wants to take 50 000 rupees with them. Their bank uses the above exchange rate but also adds a commission of 1%. How much will the rupees cost the tourist altogether? (2 marks) (d) Over the next few months, the exchange rate is expected to change so that one Australian dollar will buy 52 rupees. Determine the percentage increase in the exchange rate from 50 to 52 rupees. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-093-2 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (51 Marks) This section has seven (7) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 50 Indian rupees. (a) How many Indian rupees can be bought for 30 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (b) Determine how many Australian dollars are required to buy 50 000 rupees. (1 mark) (c) A tourist going to India wants to take 50 000 rupees with them. Their bank uses the above exchange rate but also adds a commission of 1%. How much will the rupees cost the tourist altogether? (2 marks) (d) Over the next few months, the exchange rate is expected to change so that one Australian dollar will buy 52 rupees. Determine the percentage increase in the exchange rate from 50 to 52 rupees. (2 marks) Solution 30 × 50 = 1 500 rupees Specific behaviours ✓ multiplies correctly Solution 50000 50 = $1000 Specific behaviours ✓ divides correctly Solution 1000 ÷ 100 = $10 commission Total cost is $1000 + $10 = $1010 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates commission ✓ calculates total cost Solution 52 −50 50 × 100 = 2 50 × 100 ",
