    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-093-1 Question 2 (8 marks) (a) Determine the value of (i) 𝑎2 + 2𝑎+ 3 when 𝑎= 7. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑥−𝑥𝑦−𝑦 when 𝑥= −2 and 𝑦= 3. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for a share with a market price of $2.75 and annual earnings per share of 25 cents. (2 marks) (c) The price-to-earnings ratio for a share is 20. If the market price of the share is $1.10, determine the annual earnings per share. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-093-2 Question 2 (8 marks) (a) Determine the value of (i) 𝑎2 + 2𝑎+ 3 when 𝑎= 7. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑥−𝑥𝑦−𝑦 when 𝑥= −2 and 𝑦= 3. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for a share with a market price of $2.75 and annual earnings per share of 25 cents. (2 marks) (c) The price-to-earnings ratio for a share is 20. If the market price of the share is $1.10, determine the annual earnings per share. (2 marks) Solution 20 = 110 𝐸 ⇒𝐸= 110 20 = 55 10 = 5.5 cents per share Specific behaviours ✓ uses PE formula correctly ✓ solves for EPS, stating units Solution 𝑃𝐸= 275 25 = 4 + 4 + 3 = 11 Specific behaviours ✓ uses PE formula with correct units ✓ evaluates ratio Solution −2 −(−2 × 3) −3 = −2 + 6 −3 = 1 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly ✓ evaluates Solution 49 + 14 + 3 = 66 Specific behaviours ✓ squares and doubles ✓ sums terms",
