    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-093-1 Question 3 (10 marks) Four matrices 𝐴, 𝐵, 𝐶 and 𝐷 are shown below. 𝐴= [ 0 2 4 −3 1 −2] , 𝐵= [ 8 0 −12 ] , 𝐶= [ 1 0 5 −1 2 0 4 3 −2 ] , 𝐷= [5 2]. (a) State the size of the square matrix. (1 mark) (b) Calculate 2𝐶+ 5𝐼, where 𝐼 is the 3 × 3 identity matrix. (3 marks) (c) Calculate 𝐷× 𝐴. (2 marks) (d) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞 given that 𝑝× [ −2 𝑞 3 ] = 𝐵. (2 marks) (e) If 𝐸= 𝐴× 𝐶, determine the value of 𝑒21. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-093-2 Question 3 (10 marks) Four matrices 𝐴, 𝐵, 𝐶 and 𝐷 are shown below. 𝐴= [ 0 2 4 −3 1 −2] , 𝐵= [ 8 0 −12 ] , 𝐶= [ 1 0 5 −1 2 0 4 3 −2 ] , 𝐷= [5 2]. (a) State the size of the square matrix. (1 mark) (b) Calculate 2𝐶+ 5𝐼, where 𝐼 is the 3 × 3 identity matrix. (3 marks) (c) Calculate 𝐷× 𝐴. (2 marks) (d) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞 given that 𝑝× [ −2 𝑞 3 ] = 𝐵. (2 marks) (e) If 𝐸= 𝐴× 𝐶, determine the value of 𝑒21. (2 marks) Solution 3 × 3 Specific behaviours ✓ states rows and columns Solution 𝑝× −2 = 8 ⇒𝑝= −4 −4 × 𝑞= 0 ⇒𝑞= 0 Specific behaviours ✓ determines 𝑝 ✓ determines 𝑞 Solution 𝐷𝐴= [−6 12 16] Specific behaviours ✓ product is 1 × 3 ✓ correct product Solution Multiply row 2 of 𝐴 by column 1 of 𝐶 to get 𝐸2,1 = −3 + −1 + −8 = −12 Specific behaviours ✓ uses correct row and column ✓ correct result Solution 2𝐶+ 5𝐼= [ 2 0 10 −2 4 0 8 6 −4 ] + [ 5 0 0 0 5 0 0 0 5 ] = [ 7 0 10 −2 9 0 8 6 1 ] Specific behaviours ✓ calculates 2𝐶 ✓ uses 5𝐼 ✓ calculates correct sum",
