    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-093-1 Question 6 (6 marks) Ann and Ben held 400 and 350 shares respectively in three public companies: Ria, Skip and Tap. Ann held 200 in Ria, 50 in Skip and the remainder in Tap. Ben held 50 in Tap, twice that number in Ria and the remainder in Skip. (a) Display this information in 𝑀, a 2 × 3 matrix. (2 marks) (b) The market value of Ria, Skip and Tap shares is $1.20, $3.50 and $2.10 respectively. Display this information in matrix 𝑁, so that matrix 𝑀× 𝑁 will show the values of each person's share holdings. Do not calculate 𝑀× 𝑁. (1 mark) (c) Explain what information the result of [1 1] × 𝑀 will show. (1 mark) (d) A stock market analyst expects the values of the shares in six months' time to be found from the result of [ 1.5 0 0 0 1.2 0 0 0 1.1 ] × 𝑁. Use this information to calculate the expected price of Skip shares. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-093-2 Question 6 (6 marks) Ann and Ben held 400 and 350 shares respectively in three public companies: Ria, Skip and Tap. Ann held 200 in Ria, 50 in Skip and the remainder in Tap. Ben held 50 in Tap, twice that number in Ria and the remainder in Skip. (a) Display this information in 𝑀, a 2 × 3 matrix. (2 marks) (b) The market value of Ria, Skip and Tap shares is $1.20, $3.50 and $2.10 respectively. Display this information in matrix 𝑁, so that matrix 𝑀× 𝑁 will show the values of each person's share holdings. Do not calculate 𝑀× 𝑁. (1 mark) (c) Explain what information the result of [1 1] × 𝑀 will show. (1 mark) (d) A stock market analyst expects the values of the shares in six months' time to be found from the result of [ 1.5 0 0 0 1.2 0 0 0 1.1 ] × 𝑁. Use this information to calculate the expected price of Skip shares. (2 marks) Solution Skip shares will increase by 20%. Expected price: $3.50 + 0.35 + 0.35 = $4.20 Specific behaviours ✓ evidence of 20% increase ✓ correct new price Solution The total number of shares held by the two, in each of Ria, Skip and Tap. Specific behaviours ✓ clear explanation Solution 𝑁= [ 1.20 3.50",
