    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-113-4 Question 12 (9 marks) A grocery store has the same brand of instant coffee for sale in three different sized jars. The 75, 205 and 340 gram jars are priced at $6.75, $17.75 and $29.05 respectively. (a) Calculate the price per 100 grams for each jar of coffee. (3 marks) (b) Assuming price is the only consideration, list the jars in order of value, best value first. (1 mark) (c) The store is considering stocking a 480 gram jar, priced at $43.45. (i) Determine how many of the existing jars are better value than this jar. (2 marks) (ii) Would your answer to (i) change if the price of the 480 g jar was decreased by 5%? Justify your response. (3 marks) Solution 6.75 ÷ 75 × 100 = $9.00 17.75 ÷ 205 × 100 = $8.66 29.05 ÷ 340 × 100 = $8.54 Specific behaviours  divides cost by weight for at least one jar  at least one price per 100 g correct  all unit prices Solution 340g, 205g, 75g Specific behaviours  correct listing Solution 43.45 ÷ 480 × 100 = $9.05 All 3 of the existing jars are better value Specific behaviours  unit price  states number Solution New price: 43.45 × 0.95 = 41.28 New unit price: 41.28 ÷ 480 × 100 = $8",
