    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-113-2 Question 10 (9 marks) A person who qualifies for a government allowance will be paid $552.30 per fortnight, so long as they do not work. In any fortnight that they do work and earn over $230, their allowance will be reduced by 50 cents in the dollar for earnings over $230. (a) A student who qualifies for the allowance earns $280 in a fortnight. Calculate the amount of allowance they will receive. (2 marks) (b) Another student who qualifies for the allowance has a part-time job for 16 hours each week, earning $15.45 per hour. Calculate (i) their fortnightly wage. (2 mark) (ii) the amount that the fortnightly allowance is reduced. (2 marks) (iii) the fortnightly sum of their allowance and wage. (3 marks)",
