    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-2 Question 11 (7 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑞 given that 𝑞= 1 𝑒 and 𝑒= 1 𝑒1 + 1 𝑒2 when 𝑒1 = 3.96 and 𝑒2 = 0.44. (2 marks) (b) The future value, 𝑉, of an annuity can be calculated using the formula below. 𝑉= 𝐶 𝑅((1 + 𝑅 𝑁) 𝑁𝑇 −1) Consider an annuity with values 𝐶= $3 750, 𝑅= 0.032, 𝑁= 12 and 𝑇= 7. (i) Calculate the future value, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (3 marks) (ii) Calculate the change in 𝑉 when the value of 𝑁 is changed from 12 to 6. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-4 Question 11 (7 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑞 given that 𝑞= 1 𝑒 and 𝑒= 1 𝑒1 + 1 𝑒2 when 𝑒1 = 3.96 and 𝑒2 = 0.44. (2 marks) (b) The future value, 𝑉, of an annuity can be calculated using the formula below. 𝑉= 𝐶 𝑅((1 + 𝑅 𝑁) 𝑁𝑇 −1) Consider an annuity with values 𝐶= $3 750, 𝑅= 0.032, 𝑁= 12 and 𝑇= 7. (i) Calculate the future value, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (3 marks) (ii) Calculate the change in 𝑉 when the value of 𝑁 is changed from 12 to 6. (2 marks) Solution 𝑉= 3750 0.032 ((1 + 0.032 12 ) 12×7 −1) 𝑉= 29378.68 𝑉≈$29 379 (nearest $) Specific behaviours ✓ evidence of correct substitution ✓ calculates 𝑉 ✓ value to nearest dollar Solution 𝑒= 1 3.96 + 1 0.44 = 250 99 = 2. 52 ̅̅̅̅ 𝑞= 1 ÷ 250 99 = 0.396 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value of 𝑒 ✓ correct answer Solution 𝑉≈$29 335 (nearest $) Decrease of 29 379 −29 335 = $44 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates 𝑉 ✓ correct decrease",
