    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-4 Question 13 (6 marks) A researcher at a weather station uses the following formula to calculate 𝐴, the absolute humidity of the air, where 𝑅 is the relative humidity and 𝑇 is the air temperature. 𝐴= 13.1 × 𝑅× (1.06)𝑇 𝑇+ 275 (a) Calculate 𝐴 when 𝑅= 55 and 𝑇= 20. (2 marks) The formula for 𝐴 was used to create the spreadsheet below for various values of 𝑅 and 𝑇. (b) Calculate the value of the entries 𝑃 and 𝑄 shown in the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) One of the entries in the spreadsheet is incorrect. State the value of 𝑇 and the value of 𝑅 for the cell in which the incorrect value lies and calculate the correct value of 𝐴. (2 marks) 𝐴 𝑅 30 40 50 60 70 𝑇 −5 1.09 𝑃 1.81 2.18 2.54 0 1.43 1.91 2.38 2.86 𝑄 5 1.88 2.50 3.13 3.76 4.38 10 3.35 3.29 4.12 4.94 5.76 Solution 𝐴= 13.1 × 55 × (1.06)20 20 + 275 = 7.83 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly ✓ correct value Solution 𝑇= 10, 𝑅= 30 𝐴= 2.47 Specific behaviours ✓ correct values of 𝑇 and 𝐻 ✓ correct value of 𝐴 Solution 𝑃= 1.45 𝑄= 3.33 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑃 ✓ value of 𝑄",
