    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-133-2 Question 17 (12 marks) A spreadsheet to track a monthly car budget is shown below, with all amounts in dollars. The figures for months 1, 2 and 3 show the actual expenditure for each item. Item Monthly Budget Month 1 Month 2 Month 3 3-Month Total Loan payment 344 344 344 344 𝑅 Insurance 215 215 215 255 685 Maintenance 129 0 88 295 383 Fuel 172 195 𝑄 173 536 Total 𝑃 754 815 1067 𝑆 (a) Determine the values of 𝑃, 𝑄, 𝑅 and 𝑆 in the spreadsheet. (3 marks) (b) A motoring organisation recommends allocating no more than 20% of a person's monthly income to running a car. Would a person on a salary of $52 200 pa and using the total monthly budget figure above meet this target? Justify your answer. (3 marks)",
