    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-133-2 Question 18 (7 marks) A shop sold three sizes of the same brand of tomato sauce. The 250 mL bottle cost $1.55, the 475 mL bottle cost $2.66 and the 920 mL bottle cost $5.52. Retail laws require the shop to display the price per 100 mL for each bottle, to the nearest cent. (a) Calculate the price per 100 mL for all three sizes of tomato sauce. (3 marks) (b) Use the unit prices to list the bottle sizes in order of value, from best to worst. (1 mark) (c) Determine the maximum price, to the nearest cent, for a 725 mL bottle of the same sauce if the shop wanted it to be better value than the other three sizes in terms of unit price. (2 marks) (d) Suggest one reason that a shopper may prefer a size other than that which offers the best value in terms of unit price. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-133-4 Question 18 (7 marks) A shop sold three sizes of the same brand of tomato sauce. The 250 mL bottle cost $1.55, the 475 mL bottle cost $2.66 and the 920 mL bottle cost $5.52. Retail laws require the shop to display the price per 100 mL for each bottle, to the nearest cent. (a) Calculate the price per 100 mL for all three sizes of tomato sauce. (3 marks) (b) Use the unit prices to list the bottle sizes in order of value, from best to worst. (1 mark) (c) Determine the maximum price, to the nearest cent, for a 725 mL bottle of the same sauce if the shop wanted it to be better value than the other three sizes in terms of unit price. (2 marks) (d) Suggest one reason that a shopper may prefer a size other than that which offers the best value in terms of unit price. (1 mark) Solution 250: 155 ÷ 250 × 100 = 62 c 475: 266 ÷ 475 × 100 = 56 c 920: 552 ÷ 920 × 100 = 60 c Specific behaviours ✓ uses unit cost for one size ✓ correct 100 mL price for one size ✓ all three prices correct Solution 475 mL, 920 mL, 250 mL Specific behaviours ✓ correct order Solution 725 ÷ 100 × 56 = 406 c To be best value, price must be less, so $4.05.",
