    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-2 Question 19 (8 marks) A right-triangular prism has dimensions shown in the diagram below. (a) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) (b) A quarter-size model is made of the prism, i.e. using a scale of 1: 4. Calculate the total surface area of this model. (2 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the prism. (1 mark) (d) Another scale model is made of the prism, so that the dimensions of the sloping face are now 4 cm by 5 cm. Calculate the volume of this scale model. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-4 Question 19 (8 marks) A right-triangular prism has dimensions shown in the diagram below. (a) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) (b) A quarter-size model is made of the prism, i.e. using a scale of 1: 4. Calculate the total surface area of this model. (2 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the prism. (1 mark) (d) Another scale model is made of the prism, so that the dimensions of the sloping face are now 4 cm by 5 cm. Calculate the volume of this scale model. (2 marks) Solution Volume: 1 2 × 24 × 7 × 20 = 1 680 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ correct volume Solution Area scale factor: ( 1 4) 2 = 1 16 Area: 1288 × 1 16 = 80.5 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates area scale factor ✓ correct area Solution Triangular ends: 2 × 1 2 × 24 × 7 = 168 Rectangles: 20 × (7 + 24 + 25) = 1120 TSA: 168 + 1120 = 1 288 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates area of triangle ✓ indicates area of rectangle ✓ correct TSA Solution Scale factor: 4 20 = 1 5. Volume sf ( 1 5) 3 = 1 125 Volume: 1680 × 1 125 = 13.44 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates scale factor for length and volume ✓ correct volume",
