    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-2 (b) Determine the allowance paid to a family with two children and a combined annual income of $105 000. (2 marks) (c) Determine the allowance paid to a family with no children and a combined annual income of $83 000. (1 mark) (d) Determine the combined income a family with one child would earn if the allowance paid to them was $4600. (2 marks) (e) Determine the possible minimum and maximum combined income a family with 6 children could earn if the allowance paid to them was $7300 (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-4 (b) Determine the allowance paid to a family with two children and a combined annual income of $105 000. (2 marks) Solution -$7300 – (105 000 – 97 000) x 0.3 = $4900 Specific behaviours ✓ uses correct allowance, (7300 and 97 000 shown in calc.) ✓ correct answer given. (c) Determine the allowance paid to a family with no children and a combined annual income of $83 000. (1 mark) Solution - Nil Specific behaviours ✓ No allowance given (d) Determine the combined income a family with one child would earn if the allowance paid to them was $4600. (2 marks) Solution 4600 = 5100 – (x – 54 000) x 0.1 Combined income of $59 000 Specific behaviours ✓ Shows calculation using 4600 and 54 000 ✓Correct combined income shown. (e) Determine the possible minimum and maximum combined income a family with 6 children could earn if the allowance paid to them was $7300. (2 marks) Solution Minimum $73 000 Maximum $97 000 Specific behaviours ✓ Shows Min. ✓ Shows Maximum.",
