    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-133-2 Question 21 (8 marks) The washer shown below is made of plastic and has an internal radius of 7 mm, an external radius of 22 mm and is 3 mm thick. (a) The plastic used to make the washers costs 95 cents per litre. Given that one litre is 1 000 cubic centimetres, determine the cost of making 8 000 of the washers. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the total surface area of one washer, giving your answer in mm2. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-133-4 Question 21 (8 marks) The washer shown below is made of plastic and has an internal radius of 7 mm, an external radius of 22 mm and is 3 mm thick. {Washer Drawing} (a) The plastic used to make the washers costs 95 cents per litre. Given that one litre is 1 000 cubic centimetres, determine the cost of making 8 000 of the washers. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the total surface area of one washer, giving your answer in mm2. (4 marks) Solution Outer cylinder: 𝐴1 = 2𝜋(22)2 + 2𝜋(22)(3) = 3456 Inner circles: 𝐴2 = 2𝜋(7)2 = 308 Inner walls: 𝐴3 = 2𝜋(7)(3) = 132 TSA: 𝐴= 3456 −308 + 132 = 3 280 mm2 Specific behaviours ✓ outer cylinder ✓ inner circles ✓ inner walls ✓ correct TSA Alternative Solution Top Face: = 2𝜋(22)2 −2𝜋(7)2 = 1366.59 Top & Bottom Face 𝐴1 = (2)(1366.59) = 2733.19 Inner wall: 𝐴2 = 2𝜋(7)(3) = 131.95 Outer walls: 𝐴3 = 2𝜋(22)(3) = 414.69 TSA: 𝐴= 2733.19 + 131.95 + 414.69 = 3 280 mm2 Specific behaviours ✓ One Area (Top/Bottom) ✓ inner wall area ✓ Outer walls area ✓ correct TSA Solution Outer volume: 𝜋× 2.22 × 0.3 = 4.562 Inner volume: 𝜋× 0.72 × 0.3 = 0.462 Total volume: (4.562 −0.462) × 8000 = 4.1 × 8000 = 32800 Cost: ",
