    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-5 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight (8) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 0.60 euros. (a) How many euros can be bought for (i) 400 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (ii) 10 000 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (b) How many Australian dollars are needed to buy 60 euros? (1 mark) One Australian dollar can buy 20 Thai baht. (c) At an airport a traveller wants to buy 4 000 Thai baht, but the exchange desk also charges them a commission of 5%. Determine the total cost, in Australian dollars, for the traveller to buy this amount of currency. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-7 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight (8) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 0.60 euros. (a) How many euros can be bought for (i) 400 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (ii) 10 000 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (b) How many Australian dollars are needed to buy 60 euros? (1 mark) One Australian dollar can buy 20 Thai baht. (c) At an airport a traveller wants to buy 4 000 Thai baht, but the exchange desk also charges them a commission of 5%. Determine the total cost, in Australian dollars, for the traveller to buy this amount of currency. (3 marks) Solution 60 ÷ 0.60 = $100 Specific behaviours ✓ correct amount Solution 10000 × 0.60 = €6 000 Specific behaviours ✓ correct amount Solution 4000 ÷ 20 = 200 200 × 5 100 = 10 Total = 200 + 10 = $210 Specific behaviours ✓ converts to dollars ✓ calculates commission ✓ correct total Solution 400 × 0.60 = €240 Specific behaviours ✓ correct amount",
