    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-5 Question 2 (6 marks) Evaluate (a) 2 × 12 −6 ÷ 3 + 9. (2 marks) (b) 4𝑦2 −3𝑦 when 𝑦= 1 2. (2 marks) (c) 𝑎2 + 𝑎𝑏+ √𝑏 when 𝑎= −6 and 𝑏= 4. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-7 Question 2 (6 marks) Evaluate (a) 2 × 12 −6 ÷ 3 + 9. (2 marks) (b) 4𝑦2 −3𝑦 when 𝑦= 1 2. (2 marks) (c) 𝑎2 + 𝑎𝑏+ √𝑏 when 𝑎= −6 and 𝑏= 4. (2 marks) Solution 2 × 12 −6 ÷ 3 + 9 = 24 −2 + 9 = 31 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of rule of order ✓ correct value Solution 4𝑦2 −3𝑦 = 4 (1 2) 2 −3 (1 2) = 4 (1 4) −11 2 = 1 −11 2 = −1 2 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly ✓ correct value Solution 𝑎2 + 𝑎𝑏+ √𝑏= (−6)2 + (−6)(4) + √4 = 36 −24 + 2 = 14 Specific behaviours ✓ evaluates at least two of the three terms correctly ✓ correct value",
