    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-5 Question 4 (6 marks) During the week, casual employees at a recycling plant are paid a wage of $25 per hour plus $1.50 for every kg of electronic waste they collect. Over the weekend, both rates are increased by 20%. A casual worked for 4 hours on Thursday, collecting 30 kg of electronic waste, and then a further 6 hours on Sunday when they collected 40 kg of electronic waste. (a) Determine the hourly pay rate for weekends. (1 mark) (b) Calculate how much the casual earned on Thursday. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the total earned by the casual over the two days. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-7 Question 4 (6 marks) During the week, casual employees at a recycling plant are paid a wage of $25 per hour plus $1.50 for every kg of electronic waste they collect. Over the weekend, both rates are increased by 20%. A casual worked for 4 hours on Thursday, collecting 30 kg of electronic waste, and then a further 6 hours on Sunday when they collected 40 kg of electronic waste. (a) Determine the hourly pay rate for weekends. (1 mark) (b) Calculate how much the casual earned on Thursday. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the total earned by the casual over the two days. (3 marks) Solution 25 × 0.2 = 5 ⇒New rate is $30 per hour Specific behaviours ✓ correct rate Solution 6 × 25 + 40 × 1.5 = 150 + 60 = 210 210 × 0.2 = 42 Sunday earns 210 + 42 = $252 Total for 2 days:145 + 252 = $397 Specific behaviours ✓ Sunday total ✓ increases Sunday total by 20% ✓ correct total for two days Solution 30 × 1.50 = 45 4 × 25 = 100 Total: 100 + 45 = $145 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates weight amount ✓ calculates hourly amount and adds to weight amount",
