    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-5 Question 6 (7 marks) An investor held 300, 400 and 1 000 shares in companies A, B and C respectively. Company A announced a dividend per share of 1.5% of the share price, company B paid the investor a dividend of $40 and company C announced a dividend of 15 cents per share. (a) Determine the total dividend the investor can expect from company A if the current price of a share is $20. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the dividend paid per share by company B. (2 marks) (c) Company C did not pay the investor the total dividend but instead paid the balance remaining after withholding a government tax of 30% of the dividend. Calculate the balance due to the investor. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-133-7 Question 6 (7 marks) An investor held 300, 400 and 1 000 shares in companies A, B and C respectively. Company A announced a dividend per share of 1.5% of the share price, company B paid the investor a dividend of $40 and company C announced a dividend of 15 cents per share. (a) Determine the total dividend the investor can expect from company A if the current price of a share is $20. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the dividend paid per share by company B. (2 marks) (c) Company C did not pay the investor the total dividend but instead paid the balance remaining after withholding a government tax of 30% of the dividend. Calculate the balance due to the investor. (3 marks) Solution 1000 × 0.15 = 150 150 × 0.3 = 45 150 −45 = $105 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates full dividend ✓ indicates tax ✓ correct balance Solution 40 400 = $0.10 = 10 cents per share Specific behaviours ✓ indicates calculation ✓ correct amount with units Solution 20 × 1.5 100 = $0.30 300 × 0.30 = $90 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates dividend per share ✓ correct dividend",
