    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-133-7 Question 7 (5 marks) Rectangular logo 𝐴𝐶𝐷𝐹, with 𝐴𝐹= 4 cm and 𝐴𝐶= 12.5 cm, has a white background with grey triangle 𝐴𝐵𝐹 and grey sector of circle 𝐷𝐶𝐸, as shown below. Given that 𝐴𝐹= 2 × 𝐴𝐵 and assuming that 𝜋= 3, determine what percentage of the area of the rectangular logo is grey. Solution 𝐴𝐵= 4 ÷ 2 = 2 𝐴𝐴𝐵𝐹= 1 2 × 2 × 4 = 4 𝐴𝐷𝐶𝐸= 1 4 × 3 × 42 = 12 𝐴𝐴𝐶𝐷𝐹= 4 × 12.5 = 50 % shaded = 4 + 12 50 × 100 = 32% Specific behaviours ✓ length 𝐴𝐵 ✓ area of triangle ✓ area of sector ✓ area of rectangle ✓ correct percentage",
