    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) The regular price of $849 for a new smartphone is discounted by 15% in a sale. Determine the sale price of the smartphone. (2 marks) (b) After a 4% increase, the price of another smartphone was $650. Determine the price of the smartphone before the increase. (2 marks) (c) The value of a smartphone, currently $1 200, is expected to decrease by 30% each year. Determine the expected value of the smartphone in 3 years. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) The regular price of $849 for a new smartphone is discounted by 15% in a sale. Determine the sale price of the smartphone. (2 marks) (b) After a 4% increase, the price of another smartphone was $650. Determine the price of the smartphone before the increase. (2 marks) (c) The value of a smartphone, currently $1 200, is expected to decrease by 30% each year. Determine the expected value of the smartphone in 3 years. (2 marks) Solution 𝑉= 1200 × (1 −0.3)3 = 1200 × 0.73 = $411.60 Specific behaviours  indicates suitable method  correct value Solution 𝑃= 650 ÷ (1 + 0.04) = 650 ÷ 1.04 = $625 Specific behaviours  indicates correct multiplier  correct price Solution 𝑃= 849 × (1 −0.15) = 849 × 0.85 = $721.65 Or P =$ 849 - $127.35 = $ 721.65 Specific behaviours  indicates correct multiplier or finds correct discount.  correct price",
