    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (9 marks) The outline of a logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 is shown, where straight lines 𝐴𝐶 and 𝐵𝐷 intersect at right-angles at 𝑂 to form quadrilateral 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. 𝑂𝐴= 24 cm, 𝑂𝐷= 45 cm, 𝐶𝐵= 35 cm and 𝐶𝐷= 53 cm. (a) Determine the length of 𝑂𝐶 and the length of 𝑂𝐵. (3 marks) (b) Determine the perimeter of logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks) (c) Determine the area of logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 Question 11 (9 marks) The outline of a logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 is shown, where straight lines 𝐴𝐶 and 𝐵𝐷 intersect at right-angles at 𝑂 to form quadrilateral 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. 𝑂𝐴= 24 cm, 𝑂𝐷= 45 cm, 𝐶𝐵= 35 cm and 𝐶𝐷= 53 cm. (a) Determine the length of 𝑂𝐶 and the length of 𝑂𝐵. (3 marks) (b) Determine the perimeter of logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks) (c) Determine the area of logo 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐵= √242 + 212 = 31.9 cm f/t from student’s OB 𝐴𝐷= √242 + 452 = 51 cm 𝑃= 31.9 + 51 + 35 + 53 = 170.9 cm Specific behaviours  length of 𝐴𝐵  length of 𝐴𝐷  correct perimeter Solution 𝐴𝐶= 24 + 28 = 52 f/t from student’s OC 𝐴𝐴𝐵𝐶= 1 2 × 52 × 21 = 546 𝐴𝐴𝐷𝐶= 1 2 × 52 × 45 = 1 170 Area = 546 + 1 170 = 1 716 cm2 Specific behaviours  clearly shows method (using 2 or 4 right-triangles)  one correct part area  correct total area Solution 𝑂𝐶= √532 −452 = 28 cm 𝑂𝐵= √352 −282 = 21 cm No f/t Specific behaviours  adds lengths to existing or new diagram(s)  value of 𝑂𝐶  value of 𝑂𝐵",
