    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF When a single block of lead is used to make one batch of weights, the unused lead is discarded. (c) Determine the volume of lead discarded when a batch is made. (2 marks) (d) Given that other manufacturing costs amount to $295 per batch, calculate the percentage profit expected by the store from selling all the weights made in a batch. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 When a single block of lead is used to make one batch of weights, the unused lead is discarded. (c) Determine the volume of lead discarded when a batch is made. (2 marks) (d) Given that other manufacturing costs amount to $295 per batch, calculate the percentage profit expected by the store from selling all the weights made in a batch. (4 marks) Solution 𝑉𝐵= 65 × 65 × 124 = 523 900 Vol remaining = 523 900 −205 251 −316 673 = 1 976 mm3 Accept 523 900 – sum of answers in a) and b). Specific behaviours  volume of original block  correct volume remaining Note: Answers to (a), (b) and (c) may vary depending on level of rounding used throughout question. Solution Income = 250 × 1.55 + 350 × 1.75 = $1000 Costs = 335 + 295 = $630 Profit = 1 000 −630 = $370 % profit = 370 630 × 100 f/t from above = 58.7% ≈59% Specific behaviours  total income  total costs  profit  percentage profit",
