    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 13 (6 marks) (a) A payday lender offers simple interest loans for periods of up to 90 days at a daily interest rate of 0.0685%. Determine the repayment when a loan of $420 is taken out and repaid in full 30 days later. (2 marks) (b) Another lender offers compound interest loans of amounts up to $10 000 at an annual rate of 16.8%. Determine the repayment when a loan of $3 500 is taken out and repaid in full 3 years later when interest is compounded (i) annually. (2 marks) (ii) monthly. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-8 Question 13 (6 marks) (a) A payday lender offers simple interest loans for periods of up to 90 days at a daily interest rate of 0.0685%. Determine the repayment when a loan of $420 is taken out and repaid in full 30 days later. (2 marks) (b) Another lender offers compound interest loans of amounts up to $10 000 at an annual rate of 16.8%. Determine the repayment when a loan of $3 500 is taken out and repaid in full 3 years later when interest is compounded (i) annually. (2 marks) (ii) monthly. (2 marks) Solution 𝐼= 420 × 0.0685 × 30 100 = $8.63 Repayment: 420 + 8.63 = $428.63 Specific behaviours  calculates interest  correct repayment Solution 𝐹= 3500(1 + 0.168)3 = $5 576.95 Specific behaviours  indicates correct expression  correct repayment Solution 𝐹= 3500 (1 + 0.168 12 ) 3×12 = $5 773.44 Specific behaviours  indicates correct expression  correct repayment",
