    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (7 marks) The number of people attending a show over a weekend is shown in the table below. (a) Write the information from the table as a 2 × 3 matrix 𝐴. (1 mark) Admission prices for children, adults and seniors are $22, $48 and $18 respectively. (b) Write this information as column matrix 𝐵, so that the matrix product 𝐴𝐵 will make sense. (2 marks) (c) Using your calculator, or otherwise, determine matrix 𝐶, where 𝐶= 𝐴𝐵. (2 marks) (d) Explain what information the elements in matrix 𝐶 show. (2 marks) Children Adults Seniors Saturday 155 243 89 Sunday 212 376 175",
