    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (8 marks) A right-triangle has vertices 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶 on the circumference of a circle so that 𝐴𝐶 is a diameter of the circle. Two segments in the circle have been shaded grey. Length 𝐴𝐵= 13.2 cm and length 𝐵𝐶= 8.5 cm. (a) Determine the diameter of the circle and hence the length of the arc 𝐴𝐶. (4 marks) (b) Determine the grey shaded area. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 Question 16 (8 marks) A right-triangle has vertices 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶 on the circumference of a circle so that 𝐴𝐶 is a diameter of the circle. Two segments in the circle have been shaded grey. Length 𝐴𝐵= 13.2 cm and length 𝐵𝐶= 8.5 cm. (a) Determine the diameter of the circle and hence the length of the arc 𝐴𝐶. (4 marks) (b) Determine the grey shaded area. (4 marks) Solution 𝑑2 = 13.22 + 8.52 = 246.49 𝑑= √246.49 = 15.7 cm Arc 𝐴𝐶= 1 2 × 𝜋× 𝑑 = 1 2 × 𝜋× 15.7 f/ t from student’s d = 24.66 cm Specific behaviours  indicates use of Pythagoras' Theorem  correct diameter  indicates arc is half of circumference  correct arc length (f/t from student’s diameter) Solution 𝐴𝑇= 1 2 × 13.2 × 8.5 = 56.1 𝑟= 15.7 ÷ 2 = 7.85 𝐴𝑆𝐶= 1 2 × 𝜋× 7.852 = 96.8 𝐴𝑆𝐻𝐴𝐷𝐸𝐷= 96.8 −56.1 = 40.7 cm2 Specific behaviours  area of triangle  calculates radius (f/t from student’s diameter)  area of semicircle  shaded area",
