    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.1 · Consumer arithmetic",
    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (6 marks) The currency of Fiji is the Fijian dollar. An Australian bank will sell customers 1.462 Fijian dollars for 𝐴$1 and it will buy 1.621 Fijian dollars back for 𝐴$1, where 𝐴$ represents Australian dollars. (a) A customer had 500 Fijian dollars. Determine, to the nearest cent, how many Australian dollars they would receive from this bank. (2 marks) An Australian airport exchange kiosk advertises the same rates as the bank, but also charges customers a fee of 2.9% of the amount exchanged. (b) Determine the cost in Australian dollars for a traveller to buy 800 Fijian dollars at the airport kiosk. (2 marks) (c) Another traveller arrived back in Australia from Fiji with 225 Fijian dollars. Determine the fee that the kiosk would charge to buy this currency back, giving your answer in Australian dollars. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-8 Question 17 (6 marks) The currency of Fiji is the Fijian dollar. An Australian bank will sell customers 1.462 Fijian dollars for 𝐴$1 and it will buy 1.621 Fijian dollars back for 𝐴$1, where 𝐴$ represents Australian dollars. (a) A customer had 500 Fijian dollars. Determine, to the nearest cent, how many Australian dollars they would receive from this bank. (2 marks) An Australian airport exchange kiosk advertises the same rates as the bank, but also charges customers a fee of 2.9% of the amount exchanged. (b) Determine the cost in Australian dollars for a traveller to buy 800 Fijian dollars at the airport kiosk. (2 marks) (c) Another traveller arrived back in Australia from Fiji with 225 Fijian dollars. Determine the fee that the kiosk would charge to buy this currency back, giving your answer in Australian dollars. (2 marks) Solution 500 ÷ 1.621 = 𝐴$308.45 Specific behaviours  uses buy rate  correct amount Solution Exchange: 𝐹$800 ÷ 1.462 = 𝐴$547.20 Add fee: 𝐴$547.20 × 1.029 = 𝐴$563.06 Specific behaviours  exchange amount  amount with fee Solution Exchange: 𝐹$225 ÷ 1.621 = 𝐴$138.80 Fee: 𝐴$138.80 × 0.029 = 𝐴$4.0",
