    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 18 (7 marks) (a) A map has a scale of 1: 75 000. The distance along a path between two campsites on the map is 32.5 cm. (i) Determine the actual distance between the campsites in kilometres. (2 marks) (ii) Given that the hiker expects to walk at an average speed of 3.9 km per hour, when will they reach the second campsite if they leave the first at 1: 15 pm on Tuesday? (2 marks) (b) A 3D printing machine can be programmed to create copies of a solid sculpture that are mathematically similar to the original but can be any required size. The machine used 320 cm3 of plastic to print a copy that was 4 cm tall. Determine the quantity of plastic required to print a copy that is 15 cm tall. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 Question 18 (7 marks) (a) A map has a scale of 1: 75 000. The distance along a path between two campsites on the map is 32.5 cm. (i) Determine the actual distance between the campsites in kilometres. (2 marks) (ii) Given that the hiker expects to walk at an average speed of 3.9 km per hour, when will they reach the second campsite if they leave the first at 1: 15 pm on Tuesday? (2 marks) (b) A 3D printing machine can be programmed to create copies of a solid sculpture that are mathematically similar to the original but can be any required size. The machine used 320 cm3 of plastic to print a copy that was 4 cm tall. Determine the quantity of plastic required to print a copy that is 15 cm tall. (3 marks) Solution Linear scale factor: 15 ÷ 4 = 3.75 Volume scale factor: 3.753 = 52.734375 Qty of plastic: 320 × 3.753 = 16 875 cm3. Specific behaviours  indicates linear scale factor  uses volume scale factor  correct quantity Solution 32.5 cm ×75000 → 2 437 500 cm 2 437 500 cm ÷100 → 24 375 m ÷1000 → 24.375 ≈24.4 km Specific behaviours  use scale correctly  correct distance in km Solution 24.375 ÷ 3.9 = 6.25 1: 15 pm ",
