    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (8 marks) A storage silo on a farm has the form of a cone of perpendicular height 2.4 m on top of a cylinder of height 2.6 m and radius 2.2 m, as shown. The silo stands on a level concrete floor. (a) Determine the volume of the silo, giving your answer to the nearest cubic metre. (3 marks) (b) Determine the slant height of the cone. (2 marks) (c) Determine the total surface area of the outside of the silo, excluding the floor. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-153-8 Question 19 (8 marks) A storage silo on a farm has the form of a cone of perpendicular height 2.4 m on top of a cylinder of height 2.6 m and radius 2.2 m, as shown. The silo stands on a level concrete floor. (a) Determine the volume of the silo, giving your answer to the nearest cubic metre. (3 marks) (b) Determine the slant height of the cone. (2 marks) (c) Determine the total surface area of the outside of the silo, excluding the floor. (3 marks) Solution 𝑉𝐶𝑌𝐿= 𝜋(2.2)2(2.6) = 39.53 𝑉𝐶𝑂= 𝜋(2.2)2(2.4) ÷ 3 = 12.16 𝑉𝑇𝑂𝑇= 39.53 + 12.16 = 51.7 ≈52 m3 Specific behaviours  volume of cylinder  volume of cone  correct total volume, rounded Solution ℎ= √2.22 + 2.42 = √10.6 = 3.26 m Specific behaviours  indicates use of Pythagoras' Theorem  correct slant height Solution 𝐴𝐶𝑌𝐿= 2𝜋(2.2)(2.6) = 35.94 𝐴𝐶𝑂= 𝜋(2.2)(3.26) = 22.50 𝑇𝑆𝐴= 35.94 + 22.5 = 58.44 m2 Specific behaviours  SA of cone  SA of cylinder  TSA of silo",
