    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 20 (8 marks) A bank offers loans of $𝑃 at an interest rate of 2.4% per annum to be repaid over 𝑛 years. The monthly loan repayment, 𝑀 dollars, is calculated using the formula 𝑀= 𝑘× 𝑃 500(𝑘−1) , where 𝑘= (1.002)12𝑛. (a) A customer takes a loan of $25 000 over 6 years. Determine (i) the value of 𝑘, rounded to 4 decimal places. (1 mark) (ii) the value of 𝑀, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (2 marks) (b) A student has a part-time job for 52 hours a month that pays $16.50 per hour. They have budgeted 40% of their gross monthly earnings on loan repayments and plan to take out a loan from this bank of $9 000 for a car and repay it over 2 years. Can the student afford this loan? Show calculations to justify your answer. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-8 Question 20 (8 marks) A bank offers loans of $𝑃 at an interest rate of 2.4% per annum to be repaid over 𝑛 years. The monthly loan repayment, 𝑀 dollars, is calculated using the formula 𝑀= 𝑘× 𝑃 500(𝑘−1) , where 𝑘= (1.002)12𝑛. (a) A customer takes a loan of $25 000 over 6 years. Determine (i) the value of 𝑘, rounded to 4 decimal places. (1 mark) (ii) the value of 𝑀, rounding your answer to the nearest dollar. (2 marks) (b) A student has a part-time job for 52 hours a month that pays $16.50 per hour. They have budgeted 40% of their gross monthly earnings on loan repayments and plan to take out a loan of $9 000 for a car and repay it over 2 years. . Can the student afford this loan? Show calculations to justify your answer. (5 marks) Solution 𝑘= (1.002)12×6 = 1.1547 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 𝑀= 1.1547 × 25000 500(1.1547 −1) = 373.2 ≈$373 (nearest dollar) Specific behaviours  indicates substitution  correct value (rounding for guidance) Solution Loan budget is 52 × 16.50 × 0.40 = $343.20 per month 𝑘= (1.002)12×2 = 1.0491 𝑀= 1.0491 × 9000 500(1.0491 −1) ≈$385 per month Advise student that they cannot ",
