    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) In order to fit a building on a small plot of land, the plan of its concrete slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 is trapezoidal with right-angled corners at 𝑅 and 𝑆. In the diagram shown 𝑃𝑆 is 3 m longer than 𝑄𝑅, 𝑄𝑅 is 7 m and 𝑅𝑆 is 4 m. (a) Determine the area of the slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (2 marks) (b) Before pouring the concrete the edge of the entire slab is surrounded with formwork at a cost of $20 per metre. Determine the cost of the formwork for the slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-7 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) In order to fit a building on a small plot of land, the plan of its concrete slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 is trapezoidal with right-angled corners at 𝑅 and 𝑆. In the diagram shown 𝑃𝑆 is 3 m longer than 𝑄𝑅, 𝑄𝑅 is 7 m and 𝑅𝑆 is 4 m. (a) Determine the area of the slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (2 marks) (b) Formwork is used to surround the edge of the entire slab when concrete is poured and costs $20 per metre. Determine the cost of the formwork for the slab 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆. (3 marks) Solution 𝑃𝑄= √32 + 42 = √25 = 5 𝑃= 5 + 7 + 4 + 10 = 26 m Cost = 26 × 20 = $520 Specific behaviours  length 𝑃𝑄  total perimeter  correct cost f/t from student’s P Solution Rectangle: 𝐴= 4 × 7 = 28 Triangle: 𝐴= 1 2 × 3 × 4 = 6 Total area: 𝐴= 28 + 6 = 34 m2 Specific behaviours  indicates suitable method  correct area",
