    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-153-7 Question 2 (5 marks) Evaluate the following: (a) 4 + 5 × 10. (1 mark) (b) 12 ÷ 6 −5 × 1 2. (2 marks) (c) √3𝑥+ 4 (𝑥−2)2 when 𝑥= 7. (2 marks) Solution 4 + 50 = 54 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 12 6 −5 2 = 2 −2.5 = −0.5 or −1 2 Specific behaviours  simplifies quotient and product  correct value Solution √3 × 7 + 4 (7 −2)2 = √25 52 = 5 25 = 1 5 or 0.2 Specific behaviours  correctly evaluates numerator or denominator  correct, simplified value",
