    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 4 (6 marks) A spreadsheet contains the following values: 𝐴 𝐵 𝐶 𝐷 𝐸 1 6.5 7.75 6.25 10.25 9.25 2 3 4.2 4.5 6.2 8.4 9.6 4 The following formulas are to be used to calculate the value in cell 𝐴2 and the value in cell 𝐴4: 𝐴2 = (𝐴1 + 𝐵1 + 𝐶1 + 𝐷1 + 𝐸1) ÷ 5 𝐴4 = (0.5 × 𝐴3 + 𝐵3 + 𝐶3 + 𝐷3 + 0.5 × 𝐸3) ÷ 4 (a) Determine the value in cell 𝐴2. (2 marks) (b) Determine the value in cell 𝐴4. (2 marks) (c) The value in cell 𝐶1 increased by 15. Determine the change in value of cell 𝐴2. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-153-7 Question 4 (6 marks) A spreadsheet contains the following values: 𝐴 𝐵 𝐶 𝐷 𝐸 1 6.5 7.75 6.25 10.25 9.25 2 3 4.2 4.5 6.2 8.4 9.6 4 The following formulas are to be used to calculate the value in cell 𝐴2 and the value in cell 𝐴4: 𝐴2 = (𝐴1 + 𝐵1 + 𝐶1 + 𝐷1 + 𝐸1) ÷ 5 𝐴4 = (0.5 × 𝐴3 + 𝐵3 + 𝐶3 + 𝐷3 + 0.5 × 𝐸3) ÷ 4 (a) Determine the value in cell 𝐴2. (2 marks) (b) Determine the value in cell 𝐴4. (2 marks) (c) The value in cell 𝐶1 increased by 15. Determine the change in value of cell 𝐴2. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴2 = (6.5 + 7.75 + 6.25 + 10.25 + 9.25) ÷ 5 = 40 ÷ 5 = 8 Specific behaviours  evidence of correct substitution/sum  correct cell value Solution 𝐴4 = (0.5 × 4.2 + 4.5 + 6.2 + 8.4 + 0.5 × 9.6) ÷ 4 = (2.1 + 4.5 + 6.2 + 8.4 + 4.8) ÷ 4 = 26 ÷ 4 = 6.5 Specific behaviours  evidence of correct substitution  correct cell value Solution 𝐴2 = (40 + 15) ÷ 5 = 55 ÷ 5 = 11 Change in cell value is 11 −8 = 3 Specific behaviours  new value of cell 𝐴2  states change in value",
