    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (7 marks) When designing an electrical circuit, an engineer uses the table below to determine 𝐹, the latency factor. 𝑅 is the number of resistors and 𝐶 is the number of capacitors in the circuit. 𝐹 𝑅 3 4 5 6 7 𝐶 4 0.33 𝐴 0.49 0.60 0.73 5 0.39 0.46 0.55 0.66 0.79 6 0.45 0.52 0.61 0.72 0.85 7 0.51 0.58 0.67 0.78 0.91 8 0.57 0.64 0.73 0.84 𝐵 (a) Determine (i) 𝐹 when a circuit has 5 resistors and 7 capacitors. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑅 when a circuit with 4 capacitors has a latency factor of 0.73. (1 mark) The formula used to calculate the latency factor is 𝐹= 𝑅2 + 6𝐶 100 . (b) Determine the value of 𝐴 and the value of 𝐵 shown in the table. (2 marks) (c) Circuit 𝑃 has 6 resistors and 11 capacitors and circuit 𝑄 has 8 resistors and 8 capacitors. Determine, with justification, which circuit has the highest latency factor. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-7 Question 5 (7 marks) When designing an electrical circuit, an engineer uses the table below to determine 𝐹, the latency factor. 𝑅 is the number of resistors and 𝐶 is the number of capacitors in the circuit. 𝐹 𝑅 3 4 5 6 7 𝐶 4 0.33 𝐴 0.49 0.60 0.73 5 0.39 0.46 0.55 0.66 0.79 6 0.45 0.52 0.61 0.72 0.85 7 0.51 0.58 0.67 0.78 0.91 8 0.57 0.64 0.73 0.84 𝐵 (a) Determine (i) 𝐹 when a circuit has 5 resistors and 7 capacitors. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑅 when a circuit with 4 capacitors has a latency factor of 0.73. (1 mark) The formula used to calculate the latency factor is 𝐹= 𝑅2 + 6𝐶 100 . (b) Determine the value of 𝐴 and the value of 𝐵 shown in the table. (2 marks) (c) Circuit 𝑃 has 6 resistors and 11 capacitors and circuit 𝑄 has 8 resistors and 8 capacitors. Determine, with justification, which circuit has the highest latency factor. (3 marks) Solution 𝐹𝐴= (42 + 6 × 4) ÷ 100 = 0.40 𝐹𝐵= (72 + 6 × 8) ÷ 100 = 0.97 Specific behaviours  value of 𝐴  value of 𝐵 Solution 𝐹𝑃= (62 + 6 × 11) ÷ 100 = 1.02 𝐹𝑄= (82 + 6 × 8) ÷ 100 = 1.12 Hence, circuit 𝑄 has highest latency factor as 1.12 is greater than 1.02. Specific behaviours  value of 𝐹 for c",
