    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (7 marks) An investor owned 700 shares in two companies, as shown in the table below. Company Number of shares Current market value of share Dividend per share Dividend per share HHA 500 $6.00 − 3% MMJ 200 $2.50 60c − (a) Determine the total market value of these shares. (2 marks) (b) Both companies are about to pay dividends to shareholders. Determine the total dividend that the investor will receive. (3 marks) (c) Calculate the percentage dividend per share (the dividend yield) for the MMJ company. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-153-7 Question 6 (7 marks) An investor owned 700 shares in two companies, as shown in the table below. Company Number of shares Current market value of share Dividend per share Dividend per share HHA 500 $6.00 − 3% MMJ 200 $2.50 60c − (a) Determine the total market value of these shares. (2 marks) (b) Both companies are about to pay dividends to shareholders. Determine the total dividend that the investor will receive. (3 marks) (c) Calculate the percent dividend per share (the dividend yield) for MMJ shares. (2 marks) Solution HHA: 3000 × 0.03 = 90 MMJ: 200 × 0.60 = 120 Total dividend: 90 + 120 = $210 Specific behaviours  first dividend  second dividend  states total dividend No f/t Solution 60c / 250c x 100% = 24% Specific behaviours  indicates correct calculation  correct percentage Solution 500 × 6 = 3000, 200 × 2.5 = 500 Total value: 3000 + 500 = $3 500 Specific behaviours  values for each company  states total value No f/t",
