    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (8 marks) Consider the matrices 𝐴= [5 −2], 𝐵= [−2 1 3 4] and 𝐶= [−3 −1 2 0 ]. (a) Calculate (i) 𝐵+ 4𝐶. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴𝐶. (2 marks) (iii) 𝐵2. (2 marks) (b) Given that 3𝐵−𝐶+ 𝑥𝐼= [ℎ 4 7 20], where 𝐼 is the identity matrix, determine the value of the constant 𝑥 and the value of the constant ℎ. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-153-7 Question 7 (8 marks) Consider the matrices 𝐴= [5 −2], 𝐵= [−2 1 3 4] and 𝐶= [−3 −1 2 0 ]. (a) Calculate (i) 𝐵+ 4𝐶. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴𝐶. (2 marks) (iii) 𝐵2. (2 marks) (b) Given that 3𝐵−𝐶+ 𝑥𝐼= [ℎ 4 7 20], where 𝐼 is the identity matrix, determine the value of the constant 𝑥 and the value of the constant ℎ. (3 marks) Solution [−2 1 3 4] + [−12 −4 8 0 ] = [−14 −3 11 4 ] Specific behaviours  correct result Solution [5 −2] × [−3 −1 2 0 ] = [−19 −5] Specific behaviours  product is correct size  correct product Solution [−2 1 3 4] × [−2 1 3 4] = [7 2 6 19] Specific behaviours  at least two correct elements in product  correct product Solution 3𝐵−𝐶= [−3 4 7 12] [−3 4 7 12] + [𝑥 0 0 𝑥] = [ℎ 4 7 20] 12 + 𝑥= 20 ⇒𝑥= 8 −3 + 8 = ℎ⇒ℎ= 5 Specific behaviours  Demonstrates the xI matrix  value of 𝑥  value of ℎ f/t from student’s x",
