    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN085-153-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (7 marks) A young person qualifies for a government allowance of $450 per fortnight, provided their fortnightly income is no more than $430. In any fortnight that a person earns more than $430, the allowance will be reduced by 50 cents in the dollar for earnings over $430 and up to $530, and reduced by 60 cents in the dollar for earnings over $530. A person who qualifies for the allowance earns $30 per hour working in an office. Each week they work 5 hours on Tuesday and 4 hours on Wednesday. (a) Calculate their fortnightly earnings. (2 marks) (b) Determine their fortnightly government allowance. (3 marks) (c) Determine the reduction in the fortnightly government allowance calculated in part (b) if they worked an extra 5 hours every Monday. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN085-153-7 Question 8 (7 marks) A young person qualifies for a government allowance of $450 per fortnight, provided their fortnightly income is no more than $430. In any fortnight that a person earns more than $430, the allowance will be reduced by 50 cents in the dollar for earnings over $430 and up to $530, and reduced by 60 cents in the dollar for earnings over $530. A person who qualifies for the allowance earns $30 per hour working in an office. Each week they work 5 hours on Tuesday and 4 hours on Wednesday. (a) Calculate their fortnightly earnings. (2 marks) (b) Determine their fortnightly government allowance. (3 marks) (c) Determine the reduction in the fortnightly government allowance calculated in part (b) if they worked an extra 5 hours every Monday. (2 marks) Solution Extra earnings: 5 × 2 × 30 = $300 Reduction will be: 300 × 0.6 = $180 Specific behaviours  indicates extra earnings  correct reduction Solution First band deduction: 530 −430 = 100, 100 × 0.5 = $50 Second band deduction: 540 −530 = 10, 10 × 0.6 = $6 Allowance remaining: 450 −50 −6 = $394 Specific behaviours  deduction for first band  deduction f",
