    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-173-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (10 marks) One weekend, a company operated three boats to run river trips. On Saturday, boats 𝑃, 𝑄 and 𝑅 carried 52, 66 and 45 adults, and 28, 42 and 22 children, respectively. (a) Represent this information in a 2 × 3 matrix 𝑋, with adults in the top row, and boats in alphabetical order. (1 mark) On Sunday, a total of 97 adults and 88 children took trips. Boats 𝑄 and 𝑅 carried an equal number of children and boat 𝑅 carried 30 adults. Compared to Saturday, boat 𝑃 took 19 fewer adults and 4 more children. (b) Represent the Sunday passenger numbers in matrix 𝑌, using the same row and column labels as matrix 𝑋. (3 marks)",
