    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-8 Question 13 (8 marks) Six decorative spheres are packed into a cuboid shaped box. Each sphere has a diameter of 14 cm, and the internal dimensions of the box are 36 cm by 32.5 cm by 30 cm. (a) Determine the percentage of the space inside the box that the spheres occupy. (4 marks) (b) A thin triangular piece of card 𝐴𝐵𝐶 is inserted into the box to limit the movement of the spheres, as shown in the diagram. Determine the perimeter of the right triangle 𝐴𝐵𝐶. (4 marks) Solution Volume of box: 𝑉𝐵= 36 × 32.5 × 30 = 35 100 cm3. Volume of one sphere of radius 7 cm: 𝑉𝑆= 4 3 × 𝜋× 73 = 1436.76 cm3. Volume occupied by 6 spheres: 𝑉6 = 1436.76 × 6 = 8621 cm3. Percentage of space occupied: 8621 ÷ 35 100 = 24.6% Specific behaviours  volume of box  volume of one sphere  volume occupied by all spheres  calculates percentage Solution Length of diagonal of base: 𝐴𝐶= √32.52 + 362 = 48.5 cm. Length of diagonal of box: 𝐴𝐵= √48.52 + 302 = 57.0 cm. Hence perimeter of card is 48.5 + 57.0 + 30 = 135.5 cm. Specific behaviours  indicates correct use of Pythagoras' Theorem  calculates length of diagonal of base  calculates length of diago",
