    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-8 Question 15 (8 marks) The image shows some recently harvested grain stored in a conical pile on level ground. The top of the pile is 12 m above the ground and the radius of the base is 35 m. (a) Determine the volume of grain contained in the pile. (2 marks) (b) Trucks that can carry a load of 28 tonnes will be used to transport the grain to the local port. If one cubic metre of grain weighs 630 kg, determine the number of truck loads of grain required to move the entire pile of grain to the port. Note that there are 1000 kg in one tonne. (2 marks) (c) Determine the slant height of the conical pile. (2 marks) (d) When rain is forecast, the sloping surface of the grain can be covered with tarpaulins. Calculate the area of grain that needs to be covered. (2 marks) Solution 𝑉= 1 3 × 𝜋× 352 × 12 = 15 394 m3 Specific behaviours  shows correct use of volume formula  calculates volume (correct to at least 3 sf) Solution 𝑠= √122 + 352 = √1369 = 37 m Specific behaviours  shows correct use of Pythagoras' Theorem  calculates correct slant height Solution 𝑊= 15 394 × 630 ÷ 1000 = 9698 tonnes 9698 ÷ 28 = 346.4 Hence will nee",
