    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-193-8 Question 16 (10 marks) (a) Kelly takes a short-term loan of $2400 at 9.6% per annum simple interest for 50 days. Determine the sum of the principal and interest that Kelly must repay at the end of the loan period. (3 marks) (b) An amount of $15 000 is invested at 4.5% per annum compounded annually for 3 years. Determine the total interest earned on this investment over the 3 years. (3 marks) (c) At the start of last year, Syed was employed as a manager with a salary of $86 000. During the year, Syed was awarded a 6.5% pay rise followed by another rise of 7.7% at the start of this year. (i) Determine Syed's salary at the start of this year. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the percentage increase in Syed's salary from the start of last year to the start of this year. (2 marks) Solution 𝐼= 2400 × 9.6 × 50 100 × 365 = 31.56 Repay 2400 + 31.56 = $2431.56. Specific behaviours  correct expression to calculate simple interest  calculates simple interest  calculates sum to repay Solution 𝑆= 86 000 × 1.065 × 1.077 = $98 642.43 Specific behaviours  indicates correct method  calculates new salary Solution 𝐴= 15 000(1.045)3 = 17 ",
