    "questionText": "Question 16 (10 marks) (a) Kelly takes a short-term loan of $2400 at 9.6% per annum simple interest for 50 days. Determine the sum of the principal and interest that Kelly must repay at the end of the loan period. (3 marks) (b) An amount of $15 000 is invested at 4.5% per annum compounded annually for 3 years. Determine the total interest earned on this investment over the 3 years. (3 marks) (c) At the start of last year, Syed was employed as a manager with a salary of $86 000. During the year, Syed was awarded a 6.5% pay rise followed by another rise of 7.7% at the start of this year. (i) Determine Syed's salary at the start of this year. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the percentage increase in Syed's salary from the start of last year to the start of this year. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-8 Question 17 (8 marks) The diagram (not to scale) shows a fabric panel used in the construction of a kite. The panel consists of a 230° sector of a circle with centre 𝑂 and radius 50 cm, and quadrilateral 𝑂𝑃𝑄𝑅 in which 𝑄𝑅= 𝑄𝑃= 108 cm. (a) Calculate the area of the sector. (2 marks) (b) Hence determine the total area of the fabric panel. (3 marks) (c) The panel is to be edged with tape. Calculate the length of tape required. (3 marks) Solution Perimeter of sector, 𝑃: 𝑃= 230 360 × 2 × 𝜋× 50 = 201 cm Total length of tape, 𝐿: 𝐿= 201 + 2 × 108 = 417 cm Specific behaviours  indicates correct method for sector perimeter  calculates sector perimeter  calculates total length of tape Solution Quadrilateral can be split into two right triangles. Area of a triangle: 𝐴= 1 2 × 50 × 108 = 2700 cm2 Hence total area is sector plus two triangles: 𝐴= 5018 + 2 × 2700 = 10 418 cm2 Specific behaviours  splits quadrilateral into two right-triangles  area of one right-triangle  calculates total area Solution 𝐴= 230 360 × 𝜋× 502 = 5018 cm2 Specific behaviours  uses appropriate method  calculates sector area",
