    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "End of questions Question 19 (9 marks) A woodturner takes a solid cylindrical wooden pole of length 66 cm and radius 8 cm and uses a machine to reduce the radius of the middle third of the pole by 30%, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). (a) Calculate, with working, the volume of wood removed by the machine. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-193-8 Question 19 (9 marks) A woodturner takes a solid cylindrical wooden pole of length 66 cm and radius 8 cm and uses a machine to reduce the radius of the middle third of the pole by 30%, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). (a) Calculate, with working, the volume of wood removed by the machine. (4 marks) Solution Volume removed will be difference in volume of middle section of pole as a cylinder with height of 66 ÷ 3 = 22 cm and initial radius of 8 cm and final radius of 8 × 0.7 = 5.6 cm. 𝑉1 = 𝜋× 82 × 22 = 4423 cm3 𝑉2 = 𝜋× 5.62 × 22 = 2167 cm3 Hence volume removed is 4423 −2167 = 2256 cm3. Specific behaviours  explanation of method or describes each step  uses correct dimensions for one cylinder  correctly calculates volume of one cylinder  correct volume removed",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/sem-1-exams-ross-2022-rossmoyne-2022-yr11-apps-u1ca-s2x-p015-question-a27331ed87.jpg",
