    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-193-8 (b) Explaining your method, determine the total surface area of the remaining object. (5 marks) Solution TSA of one large end cylinder: 𝐴1 = 2𝜋× 82 + 2𝜋× 8 × 22 = 402.1 + 1105.84 = 1508 cm2 Area of curved surface of small middle cylinder: 𝐴2 = 2𝜋× 5.6 × 22 = 774 cm2 Area of one circular end of small middle cylinder: 𝐴3 = 𝜋× 5.62 = 98.5 cm2 TSA of remaining object: 𝐴= 2𝐴1 + 𝐴2 −2𝐴3 = 3016 + 774 −197 = 3593 cm2 Specific behaviours  explanation of method or describes each step  correct use of TSA formula for one cylinder  correctly calculates TSA of one cylinder  correct use of circle formula for cylinder ends  correct TSA of object",
