    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has seven questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) (a) Evaluate 30 −20 ÷ 2 + 3. (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of 𝑣 when 𝑡= 3, 𝑎= 2.5 and 𝑣= 2𝑎𝑡2 −(𝑡+ 5)(𝑎−2). (2 marks) (c) Evaluate the expression 𝑎+ 16 √5𝑎−𝑏 when 𝑎= 8 and 𝑏= 4. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-3 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has seven questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) (a) Evaluate 30 −20 ÷ 2 + 3. (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of 𝑣 when 𝑡= 3, 𝑎= 2.5 and 𝑣= 2𝑎𝑡2 −(𝑡+ 5)(𝑎−2). (2 marks) (c) Evaluate the expression 𝑎+ 16 √5𝑎−𝑏 when 𝑎= 8 and 𝑏= 4. (2 marks) Solution 𝑎+ 16 √5𝑎−𝑏 = 8 + 16 √5(8) −4 = 24 √40 −4 = 24 √36 = 24 ÷ 6 = 4 Specific behaviours  substitutes  evaluates Solution 𝑣= 2(2.5)(3)2 −(3 + 5)(2.5 −2) = 5(9) −8(0.5) = 45 −4 = 41 Specific behaviours  substitutes  evaluates Solution 30 −20 ÷ 2 + 3 = 30 −10 + 3 = 23 Specific behaviours  correctly evaluates",
