    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 2 (5 marks) Lara works part-time as a porter at a hotel. Her timesheet for three shifts she worked in January this year is shown below. Day Start time Finish time Monday 3: 45 pm 10: 15 pm Tuesday 11: 15 am 7: 45 pm Wednesday (Australia Day holiday) 7: 30 am 3: 00 pm The hotel pays porters $20 per hour, except for (i) hours worked after 5: 45 pm when time-and-a- half is paid; and (ii) all hours worked on a public holiday when double time is paid. Determine Lara's pay for the three shifts she worked.",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-3 Question 2 (5 marks) Lara works part-time as a porter at a hotel. Her timesheet for three shifts she worked in January this year is shown below. Day Start time Finish time Monday 3: 45 pm 10: 15 pm Tuesday 11: 15 am 7: 45 pm Wednesday (Australia Day holiday) 7: 30 am 3: 00 pm The hotel pays porters $20 per hour, except for (i) hours worked after 5: 45 pm when time-and-a- half is paid; and (ii) all hours worked on a public holiday when double time is paid. Determine Lara's pay for the three shifts she worked. Solution Normal hours (until 5: 45 pm) on Mon and Tues in hours and minutes: 2h + 6h 30m = 8h 30m Time-and-a-half hours (after 5: 45 pm) on Mon and Tues: 4h 30m + 2h = 6h 30m Double time on Wed: 7h 30m Using bonus rates, time paid, in hours: 8.5 + (6.5 × 1.5) + (7.5 × 2) = 8.5 + 9.75 + 15 = 33.25 ℎ𝑟𝑠 Lara's pay for three shifts: 33.25 × 20 = $665 Specific behaviours  indicates hours worked at normal rates  indicates hours worked at time-and-a-half  indicates hours worked at double time  correctly adjusts time worked by bonus rates  calculates total pay Alternative solutions NB Alternative methods exist, such a",
