    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 3 (8 marks) (a) State the size of the following matrices in the form 𝑎× 𝑏. (i) [ 12 −3 −7 0 5 8 ] (1 mark) (ii) The identity matrix with 6 rows. (1 mark) (b) The column matrix 𝐙 has 4 elements. Write a suitable matrix 𝐙, given that its 4 elements are all whole numbers and have a sum of 10. (2 marks) (c) Write as a single matrix (i) 2 [ 4 −1 −5 3 ] + [ 1 7 −4 0]. (2 marks) (ii) [−3 5] [−4 1 2 −3]. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-3 Question 3 (8 marks) (a) State the size of the following matrices in the form 𝑎× 𝑏. (i) [ 12 −3 −7 0 5 8 ] (1 mark) (ii) The identity matrix with 6 rows. (1 mark) (b) The column matrix 𝐙 has 4 elements. Write a suitable matrix 𝐙, given that its 4 elements are all whole numbers and have a sum of 10. (2 marks) (c) Write as a single matrix (i) 2 [ 4 −1 −5 3 ] + [ 1 7 −4 0]. (2 marks) (ii) [−3 5] [−4 1 2 −3]. (2 marks) Solution [−3 5] [−4 1 2 −3] = [12 + 10 −3 −15] = [22 −18] Specific behaviours  1 × 2 matrix with one element correct  correct single matrix Solution 2 [ 4 −1 −5 3 ] + [ 1 7 −4 0] = [ 8 −2 −10 6 ] + [ 1 7 −4 0] = [ 9 5 −14 6] Specific behaviours  correctly calculates scalar multiple  correct single matrix Solution One of many possibilities is 𝐙= [ 1 2 3 4 ]. Specific behaviours  correct size matrix  elements are non-negative integers with correct sum Solution Size is 3 × 2. Specific behaviours  correct size in required form Solution Size is 6 × 6. Specific behaviours  correct size in required form",
