    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (10 marks) A company manufactures Regular and Special liquid level sensors (shown at right), with each model requiring different numbers of diodes, and capacitors as shown in matrix 𝐀: 𝐀= [4 2 3 1] The numbers in the first row of 𝐀 are the components required for the Special model, with the first and second columns showing the number of diodes and capacitors respectively. (a) Write down the element 𝑎2,1 of 𝐀 and describe what this number represents. (2 marks) The cost of diodes and capacitors from Supplier X is 50 and 40 cents respectively, whilst from Supplier Y is 40 and 30 cents respectively. (b) Arrange this information into cost matrix 𝐂 and hence determine the matrix 𝐃= 𝐀× 𝐂. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-3 Question 5 (10 marks) A company manufactures Regular and Special liquid level sensors (shown at right), with each model requiring different numbers of diodes, and capacitors as shown in matrix 𝐀: : 𝐀= [4 2 3 1] The numbers in the first row of 𝐀 are the components required for the Special model, with the first and second columns showing the number of diodes and capacitors respectively. (a) Write down the element 𝑎2,1 of 𝐀 and describe what this number represents. (2 marks) The cost of diodes and capacitors from Supplier X is 50 and 40 cents respectively, whilst from Supplier Y is 40 and 30 cents respectively. (b) Arrange this information into cost matrix 𝐂 and hence determine the matrix 𝐃= 𝐀× 𝐂. (3 marks) Solution 𝑎2,1 = 3. This number represents the number of diodes required for a Regular model. Specific behaviours  correct element  identifies correct component and model Solution 𝐂= [50 40 40 30] , 𝐃= 𝐀× 𝐂= [4 2 3 1] × [50 40 40 30] = [280 220 190 150] Specific behaviours  correct cost matrix (columns can be swapped - follow through in c)  calculates at least one correct element of product  correct product",
