    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (c) Explain what the element 𝑑1,2 of matrix 𝐃 represents. (2 marks) (d) The company has an order for 300 Regular and 100 Special models. Show use of matrix multiplication to calculate a 1 × 1 matrix that represents the total cost, in dollars, of the components required for this order from Supplier X. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-193-3 (c) Explain what the element 𝑑1,2 of matrix 𝐃 represents. (2 marks) (d) The company have an order for 300 Regular and 100 Special models. Show use of matrix multiplication to calculate a 1 × 1 matrix that represents the total cost, in dollars, of the components required for this order from Supplier X. (3 marks) Solution [100 300] × [2.80 (𝑠) 1.90 (𝑟)] = [850] or equivalent, such as... 1 100 × 300 × [280 190] = [850] Or [300 100] × [1.90 (𝑟) 2.80 (𝑠)] = [850] If students do this [300 100] × [2.80 (𝑠) 1.90 (𝑟)] = [1030] (2 out of 3 marks only) Specific behaviours  shows appropriate order and cost matrices  shows use of matrix multiplication  correct total cost matrix Solution 𝑑1,2 represents the total cost of components used in a Special model from Supplier Y. Specific behaviours  indicates total cost of components  identifies correct model and supplier",
