    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (8 marks) The sketch diagram (not drawn to scale) shows a plot of land bound by six straight sides. The length of each side is shown in metres. (a) A fence that costs $30 per metre is to be erected around the perimeter of the plot. Determine the total cost of fencing. (3 marks) (b) Once the fence is in place, the plot is to be treated with weedkiller at a rate of 10 mL per square metre. The weedkiller is sold in 3 litre containers. Determine, with justification, the number of containers of weedkiller required. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-193-3 Question 6 (8 marks) The sketch diagram (not drawn to scale) shows a plot of land bound by six straight sides. The length of each side is shown in metres. (a) A fence that costs $30 per metre is to be erected around the perimeter of the plot. Determine the total cost of fencing. (3 marks) (b) Once the fence is in place, the plot is to be treated with weedkiller at a rate of 10 mL per square metre. The weedkiller is sold in 3 litre containers. Determine, with justification, the number of containers of weedkiller required. (5 marks) Solution 𝑃= 50 + 41 + 39 + 20 + 20 + 20 = 190 m 𝐶= 190 × 30 = $5700 Specific behaviours  indicates correct calculation for perimeter  indicates correct calculation for total cost  correct total cost Solution Rectangle: 𝐴𝑅= 50 × 40 = 2000 Square: 𝐴𝑆= 20 × 20 = 400 Triangle: 𝐴𝑇= 1 2 × 9 × 40 = 180 Total area: 𝐴= 2000 −400 + 180 = 1780 m2 Litres of weedkiller: 1780 × 0.01 = 17.8 L and so 6 containers will be required. Specific behaviours  correctly partitions plot into suitable composite areas  calculates all composite areas correctly  calculates total area  calculates litres (or mL) of ",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/sem-1-exams-ross-2022-rossmoyne-2022-yr11-apps-u1cf-s1-p010-question-3f428587d2.jpg",
