    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-193-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar pentagons 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸 and 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′. The lengths of some of the sides are shown in centimetres. (a) Determine the length of side 𝐴′𝐸′ and the length of side 𝐷𝐸. (3 marks) The perimeter of 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′ is 120 cm. (b) Determine the length of side 𝐶𝐷. (2 marks) The area of 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸 is 50 cm2. (c) Determine the area of 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-193-3 Question 7 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar pentagons 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸 and 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′. The lengths of some of the sides are shown in centimetres. (a) Determine the length of side 𝐴′𝐸′ and the length of side 𝐷𝐸. (3 marks) The perimeter of 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′ is 120 cm. (b) Determine the length of side 𝐶𝐷. (2 marks) The area of 𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸 is 50 cm2. (c) Determine the area of 𝐴′𝐵′𝐶′𝐷′𝐸′. (2 marks) Solution Scale factor: 𝐵′𝐶′ 𝐵𝐶= 24 6 = 4 𝐴′𝐸′ = 12 × 4 = 48 cm, 𝐷𝐸= 20 ÷ 4 = 5 cm Specific behaviours  calculates scale factor (either 4 or 1 4 ⁄ )  length of 𝐴′𝐸′  length of 𝐷𝐸 Solution 𝐴′𝐵′ = 4 × 4 = 16 𝐶′𝐷′ = 120 −(16 + 24 + 48 + 20) = 120 −108 = 12 𝐶𝐷= 12 ÷ 4 = 3 cm 𝑃𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐸= 120 ÷ 4 = 30 𝐶𝐷= 30 −(4 + 6 + 5 + 12) = 30 −27 = 3 cm Specific behaviours  uses scale factor to obtain 𝐴′𝐵′ or small pentagon perimeter  correct side length Solution Area scale factor is 42 = 16 Area = 50 × 16 = 800 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct area scale factor  uses area scale factor to obtain area",
