    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has seven questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (7 marks) Consider the matrices 𝑷= [ 2 0 −1 1] , 𝑸= [3 0], 𝑹= [−3 0 ] and 𝑺= [4 2 0 1 0 −2]. (a) The size of the matrix that has a zero in its second row and first column is 𝑎× 𝑏. State the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (1 mark) (b) Calculate 𝑷+ 4𝑰, where 𝑰 is the 2 × 2 identity matrix. (2 marks) (c) The sum of matrices 𝑺 and 𝑻 is [3 2 1 3 2 1]. Determine matrix 𝑻. (2 marks) (d) Calculate the matrix product 𝑷𝑺. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-3 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has seven questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (7 marks) Consider the matrices 𝑷= [ 2 0 −1 1] , 𝑸= [3 0], 𝑹= [−3 0 ] and 𝑺= [4 2 0 1 0 −2]. (a) The size of the matrix that has a zero in its second row and first column is 𝑎× 𝑏. State the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (1 mark) (b) Calculate 𝑷+ 4𝑰, where 𝑰 is the 2 × 2 identity matrix. (2 marks) (c) The sum of matrices 𝑺 and 𝑻 is [3 2 1 3 2 1]. Determine matrix 𝑻. (2 marks) (d) Calculate the matrix product 𝑷𝑺. (2 marks) Solution The size of matrix 𝑹 is 2 × 1 and so 𝑎= 2 and 𝑏= 1. Specific behaviours ✓ correct values Solution 𝑷𝑺= [ 2 0 −1 1] × [4 2 0 1 0 −2] = [ 8 4 0 −3 −2 −2] Specific behaviours ✓ at least three correct entries ✓ correct product Solution 𝑻= [3 2 1 3 2 1] −[4 2 0 1 0 −2] = [−1 0 1 2 2 3] Specific behaviours ✓ at least three correct entries ✓ correct matrix 𝑻 Solution 𝑷+ 4𝑰= [ 2 0 −1 1] + 4 [1 0 0 1] = [ 6 0 −1 5] Specific behaviours ✓ correctly indicates 4𝑰 ✓ correct matrix result",
