    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-213-3 Question 2 (6 marks) (a) Given , (i) find d if 𝑎= −1, 𝑏= 4, 𝑐= 1 and 𝑒= −10. (2 marks) (ii) find c if 𝑎= −2, 𝑏= 3, 𝑑= −4 and 𝑒= −2. (2 marks) (b) Simplify the expression 14 + 2𝑥 𝑥2 + 𝑥−8 when 𝑥= −5. (2 marks) Solution 14 + 2𝑥 𝑥2 + 𝑥−8 = 14 + 2(−5) (−5)2 + (−5) −8 = 14 −10 25 −5 −8 = 4 12 = 1 3 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly evaluates numerator ✓ correctly evaluates denominator -1 mark if not simplified Solution −2 × 3 𝑐 −4 = −2 𝑐= −3 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly substitutes ✓ correct value Solution −1 × 4 1 + 𝑑= −10 𝑑= −6 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly substitutes ✓ correct value",
