    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-213-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (6 marks) These two triangles are similar. Note that they are not drawn to scale. (a) Write a similarity statement for the triangles above. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of the missing side. (1 mark) (c) The area of ΔWXY is 192cm2. Use the length scale factor to calculate the area of ΔABC. (2 marks) (d) These triangles are the front view of two similar triangular prisms. What is the ratio of their volumes? (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-213-3 Question 6 (6 marks) These two triangles are similar. Note that they are not drawn to scale. (a) Write a similarity statement for the triangles above. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of the missing side. (1 mark) (c) The area of ΔWXY is 192cm2. Use the length scale factor to calculate the area of ΔABC. (2 marks) (d) These triangles are the front view of two similar triangular prisms. What is the ratio of their volumes? (1 mark) Solution ∆𝐴𝐵𝐶 ~ ∆𝑊𝑌𝑋 (𝑆𝐴𝑆) Specific behaviours ✓ letters in correct order with correct similarity symbol ✓ states similarity test Solution 𝐵𝐶= 28 ÷ 4 = 7 𝑐𝑚 Specific behaviours ✓ correct length Solution 𝐴𝑆𝐹= 𝐿𝑆𝐹2 = 42 = 16 𝐴= 192 ÷ 16 = 12 𝑐𝑚2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct area scale factor ✓ correct area Alternate Solution 𝑆𝐹= 12: 42 = 1: 16 𝐴= 192 ÷ 16 = 12 𝑐𝑚2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct ratio for scale factor ✓ correct area Solution 𝑉𝑆𝐹= 𝐿𝑆𝐹3 = 43 = 64 Specific behaviours ✓ correct volume scale factor No mark if left it as 43 Alternate Solution 𝑆𝐹= 13: 43 = 1: 64 Specific behaviours ✓ correct ratio for scale factor No mark if left it as 13: 43",
