    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-213-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (7 marks) (a) The gear ratio 𝑅 of a mechanical system is calculated using 𝑅= 𝑑2 𝑑1 + 8 − 𝑑1 𝑑2 −1, where 𝑑1 and 𝑑2 are the diameters of two cogs. Determine the value of 𝑅 when 𝑑1 = 4 cm and 𝑑2 = 9 cm. (2 marks) (b) When an object is placed at a distance of 𝑥 cm from a lens with focal length of 𝑓 cm, its image will appear at a distance 𝑑 cm from the lens, where 𝑑= 𝑥𝑓 𝑥−𝑓 . An object is 12.5 cm from a lens that has a focal length of 10 cm. Determine how far its image will appear from the lens. (2 marks) (c) The velocity of a model car is given by 𝑣= √𝑢2 + 2𝑎𝑠 cm/s. Determine (i) the velocity of the model car when 𝑢= 4, 𝑎= 1.5 and 𝑠= 3. (1 mark) (ii) the change in velocity of the model car when 𝑢= 4 and 𝑎= 1.5, as the value of 𝑠 increases from 3 to 16. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-213-3 Question 7 (7 marks) (a) The gear ratio 𝑅 of a mechanical system is calculated using 𝑅= 𝑑2 𝑑1 + 8 − 𝑑1 𝑑2 −1, where 𝑑1 and 𝑑2 are the diameters of two cogs. Determine the value of 𝑅 when 𝑑1 = 4 cm and 𝑑2 = 9 cm. (2 marks) (b) When an object is placed at a distance of 𝑥 cm from a lens with focal length of 𝑓 cm, its image will appear at a distance 𝑑 cm from the lens, where 𝑑= 𝑥𝑓 𝑥−𝑓 . An object is 12.5 cm from a lens that has a focal length of 10 cm. Determine how far its image will appear from the lens. (2 marks) (c) The velocity of a model car is given by 𝑣= √𝑢2 + 2𝑎𝑠 cm/s. Determine (i) the velocity of the model car when 𝑢= 4, 𝑎= 1.5 and 𝑠= 3. (1 mark) (ii) the change in velocity of the model car when 𝑢= 4 and 𝑎= 1.5, as the value of 𝑠 increases from 3 to 16. (2 marks) Solution 𝑑= 12.5 × 10 12.5 −10 = 125 2.5 = 250 5 = 50 cm Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes and evaluates both parts of fraction ✓ correct distance Solution 𝑅= 9 4 + 8 − 4 9 −1 = 9 12 −4 8 = 3 4 −1 2 = 1 4 (= 0.25) Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes and simplifies denominators ✓ correct simplified value Allow 1 mark for 9 12 − 4 8 Solution 𝑣= √42 + 2 ×",
