    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (8 marks) Casual staff at a business are paid according to their age, as shown in the following table: Age in years 16 17 18 19 20 21 or older Hourly pay rate ($) 14.95 15.54 20.14 22.72 25.31 27.89 The following spreadsheet is used by the business to calculate the gross weekly wage for each of their casual staff, who are paid time-and-a-half for all overtime. Name Age Normal hours Overtime hours Gross weekly wage ($) Juke 18 21 3 513.57 Kiki 16 25 2 Lacy 27 22 𝑄 697.25 Moya 19 𝑃 0 522.56 (a) Calculate the gross weekly wage for Kiki. (3 marks) (b) The business makes a contribution equal to 10.5% of each person’s gross weekly wage into their superannuation fund. Determine the contribution, to the nearest cent, that Lacy will receive. (1 mark) (c) Determine the value of 𝑃 and the value of 𝑄 in the table. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-213-4 Question 8 (8 marks) Casual staff at a business are paid according to their age, as shown in the following table: Age in years 16 17 18 19 20 21 or older Hourly pay rate ($) 14.95 15.54 20.14 22.72 25.31 27.89 The following spreadsheet is used by the business to calculate the gross weekly wage for each of their casual staff, who are paid time-and-a-half for all overtime. Name Age Normal hours Overtime hours Gross weekly wage ($) Juke 18 21 3 513.57 Kiki 16 25 2 Lacy 27 22 𝑄 697.25 Moya 19 𝑃 0 522.56 (a) Calculate the gross weekly wage for Kiki. (3 marks) (b) The business makes a contribution equal to 10.5% of each person’s gross weekly wage into their superannuation fund. Determine the contribution, to the nearest cent, that Lacy will receive. (1 mark) (c) Determine the value of 𝑃 and the value of 𝑄 in the table. (4 marks) Solution Pay rate for Moya is 22.72 and so 𝑃= 522.56 ÷ 22.72 = 23. Pay rate for Lacy is 27.89 and 22 × 27.89 = 613.58. 697.25 −613.58 = 83.67 𝑌= 83.67 ÷ 1.5 ÷ 27.89 = 2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value of 𝑃 ✓ finds normal hours pay and subtracts ✓ shows correct method to find overtime hours ✓ c",
