    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (7 marks) Information about shares in a company at the end of 2021 and 2022 is shown in the table below. Year Share price ($) Earnings per share (cents) Annual dividend per share (cents) 2021 10.64 76 58 2022 10.45 95 68 (a) An investor owned 8250 shares in the company. Determine the annual dividend payment, in dollars, that they received in 2021. (2 marks) (b) Determine the dividend yield (percentage dividend paid) in the year 2022. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for both years and hence state in which year an investor would have paid the least for each dollar of the company’s earnings. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-4 Question 9 (7 marks) Information about shares in a company at the end of 2021 and 2022 is shown in the table below. Year Share price ($) Earnings per share (cents) Annual dividend per share (cents) 2021 10.64 76 58 2022 10.45 95 68 (a) An investor owned 8250 shares in the company. Determine the annual dividend payment, in dollars, that they received in 2021. (2 marks) (b) Determine the dividend yield (percentage dividend paid) in the year 2022. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for both years and hence state in which year an investor would have paid the least for each dollar of the company’s earnings. (3 marks) Solution 68 ÷ 1045 = 0.065 = 6.5% Specific behaviours ✓ shows quotient of annual DPS and share price ✓ correct percentage Solution P/E2021 = 10.64 ÷ 0.76 = 14 P/E2022 = 10.45 ÷ 0.95 = 11 Investor paid least in the year 2022. Specific behaviours ✓ shows quotient of share price and EPS for one year ✓ shows correct P/E ratio for one year ✓ shows two P/E ratios and chooses year of smallest Solution 8250 × 58 ÷ 100 = $4785 Specific behaviours ✓ shows product of annual DPS and number of shares ✓ c",
