    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (9 marks) Five students have just formed a study group and want to communicate via email. • Dave only has an email address for Eula • Eula only has an email address for Gugu and Heng • Faye only has an email address for Eula • Gugu only has an email address for Dave and Faye • Heng only has an email address for Dave (a) Construct matrix 𝑵 to represent this communication network, with names in alphabetical order and with element 𝑛𝑖,𝑗 equal to 1 if person 𝑖 can send an email to person 𝑗, and equal to 0 if not. Assume that nobody can send an email to themself. (2 marks) (b) Determine matrix 𝑴, where 𝑴= 𝑵2. (2 marks) (c) State the value of element 𝑚4,2 and explain in the context of the question what this value means. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-213-4 Question 10 (9 marks) Five students have just formed a study group and want to communicate via email. • Dave only has an email address for Eula • Eula only has an email address for Gugu and Heng • Faye only has an email address for Eula • Gugu only has an email address for Dave and Faye • Heng only has an email address for Dave (a) Construct matrix 𝑵 to represent this communication network, with names in alphabetical order and with element 𝑛𝑖,𝑗 equal to 1 if person 𝑖 can send an email to person 𝑗, and equal to 0 if not. Assume that nobody can send an email to themself. (2 marks) (b) Determine matrix 𝑴, where 𝑴= 𝑵2. (2 marks) (c) State the value of element 𝑚4,2 and explain in the context of the question what this value means. (2 marks) Solution 𝑵= [ 0 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 1 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 0 1 0 0 0 0] Specific behaviours ✓ matrix contains seven 1’s and leading diagonal all 0’s ✓ correct matrix Solution 𝑚4,2 = 2. Gugu has 2 ways to send an email to Eula via a third person. Specific behaviours ✓ correct value ✓ correct explanation Solution 𝑴= 𝑵2 = [ 0 0 0 1 1 2 0 1 0 0 0 0 0 1 1 0 2 0 0 0 0 1 0 0 0] Specific behaviours ✓",
