    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (8 marks) The diagram (not to scale) shows the dimensions in millimetres of a solid metal elbow used in the furniture industry. All of the surfaces of the elbow meet at right-angles. (a) Determine the total surface area of the metal elbow. (4 marks) (b) A new elbow is made so that it is a similar figure to the one above and the edge that was 54 mm is now 324 mm long. Determine (i) the length, in the new elbow, of the edge that was 45 mm long. (2 marks) (ii) the volume of the new elbow, given that the volume of the original elbow is 105.5𝑐𝑚3. (2 marks)",
