    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-4 (d) Use the unit cost method to determine which supplier the shipyard should buy steel ballast from so that the cost per cubic centimetre is minimised. (3 marks) Solution RR: 650 ÷ 2572 = 0.253 cents per cm3. SS: 550 ÷ 1779 = 0.309 cents per cm3. TT: 750 ÷ 2160 = 0.347 cents per cm3. Hence best value steel ballast is supplied by Ronda Reno. Specific behaviours ✓ calculates one unit cost correctly ✓ calculates all unit costs correctly ✓ correctly states best value supplier Alternate Solution RR: 2572 ÷ 6.50 = 395 cm3 per $1. SS: 1779 ÷ 6.50 = 323 cm3 per $1. TT: 2160 ÷ 7.50 = 288 cm3 per $1. Hence best value steel ballast is supplied by Ronda Reno. Specific behaviours ✓ calculates one unit cost correctly ✓ calculates all unit costs correctly ✓ correctly states best value supplier",
