    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (8 marks) The price of a classic car in need of restoration was $8800. Laine bought the car, borrowing the full purchase price from a bank at a rate of 13.2% per annum simple interest. (a) Determine the interest owed on this loan after six months. (2 marks) Restoring the car cost a total of $17 350, including parts, labour and loan interest. Laine then sold the car for $31 600. (b) Calculate the profit that Laine made from the car restoration. (1 mark) (c) Determine the percentage increase in the value of the car from its initial value of $8800 to its restored value of $31 600. (2 marks) (d) Laine considered a loan for the purchase price of $8800 from another bank that charged a rate of 11.5% per annum compounded annually. Determine the interest that would accumulate on this loan after two years. (3 marks)",
