    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF The business sells the crema, espresso and mocha coffee beans for $32, $36 and $43 per kilogram respectively. (e) Represent the selling prices in matrix 𝑷, so that 𝑷 can be multiplied with matrix 𝑨 to produce a meaningful result. (1 mark) (f) The three matrices 𝑨, 𝑪 and 𝑷 can be multiplied together, not necessarily in that order, to produce a meaningful result. Clearly showing the order you use, determine the resulting matrix and describe what it represents. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-213-4 The business sells the crema, espresso and mocha coffee beans for $32, $36 and $43 per kilogram respectively. (e) Represent the selling prices in matrix 𝑷, so that 𝑷 can be multiplied with matrix 𝑨 to produce a meaningful result. (1 mark) (f) The three matrices 𝑨, 𝑪 and 𝑷 can be multiplied together, not necessarily in that order, to produce a meaningful result. Clearly showing the order you use, determine the resulting matrix and describe what it represents. (3 marks) Solution 𝑪× 𝑨× 𝑷= [1 1 1] × [ 25.5 13.5 10.0 33.0 22.5 8.5 39.5 19.5 12.5 ] × [ 32 36 43 ] = [6467] The result shows the total revenue from sales of coffee beans at the three stores during the week. Note that all other matrix products produce meaningless results Specific behaviours ✓ shows correct order of multiplication ✓ correct matrix product ✓ correct description Solution 𝑷= [ 32 36 43 ] Specific behaviours ✓ correct matrix",
