    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-213-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (8 marks) A solid prism of length 32 cm has a composite cross-section as shown in the diagram (not to scale), in which a square of side 11 cm has a quarter- circle of radius 7 cm removed. (a) Determine the area of the composite cross-section. (3 marks) (b) Calculate the volume of the solid prism, rounding your answer to the nearest 10 cubic cm. (2 marks) (c) All the edges where the various surfaces meet must be trimmed with a thin silver wire. Determine the total length of wire required. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-213-4 Question 19 (8 marks) A solid prism of length 32 cm has a composite cross-section as shown in the diagram (not to scale), in which a square of side 11 cm has a quarter- circle of radius 7 cm removed. (a) Determine the area of the composite cross-section. (3 marks) (b) Calculate the volume of the solid prism, rounding your answer to the nearest 10 cubic cm. (2 marks) (c) All the edges where the various surfaces meet must be trimmed with a thin silver wire. Determine the total length of wire required. (3 marks) Solution Quarter of circumference of circle: 1 4 × 2 × 𝜋× 7 = 11.0 Edge of composite cross-section: 4 + 11 + 11 + 4 + 11.0 = 41 Total edge length: 5 × 32 + 2 × 41 = 160 + 82 = 242 cm. Specific behaviours ✓ quarter of circle ✓ edge of cross-section ✓ total edge length Solution 𝑉= 82.5 × 32 = 2640 cm3 Hence volume is 2640 cm3 to the nearest 10 cubic cm. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct calculation ✓ correct volume, rounded Solution Area of square is 11 × 11 = 121 Area of quadrant is 1 4 × 𝜋× 72 = 38.5 Area of composite is 121 −38.5 = 82.5 cm2. Specific behaviours ✓ area of square ✓ area of quadrant ✓ a",
