    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-233-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 1 (4 marks) (a) Determine the value of the expression 15 𝑥2 −√𝑦 when 𝑥= 4 and 𝑦= 36. (2 marks) (b) Use the formula 𝐴= ℎ 2 (𝑎+ 𝑏) to determine the value of 𝐴 when 𝑎= 15, 𝑏= 27 and ℎ= 10. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-233-3 Question 1 (4 marks) (a) Determine the value of the expression 15 𝑥2 −√𝑦 when 𝑥= 4 and 𝑦= 36. (2 marks) (b) Use the formula 𝐴= ℎ 2 (𝑎+ 𝑏) to determine the value of 𝐴 when 𝑎= 15, 𝑏= 27 and ℎ= 10. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴= 10 2 (15 + 27) = 10 2 × 42 = 10 × 21 = 210 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly substitutes and simplifies bracketed term ✓ correct value of 𝐴 Solution 15 42 −√36 = 15 16 −6 = 15 10 = 3 2 = 1.5 Specific behaviours ✓ simplifies denominator ✓ simplifies fraction or obtains decimal equivalent",
