    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 2 (8 marks) (a) An item is priced at $135 excluding GST. Determine the price of the item once 10% GST has been included. (2 marks) (b) A homeowner is offered a 2% discount for early payment of their $1700 annual council rates bill. How much would they pay if they took up the offer? (2 marks) (c) A watch enthusiast paid $500 for a timepiece but later sold it for just $440. Determine the percentage loss made by the enthusiast. (2 marks) (d) A gallery charges a 35% commission on the price of all artworks that it sells. If it sells a small sculpture for $560 what commission will it charge? (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-3 Question 2 (8 marks) (a) An item is priced at $135 excluding GST. Determine the price of the item once 10% GST has been included. (2 marks) (b) A homeowner is offered a 2% discount for early payment of their $1700 annual council rates bill. How much would they pay if they took up the offer? (2 marks) (c) A watch enthusiast paid $500 for a timepiece but later sold it for just $440. Determine the percentage loss made by the enthusiast. (2 marks) (d) A gallery charges a 35% commission on the price of all artworks that it sells. If it sells a small sculpture for $560 what commission will it charge? (2 marks) Solution 10% →$56, 5% →$28, 20% →$112 Commission is 56 + 28 + 112 = $196. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates any correct method to obtain commission ✓ correct commission Solution 500 −440 = 60 60 500 = 6 50 = 12 100 = 12% loss Specific behaviours ✓ correctly indicates loss ✓ correct percentage loss, must state ‘loss’ or ‘-12%’ Solution 1% →$17, 2% →$34 1700 −34 = $1666 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly indicates 2% of bill ✓ correct amount Solution 135 + 13.50 = $148.50 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly indicates 10% of price",
