    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-233-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (7 marks) Information about two companies listed on a stock exchange is shown in the table below. Company Code Share price ($) Annual earnings per share (cents) Last dividend paid per share (cents) CBQ 1.44 3 5 QLM 2.00 5 7 (a) Determine the last dividend payment to an investor who owned 4200 shares in CBQ. (2 marks) (b) The last dividend paid per share by QLM was 7 cents when its share price was $2.00. Determine the equivalent percentage dividend. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for each company. (2 marks) (d) State, with justification, in which of the two companies an investor would pay the least for each dollar of the company’s earnings. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-233-3 Question 5 (7 marks) Information about two companies listed on a stock exchange is shown in the table below. Company Code Share price ($) Annual earnings per share (cents) Last dividend paid per share (cents) CBQ 1.44 3 5 QLM 2.00 5 7 (a) Determine the last dividend payment to an investor who owned 4200 shares in CBQ. (2 marks) (b) The last dividend paid per share by QLM was 7 cents when its share price was $2.00. Determine the equivalent percentage dividend. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the price-to-earnings ratio for each company. (2 marks) (d) State, with justification, in which of the two companies an investor would pay the least for each dollar of the company’s earnings. (1 mark) Solution QLM – it has the lowest P/E ratio. Specific behaviours ✓ correct company, with justification that references P/E ratio Solution CBQ: 144 3 = 48, QLM: 200 5 = 40 or CBQ: 1.44 0.03 = 48, QLM: 2 0.05 = 40 Specific behaviours ✓ correct ratio for CBQ ✓ correct ratio for QLM Solution 7 200 = 3.5 100 ∴3.5% Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct expression for percentage ✓ correct percentage Solution 4200 × 5 ÷ 100 = 42 × 5 = $210 or 4200 × ",
