    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (8 marks) (a) A floor plan of a home is drawn where 4 cm on the plan represents 2.4 m in the actual home. The scale factor for this plan is 1: 𝑛, where 𝑛 is a whole number. Determine the value of 𝑛. (2 marks) (b) The side lengths of triangle 𝐴 are 5 cm, 7 cm and 8 cm. The side lengths of triangle 𝐵 are 20 cm, 28 cm and 36 cm. Are these triangles similar figures? Justify your answer. (3 marks) (c) The shaded region on the grid to the right is a scale drawing of a concrete slab, where each small square has a side length of 4 mm. If the area of the actual concrete slab is 360 square metres, determine the scale factor of the drawing. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-3 Question 6 (8 marks) (a) A floor plan of a home is drawn where 4 cm on the plan represents 2.4 m in the actual home. The scale factor for this plan is 1: 𝑛, where 𝑛 is a whole number. Determine the value of 𝑛. (2 marks) (b) The side lengths of triangle 𝐴 are 5 cm, 7 cm and 8 cm. The side lengths of triangle 𝐵 are 20 cm, 28 cm and 36 cm. Are these triangles similar figures? Justify your answer. (3 marks) (c) The shaded region on the grid to the right is a scale drawing of a concrete slab, where each small square has a side length of 4 mm. If the area of the actual concrete slab is 360 square metres, determine the scale factor of the drawing. (3 marks) Solution Ratio of shortest sides: 20 ÷ 5 = 4. Ratio of middle sides: 28 ÷ 7 = 4. Ratio of longest sides: 36 ÷ 8 = 4.5. Hence the triangles are not similar as the ratios of corresponding sides are not the same for all three pairs of sides. Specific behaviours ✓ correctly calculates two ratios of side lengths that show not equal ✓ states triangles are not similar ✓ correctly justifies why triangles are not similar Solution 2.4 m is 240 cm. Hence ratio is 4: 240 which simplif",
