    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN085-233-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (7 marks) A large three-dimensional sculpture is to be suspended outside a sports arena to advertise a skateboarding competition. The sculpture comprises three two-metre cubes and two triangular prisms that will be glued together to form the composite figure as shown in the diagram (not to scale). All dimensions are in metres and the triangular cross-section of each prism has sides of 5.2 m, 4.8 m and 2 m. (a) Show that the volume of the smaller triangular prism is 9.6 cubic metres. (1 mark) (b) Determine the volume of the composite figure. (2 marks) (c) The sculpture needs to be coated with a waterproof sealant spray. Determine the total surface area of the composite figure that needs to be covered. Show clear evidence of the method you use. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN085-233-3 Question 7 (7 marks) A large three-dimensional sculpture is to be suspended outside a sports arena to advertise a skateboarding competition. The sculpture comprises three two-metre cubes and two triangular prisms that will be glued together to form the composite figure as shown in the diagram (not to scale). All dimensions are in metres and the triangular cross-section of each prism has sides of 5.2 m, 4.8 m and 2 m. (a) Show that the volume of the smaller triangular prism is 9.6 cubic metres. (1 mark) (b) Determine the volume of the composite figure. (2 marks) (c) The sculpture needs to be coated with a waterproof sealant spray. Determine the total surface area of the composite figure that needs to be covered. Show clear evidence of the method you use. (4 marks) Solution There are 11 exposed faces of the cubes: 𝐴1 = 11 × 2 × 2 = 44 There are 4 triangular faces: 𝐴2 = 4 × 4.8 = 19.2 There are 4 rectangular faces of the triangular prisms: 𝐴3 = 2 × 5.2 + 4 × 5.2 + 2 × 4.8 + 4 × 4.8 = 60 Hence the total surface area is: TSA = 44 + 19.2 + 60 = 123.2 m2 Specific behaviours ✓ clearly shows method employed ✓ obtains or ind",
