    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (8 marks) Jian wants to transfer 1100 Australian dollars to his sister who lives in Singapore and will carry out the transaction using his own bank (ANZ), PayPal or Wise. The table below shows the exchange rate (how many Singapore dollars that one Australian dollar will buy) and the transfer fee charged by each company in Australian dollars. Jian will pay the transfer fee upfront to ensure that his sister receives the full amount of the transfer in Singapore dollars. Own bank (ANZ) PayPal Wise Exchange rate 0.8464 0.8366 0.8750 Transfer fee $9.00 5% of transfer* $0.83 + 0.55% of transfer * A minimum transfer fee of $0.99 and maximum transfer fee of $5.99 applies for PayPal. (a) Which company will charge Jian the least transfer fee? Justify your answer. (3 marks) (b) Determine the amount, in Singapore dollars, his sister would receive if Jian used the most favourable exchange rate offered. (2 marks) (c) Jian’s sister has told him that 1100 Australian dollars is not enough because she needs 1400 Singapore dollars. Determine the total funds, in Australian dolla",
