    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (9 marks) (a) A supermarket customer assistant was employed at a base rate of $22.40 per hour. Calculate his total earnings in a week when he worked for 36 hours at his base rate and for 5 hours 30 minutes of over-time, for which he was paid time-and-a-half. (3 marks) (b) Another person who ran an instore promotion for air fryers in the supermarket was paid a weekly retainer of $245 plus 14.5% commission on the total value of the air fryers that the supermarket sold. Calculate the earnings for this person in a week when 26 small and 16 large air fryers were sold for $119 and $229 respectively. (3 marks) (c) The supermarket sells the same yoghurt in two different sized cartons: 125 g for $2.40 and 420 g for $8.19. Use the unit cost method to compare the prices of each size carton and hence state which size represents the best value. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-4 Question 9 (9 marks) (a) A supermarket customer assistant was employed at a base rate of $22.40 per hour. Calculate his total earnings in a week when he worked for 36 hours at his base rate and for 5 hours 30 minutes of over-time, for which he was paid time-and-a-half. (3 marks) (b) Another person who ran an instore promotion for air fryers in the supermarket was paid a weekly retainer of $245 plus 14.5% commission on the total value of the air fryers that the supermarket sold. Calculate the earnings for this person in a week when 26 small and 16 large air fryers were sold for $119 and $229 respectively. (3 marks) (c) The supermarket sells the same yoghurt in two different sized cartons: 125 g for $2.40 and 420 g for $8.19. Use the unit cost method to compare the prices of each size carton and hence state which size represents the best value. (3 marks) Solution Overtime hours: 5.5 × 1.5 = 8.25 Total hours: 36 + 8.25 = 44.25 Total earnings: 44.25 × 22.40 = $991.20. Specific behaviours ✓ adjusts overtime hours ✓ correct expression for base or overtime earnings using pay rate ✓ correct total earnings Solution Value of ",
