    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (10 marks) Giovanna made some gelato and left it to cool in a cylindrical glass container with an internal diameter of 17 cm. (a) The container is filled with gelato to a uniform depth of 14 cm. Determine the volume of gelato that Giovanna has made, to the nearest cm3. (3 mark) Previously, Giovanna had made 2650 cubic centimetres of gelato and used it to fill right circular waffle cones with internal radius 2.5 cm and height 11 cm as treats for his friends. (b) Determine the volume of gelato required to fill one of these cones level with its circular top. (2 marks) (c) How many complete cones could Giovanna fill? (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-4 Question 10 (10 marks) Giovanna made some gelato and left it to cool in a cylindrical glass container with an internal diameter of 17 cm. (a) The container is filled with gelato to a uniform depth of 14 cm. Determine the volume of gelato that Giovanna has made, to the nearest cm3. (3 mark) Previously, Giovanna had made 2650 cubic centimetres of gelato and used it to fill right circular waffle cones with internal radius 2.5 cm and height 11 cm as treats for his friends. (b) Determine the volume of gelato required to fill one of these cones level with its circular top. (2 marks) (c) How many complete cones could Giovanna fill? (1 mark) Solution 𝑉= 1 3 𝜋(2.5)2 × 11 = 71.9948 cm3 = 72.0 cm3 Volume of gelato to fill one cone is 72 cm3. Specific behaviours ✓ correctly substitutes into volume formula ✓ correct volume – accept either answer Solution Number of cones is 2650 ÷ 72 = 36.806. Giovanna could fill 36 cones completely. Specific behaviours ✓ correct number of cones Solution 𝑉= 𝜋× 8.52 × 14 = 3178 cm3 Volume of gelato is 3178 cm3. Specific behaviours ✓ Uses radius not diameter ✓ correctly substitutes into formula ✓ c",
