    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (12 marks) Tamsin has prepared a weekly budget to check that she can afford to run a second-hand petrol fuelled car using the income from her casual job and government allowance. Budget item Weekly amount ($) Loan repayment 64 Registration and compulsory insurance 29 Comprehensive insurance 𝑥 Petrol 45 Servicing 11 Roadside emergency assistance 3 (a) Name a budget item from the table above that is an example of (i) a fixed expense. (1 mark) (ii) a discretionary expense. (1 mark) (b) Assuming there are exactly 52 weeks in a year, determine (i) the annual amount that Tamsin has budgeted for petrol. (1 mark) (ii) the value of 𝑥 in the table (the weekly amount Tamsin has budgeted for comprehensive insurance) if her insurance policy costs $78 per month. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-4 Question 11 (12 marks) Tamsin has prepared a weekly budget to check that she can afford to run a second-hand petrol fuelled car using the income from her casual job and government allowance. Budget item Weekly amount ($) Loan repayment 64 Registration and compulsory insurance 29 Comprehensive insurance 𝑥 Petrol 45 Servicing 11 Roadside emergency assistance 3 (a) Name a budget item from the table above that is an example of (i) a fixed expense. (1 mark) (ii) a discretionary expense. (1 mark) (b) Assuming there are exactly 52 weeks in a year, determine (i) the annual amount that Tamsin has budgeted for petrol. (1 mark) (ii) the value of 𝑥 in the table (the weekly amount Tamsin has budgeted for comprehensive insurance) if her insurance policy costs $78 per month. (2 marks) Solution Annual amount: 78 × 12 = $936. Weekly amount: 𝑥= 936 ÷ 52 = $18. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct annual amount ✓ correct weekly amount Solution Loan repayment or Registration and compulsory insurance. Specific behaviours ✓ names a correct fixed expense Solution Comprehensive insurance or Petrol or Servicing or Roadside emergency assi",
