    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Tamsin is eligible for a maximum fortnightly Youth Allowance payment of $425, but the actual amount she receives is reduced because she has a casual job from which she earns $360 per week. Youth Allowance payments reduce according to the following rules: Amount your payment reduces by if you earn between $480 and $575 per fortnight Amount your payment reduces by if you earn more than $575 per fortnight 50 cents for each dollar over $480 $47.50 plus 60 cents for each dollar over $575 (c) Determine the Youth Allowance payment made to Tamsin each fortnight. (3 marks) Tamsin cannot afford to spend more than 35% of her total earnings and allowance to run a car. (d) Will she have to find a way to reduce her budget? Justify your answer. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-4 Tamsin is eligible for a maximum fortnightly Youth Allowance payment of $425, but the actual amount she receives is reduced because she has a casual job from which she earns $360 per week. Youth Allowance payments reduce according to the following rules: Amount your payment reduces by if you earn between $480 and $575 per fortnight Amount your payment reduces by if you earn more than $575 per fortnight 50 cents for each dollar over $480 $47.50 plus 60 cents for each dollar over $575 (c) Determine the Youth Allowance payment made to Tamsin each fortnight. (3 marks) Tamsin cannot afford to spend more than 35% of her total earnings and allowance to run a car. (d) Will she have to find a way to reduce her budget? Justify your answer. (4 marks) Solution Fortnightly earnings: 2 × 360 = $720. Payment reduction: 47.50 + 0.60 × (720 −575) = 47.50 + 0.60 × 145 = 47.50 + 87 = $134.50 Fortnightly payment will be 425 −134.50 = $290.50 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates fortnightly earnings ✓ calculates payment reduction ✓ correct fortnightly payment Solution Total weekly income: 360 + 290.50 ÷ 2 = 360 + 145.25 = $505.25 Tasmin cann",
