    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (10 marks) A manufacturer sells a range of rectangular timber-framed windows with a clipped corner. Four of the edge lengths of a piece of glass used to glaze one of these windows are shown in the diagram below, where the dashed line shows the triangular corner that is removed. The lengths are in centimetres and the diagram is not drawn to scale. (a) Determine the area of glass removed when the triangular corner is clipped. (3 marks) (b) Determine the area of glass that remains once the corner has been clipped. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-4 Question 12 (10 marks) A manufacturer sells a range of rectangular timber-framed windows with a clipped corner. Four of the edge lengths of a piece of glass used to glaze one of these windows are shown in the diagram below, where the dashed line shows the triangular corner that is removed. The lengths are in centimetres and the diagram is not drawn to scale. (a) Determine the area of glass removed when the triangular corner is clipped. (3 marks) (b) Determine the area of glass that remains once the corner has been clipped. (2 marks) Solution Base of triangle is 315 −187 = 128. Height of triangle is 205 −77 = 128. Area of triangle: 𝐴= 1 2 × 128 × 128 = 8192 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly calculates one dimension of triangle – can be given in the formula working ✓ shows correct use of area formula ✓ correct area – accept 0.82 𝑚2 Solution Area of rectangle: 𝐴𝑅= 205 × 315 = 64 575 Area of glass remaining: 𝐴= 64 575 −8192 = 56 383 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates area of rectangle – accept 6.46 𝑚2 ✓ calculates remaining area– accept 5.64 𝑚2 Allow F/T from (a) if working shown.",
