    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 13 (11 marks) A financial advisor rents a small office to work in and meet clients. (a) A year ago, the annual rent payable for the office was set at $460 per square metre. This amount is subject to an annual increase of 2.5% plus the percentage increase in the consumer price index over the previous year. The consumer price index rose from 124.2 to 132.4 over the past year. (i) Show that the percentage increase in the consumer price index was 6.60%. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the new annual rent payable for the office given that it has a floor area of 62.5 square metres. (3 marks) (b) A client of the financial advisor wanted a 60 day loan of $1095. If the loan attracted simple interest at 12.5% per annum, determine the total amount that the client would have to repay at the end of the loan period. (3 marks)",
