    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 14 (10 marks) A student has designed three metal scoops with identical wooden handles that can all be used by a baker to scoop exactly 150 grams of flour out of a large bin of the ingredient. They are shown in the diagram below, not drawn to scale. One scoop is cylindrical with a radius of 4.5 cm and a height of 3 cm, one is hemispherical with a radius of 4.5 cm, and the other is conical with a radius of 4.5 cm and a perpendicular height of 9 cm. (a) Determine the area of metal required to make the cylindrical scoop. (2 marks) (b) Determine the area of metal used to make the hemispherical scoop. (2 marks) (c) Determine the slant height of the conical scoop and hence state the area of metal required to make the conical scoop. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-4 Question 14 (10 marks) A student has designed three metal scoops with identical wooden handles that can all be used by a baker to scoop exactly 150 grams of flour out of a large bin of the ingredient. They are shown in the diagram below, not drawn to scale. One scoop is cylindrical with a radius of 4.5 cm and a height of 3 cm, one is hemispherical with a radius of 4.5 cm, and the other is conical with a radius of 4.5 cm and a perpendicular height of 9 cm. (a) Determine the area of metal required to make the cylindrical scoop. (2 marks) (b) Determine the area of metal used to make the hemispherical scoop. (2 marks) (c) Determine the slant height of the conical scoop and hence state the area of metal required to make the conical scoop. (3 marks) Solution Slant height: ℎ= √4.52 + 92 = 10.06 cm Area of metal for conical scoop: 𝐴= 𝜋(4.5)(10.06) = 142.22 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct slant height – accept 10.1 cm and 10 cm ✓ indicates correct method to calculate surface area – no lid ✓ correct area of metal If used 10.1 cm, accept A = 142.29 cm2 If used 10 cm, accept A = 141.37 cm2 Solution Area of metal for hemisphe",
