    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (d) By first calculating the volume of any one of the scoops, determine the volume of one gram of flour. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-233-4 (d) By first calculating the volume of any one of the scoops, determine the volume of one gram of flour. (3 marks) Solution 𝑉𝐶𝑌𝐿= 𝜋(4.5)2(3) = 190.85 cm3 𝑉𝐻𝑆= 4𝜋(4.5)3 3 × 1 2 = 190.85 cm3 𝑉𝐶𝑂𝑁𝐸= 𝜋(4.5)2(9) 3 = 190.85 cm3 Hence volume of one gram of flour is 190.85 ÷ 150 = 1.27 cm3. Specific behaviours ✓ shows correct use of formula for chosen scoop ✓ obtains correct volume ✓ correct volume of one gram",
