    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (10 marks) Danielle’s bedroom is a rectangular room that measures 4.65 m by 6.35 m and she has created a scale drawing of it using a scale of 1: 25. (a) Would her drawing fit on a 20 cm by 25 cm sheet of paper? Justify your answer. (3 marks) (b) On the floor of her bedroom she has a circular rug with a radius of 1.05 m. It is split into different coloured sectors, the green one having a central angle of 55°. Determine (i) the area of the green sector of the actual rug. (2 marks) (ii) the area, in square centimetres, of the green sector on her scale drawing of the rug. (2 marks) (c) A cube of foam in her bedroom that her friends sit on needs a new cover. On her scale drawing, the length of one side of the cube is 22 mm. Allowing an extra 20% for seams and wastage, how many square centimetres of fabric should be bought to make a new cover for the cube? (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-233-4 Question 16 (10 marks) Danielle’s bedroom is a rectangular room that measures 4.65 m by 6.35 m and she has created a scale drawing of it using a scale of 1: 25. (a) Would her drawing fit on a 20 cm by 25 cm sheet of paper? Justify your answer. (3 marks) (b) On the floor of her bedroom she has a circular rug with a radius of 1.05 m. It is split into different coloured sectors, the green one having a central angle of 55°. Determine (i) the area of the green sector of the actual rug. (2 marks) (ii) the area, in square centimetres, of the green sector on her scale drawing of the rug. (2 marks) (c) A cube of foam in her bedroom that her friends sit on needs a new cover. On her scale drawing, the length of one side of the cube is 22 mm. Allowing an extra 20% for seams and wastage, how many square centimetres of fabric should be bought to make a new cover for the cube? (3 marks) Solution Actual side length of cube is 2.2 × 25 = 55 cm. Total surface area of cube is 6 × 552 = 18 150 cm2. Fabric required is 20% more: 18 150 × 1.20 = 21 780 cm2. Specific behaviours ✓ correct side length of cube ✓ correct TSA for cube ✓ correc",
