    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 19 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-233-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (8 marks) A borrower must make 𝑛 monthly repayments of 𝐴 dollars to repay a loan of 𝐿 dollars when the interest rate on their loan is 𝑅% per annum compounded monthly. To calculate the monthly repayment 𝐴, the following formulas are used: 𝐴= 𝐿𝑟 𝑏 , where 𝑟= 𝑅 1200 and 𝑏= 1 −(1 + 𝑟)−𝑛. (a) Lars has negotiated a loan of $52 000 to buy a new EV. The interest rate on his loan is 7.8% per annum compounded monthly and he will make 60 monthly repayments. (i) Calculate the value of 𝑟 for this loan. (1 mark) (ii) Calculate the value of 𝑏, rounding your answer to 6 decimal places. (2 marks) (iii) Show that the monthly repayment Lars must make is $1049.40. (1 mark) (b) Leigh has budgeted monthly repayments of no more than $150 to buy an electric scooter priced at $3250. She has been offered a loan for the full purchase price with 24 monthly repayments at an interest rate of 8.4% per annum compounded monthly. If Leigh goes ahead with the loan, will the repayments satisfy her budget? Justify your answer. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 19 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-233-4 Question 17 (8 marks) A borrower must make 𝑛 monthly repayments of 𝐴 dollars to repay a loan of 𝐿 dollars when the interest rate on their loan is 𝑅% per annum compounded monthly. To calculate the monthly repayment 𝐴, the following formulas are used: 𝐴= 𝐿𝑟 𝑏 , where 𝑟= 𝑅 1200 and 𝑏= 1 −(1 + 𝑟)−𝑛. (a) Lars has negotiated a loan of $52 000 to buy a new EV. The interest rate on his loan is 7.8% per annum compounded monthly and he will make 60 monthly repayments. (i) Calculate the value of 𝑟 for this loan. (1 mark) (ii) Calculate the value of 𝑏, rounding your answer to 6 decimal places. (2 marks) (iii) Show that the monthly repayment Lars must make is $1049.40. (1 mark) (b) Leigh has budgeted monthly repayments of no more than $150 to buy an electric scooter priced at $3250. She has been offered a loan for the full purchase price with 24 monthly repayments at an interest rate of 8.4% per annum compounded monthly. If Leigh goes ahead with the loan, will the repayments satisfy her budget? Justify your answer. (4 marks) Solution 𝑟= 8.4 ÷ 1200 = 0.007 𝑏= 1 −(1 + 0.007)−24 = 0.154151 𝐴= 3250 × 0.007 ÷ 0.154151 = 147.58 Th",
