    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-3 Question 3 (8 marks) In matrix 𝑿= [5 7 8 6 7 6], element 𝑥𝑖,𝑗 is the number of single people (𝑖= 1) or couples (𝑖= 2) who attended a dance class on night 𝑗. (a) Show that a total of 17 people attended the dance class on night 1. (1 mark) (b) Determine [1 2] × 𝑿 and explain what information is contained in your answer. (2 marks) The fee to attend a dance class for one night was $20 for a single and $30 for a couple. (c) Represent the fees in row matrix 𝒀 so that the matrix product 𝒀× 𝑿 will have a meaningful result. (1 mark) (d) Determine 𝒀× 𝑿× [ 1 1 1 ]. (3 marks) (e) Explain what information is contained in the matrix calculated in part (d). (1 mark) Solution 𝒀× 𝑿× [ 1 1 1 ] = [20 30] × [5 7 8 6 7 6] × [ 1 1 1 ] = [20 30] × [20 19] = [970] or 𝒀× 𝑿× [ 1 1 1 ] = [20 30] × [5 7 8 6 7 6] × [ 1 1 1 ] = [280 350 340] × [ 1 1 1 ] = [970] Specific behaviours ✓ at least one correct element seen in attempt to multiply a pair of matrices ✓ one correct matrix product seen ✓ correct result Solution [1 2] × [5 7 8 6 7 6] = [17 21 20] The matrix shows the number of people who attended the dance class on each night. Specific behaviou",
