    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-253-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 4 (7 marks) (a) A vertical flagpole, of height 3.6 metres, stands near a vertical lighting tower on a level sports ground. At the instant the length of the shadow of the flagpole is 2.5 metres, the length of shadow of the lighting tower is 7.5 metres. By first sketching the two similar triangles involved in this situation, determine the height of the lighting tower. (3 marks) (b) A measurement of 60 millimetres on a construction plan represents a length of 12 metres in a building. Determine the scale factor of the plan in the form 1: 𝑛. (2 marks) (c) The straight-line distance between points 𝑃 and 𝑄 on a map drawn to a scale of 1: 25 000 is 10 centimetres. Determine the actual straight-line distance between the points in kilometres. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-253-3 Question 4 (7 marks) (a) A vertical flagpole, of height 3.6 metres, stands near a vertical lighting tower on a level sports ground. At the instant the length of the shadow of the flagpole is 2.5 metres, the length of shadow of the lighting tower is 7.5 metres. By first sketching the two similar triangles involved in this situation, determine the height of the lighting tower. (3 marks) (b) A measurement of 60 millimetres on a construction plan represents a length of 12 metres in a building. Determine the scale factor of the plan in the form 1: 𝑛. (2 marks) (c) The straight-line distance between points 𝑃 and 𝑄 on a map drawn to a scale of 1: 25 000 is 10 centimetres. Determine the actual straight-line distance between the points in kilometres. (2 marks) Solution Actual distance is 10 × 25 000 = 250 000 cm. 250 000 cm is 2500 metres which is 2.5 kilometres. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct distance in centimetres ✓ correct distance in kilometres Solution 60 mm: 12 m = 60: 12 000 = 6: 1200 = 1: 200 Specific behaviours ✓ writes a correct ratio after eliminating units ✓ correct scale factor Solution Scale factor of si",
