    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (7 marks) Takeshi lives in a boarding house that charges him $420 each week for food and lodging. He has allocated all his weekly income of $840 to one of five budget categories shown at right. He always allocates 15% of his weekly income to savings. (a) The boarding house fines residents 5% of their weekly charge for late payment. Determine how much Takeshi would be fined for late payment. (1 mark) (b) Determine his budget allocation for savings (y). (1 mark) (c) Takeshi estimates that 40% of his car budget is spent on fuel. Assuming a year of exactly 52 weeks, determine his annual fuel costs. (3 marks) (d) Takeshi plans to increase the budget allocation for Technology by $12 and for Other by the same amount. When he does so, which of these two categories will have the largest percentage increase? Justify your answer. (2 marks) $x $y",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-3 Question 5 (7 marks) Takeshi lives in a boarding house that charges him $420 each week for food and lodging. He has allocated all his weekly income of $840 to one of five budget categories shown at right. He always allocates 15% of his weekly income to savings. (a) The boarding house fines residents 5% of their weekly charge for late payment. Determine how much Takeshi would be fined for late payment. (1 mark) (b) Determine his budget allocation for savings. (1 mark) (d) Takeshi plans to increase the budget allocation for Technology by $12 and for Other by the same amount. When he does so, which of these two categories will have the largest percentage increase? Justify your answer. (2 marks) Takeshi estimates that 40% of his car budget is spent on fuel. (c) Assuming a year of exactly 52 weeks, determine his annual fuel costs. (3 marks) Solution $420 + $55 + $126 + $99 = $700 Car budget is $840 −$700 = $140. 40% of $140 is $56 Annual cost is 52 × $56 = $2912 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates amount budgeted for car ✓ calculates 40% of budgeted amount ✓ correct annual fuel cost (F/T allowed) Solution $840 × 10% = $84, $84",
