    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-253-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (8 marks) The floor plan of a room, not drawn to scale, is shown. All corners are right-angled and all measurements are in centimetres. The floor of the room is to be tiled with rectangular tiles that measure 0.3 metres by 0.6 metres. The tiles are sold in boxes of 10 at a cost of $90 per box. Only full boxes can be bought. (a) How long is the longest side of the room, in metres? (1 mark) (b) Determine how much it will cost to buy tiles for the room. (5 marks) Once the floor has been tiled, a thin wooden strip that costs $5 per metre is to be glued around the edge of the tiled area. (c) Determine the cost of wooden strip to edge the tiles. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN085-253-3 Question 6 (8 marks) The floor plan of a room, not drawn to scale, is shown. All corners are right-angled and all measurements are in centimetres. The floor of the room is to be tiled with rectangular tiles that measure 0.3 metres by 0.6 metres. The tiles are sold in boxes of 10 at a cost of $90 per box. Only full boxes can be bought. (a) How long is the longest side of the room, in metres? (1 mark) (b) Determine how much it will cost to buy tiles for the room. (5 marks) Once the floor has been tiled, a thin wooden strip that costs $5 per metre is to be glued around the edge of the tiled area. (c) Determine the cost of wooden strip to edge the tiles. (2 marks) Solution Perimeter is 6 + 6 + 3.6 + 3.6 + 0.6 + 0.6 = 20.4 metres. Cost is 20.4 × $5 = $102. Specific behaviours ✓ correct length of wooden strip required ✓ correct cost Solution LH part of room (360 × 120) needs 6 × 4 = 24 tiles. Central part of room (300 × 360) needs 5 × 12 = 60 tiles. Total number of tiles will be 24 + 60 + 24 = 108. Number of boxes needed is 108 ÷ 10 = 10 r8, so 11 full boxes. Cost of tiles is 11 × $90 = $990. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates ",
