    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-253-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (8 marks) Fruit pickers at a farm are paid $10 per carton of pears plus a wage of $20 per hour, with both rates increasing by 50% on weekends. (a) Determine how much Amana will earn for picking 12 cartons of pears during an 8 hour shift on a Wednesday. (2 marks) (b) Determine how much Babbe will earn for picking 8 cartons of pears during a 6 hour shift on a Saturday. (2 marks) (c) Carma picked 8 cartons of pears during a 5 hour shift on Sunday and 11 cartons during a second shift on Monday. Given that she earned $520 for the two days' work, determine how long she worked for on Monday. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-253-3 Question 7 (8 marks) Fruit pickers at a farm are paid $10 per carton of pears plus a wage of $20 per hour, with both rates increasing by 50% on weekends. (a) Determine how much Amana will earn for picking 12 cartons of pears during an 8 hour shift on a Wednesday. (2 marks) (b) Determine how much Babbe will earn for picking 8 cartons of pears during a 6 hour shift on a Saturday. (2 marks) (c) Carma picked 8 cartons of pears during a 5 hour shift on Sunday and 11 cartons during a second shift on Monday. Given that she earned $520 for the two days' work, determine how long she worked for on Monday. (4 marks) Solution Sunday earnings: $10 × 8 × 1.5 + $20 × 5 × 1.5 = $120 + $150 = $270 Monday cartons: $10 × 11 = $110 Monday wages: $520 −$270 −$110 = $140 Monday hours: $140 ÷ $20 = 7 hours Specific behaviours ✓ calculates Sunday earnings ✓ calculates earnings from cartons on Monday ✓ calculates wages for Monday ✓ correct Monday hours worked (F/T allowed) Solution Cartons: $10 × 1.5 × 8 = $120 Wage: $20 × 1.5 × 6 = $180 Total: $120 + $180 = $300 Specific behaviours ✓ correct earnings from cartons or wages ✓ correct earning",
