    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (10 marks) A closed rectangular cardboard box has a height of 21 centimetres and base dimensions of 56 by 33 centimetres as shown. (a) Determine the volume of the box. (1 mark) (b) Determine the total surface area of the six faces of the box. (3 marks) (c) The 12 edges of the box are to be reinforced with rubber tape. Determine the total length of edges that need reinforcing, giving your answer in metres. (2 marks) (d) Determine the length of the longest thin wooden rod that can be placed in the box if (i) the entire length of the rod must be in contact with the base of the box. (2 marks) (ii) the rod can lay in any position. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-4 Question 8 (10 marks) A closed rectangular cardboard box has a height of 21 centimetres and base dimensions of 56 by 33 centimetres as shown. (a) Determine the volume of the box. (1 mark) (b) Determine the total surface area of the six faces of the box. (3 marks) (c) The 12 edges of the box are to be reinforced with rubber tape. Determine the total length of edges that need reinforcing, giving your answer in metres. (2 marks) (d) Determine the length of the longest thin wooden rod that can be placed in the box if (i) the entire length of the rod must be in contact with the base of the box. (2 marks) (ii) the rod can lay in any position. (2 marks) Solution 𝐿= 4 × (56 + 33 + 21) = 4 × 110 = 440 cm Length of edges is 4.4 metres. Specific behaviours ✓ correct sum of edges ✓ correct length in metres Solution 𝐴= 2 × (56 × 33 + 56 × 21 + 33 × 21) = 2 × (1848 + 1176 + 693) = 2 × 3717 = 7434 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates one correct rectangular area ✓ indicates all correct rectangular areas ✓ correct total surface area Solution 𝑉= 56 × 33 × 21 = 38 808 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ correct volume Solution Rod lies diagonal",
