    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (7 marks) The formula below calculates the monthly repayment 𝑃, in dollars, when a $2500 loan is repaid over a period of 𝑛 years and the interest rate on the loan is 𝑟 percent per annum: 𝑃= 2500𝑚𝑖 𝑚−1 where 𝑚= (1 + 𝑖)12𝑛 and 𝑖= 𝑟 1200 . The formula for 𝑃 is used to generate the values in the shaded cells from C3 onwards in the spreadsheet shown below. (a) What is the monthly repayment when the loan is repaid over 2 years and the interest rate is 4% per annum. (1 mark) (b) Determine the values of 𝑖 and 𝑚 used to calculate the value of 𝑃 shown in cell G3 of the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) Determine the value that would appear in cell H9 of the spreadsheet if the repayment periods in row 2 and interest rates in column B continue to increase as shown. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-4 Question 9 (7 marks) The formula below calculates the monthly repayment 𝑃, in dollars, when a $2500 loan is repaid over a period of 𝑛 years and the interest rate on the loan is 𝑟 percent per annum: 𝑃= 2500𝑚𝑖 𝑚−1 where 𝑚= (1 + 𝑖)12𝑛 and 𝑖= 𝑟 1200 . The formula for 𝑃 is used to generate the values in the shaded cells from C3 onwards in the spreadsheet shown below. (a) What is the monthly repayment when the loan is repaid over 2 years and the interest rate is 4% per annum. (1 mark) (b) Determine the values of 𝑖 and 𝑚 used to calculate the value of 𝑃 shown in cell G3 of the spreadsheet. (2 marks) (c) Determine the value that would appear in cell H9 of the spreadsheet if the repayment periods in row 2 and interest rates in column B continue to increase as shown. (4 marks) Solution In cell H9, 𝑟= 9 and 𝑛= 6. 𝑖= 9 ÷ 1200 = 0.0075 𝑚= (1 + 0.0075)12×6 = 1.71255 𝑃= 2500 × 1.71255 × 0.0075 1.71255 −1 = 45.06 Specific behaviours ✓ correct values for 𝑟 and 𝑛 ✓ calculates value of 𝑖 ✓ calculates value of 𝑚 ✓ correct value Solution 𝑟= 3, 𝑖= 3 1200 = 0.0025 𝑛= 5, 𝑚= (1 + 0.0025)12×5 = 1.1616 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value of 𝑖",
