    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (d) Explain why the area of the curved surface of the prism is 1650 square centimetres. (2 marks) (e) Determine the total surface area of the concrete prism. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-4 (d) Explain why the area of the curved surface of the prism is 1650 square centimetres. (2 marks) (e) Determine the total surface area of the concrete prism. (3 marks) Solution If the curved surface was flattened it would be a rectangle of length equal to the height of the prism, 25 cm, and width equal to the length of arc of the sector, 66 cm. Hence 𝐴= 25 × 66 = 1650 cm2. Specific behaviours ✓ explains why area is rectangular (labelled graph is allowed) ✓ explains dimensions of rectangle Solution Area of one rectangular face: 𝐴= 25 × 17.2 = 430 Total surface area: 𝐴= 2 × 430 + 2 × 568 + 1650 = 860 + 1136 + 1650 = 3646 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates area of rectangular face ✓ shows calculation for total surface area using all five surfaces ✓ correct total surface area (F/T)",
