    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (12 marks) Maureen has a special bank account that enables her to hold Australian dollars and several foreign currencies at the same time. She can exchange currencies at any time she wishes, and her account currently holds $1150, €386 and ฿7540. The buy and sell rates for one Australian dollar that her bank offers on these currencies are shown in the table below. The bank charges no conversion or other fees to account holders. Currency (region, symbol) Buy rate Sell rate Euro (European Union, €) 0.6044 0.5812 Baht (Thailand, ฿) 21.96 21.09 (a) Explain why the buy rate is used when she converts Thai baht into Australian dollars. (1 mark) (b) Determine the balance of her account if she converted all her foreign currencies into Australian dollars. (2 marks) Maureen wants to exchange some of her Australian dollars into euro so that her holding of this currency increases from €386 to €750. (c) Determine how many Australian dollars would remain in her account after the exchange is complete. (3 marks)",
