    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Maureen is a shareholder in the listed companies Marjoke and Nemesis that have current market prices of $11.40 and $1.73 respectively per share. She owns 1860 shares in Marjoke that has recently declared a dividend of 26 cents per share, and 13 620 shares in Nemesis that has declared a dividend yield of 1.2%. (d) Determine the total dividend Maureen will receive. (3 marks) (e) Calculate the percentage dividend yield for shares in Marjoke. (2 marks) (f) Determine the price-to-earnings ratio for Nemesis, given that it has annual earnings per share of 6.2 cents. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-4 Maureen is a shareholder in the listed companies Marjoke and Nemesis that have current market prices of $11.40 and $1.73 respectively per share. She owns 1860 shares in Marjoke that has recently declared a dividend of 26 cents per share, and 13 620 shares in Nemesis that has declared a dividend yield of 1.2%. (d) Determine the total dividend Maureen will receive. (3 marks) (e) Calculate the percentage dividend yield for shares in Marjoke. (2 marks) (f) Determine the price-to-earnings ratio for Nemesis, given that it has annual earnings per share of 6.2 cents. (1 mark) Solution Yield is 0.26 ÷ 11.40 = 0.0228 Percentage yield is 2.28% Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct method ✓ correct percentage dividend yield Solution Price-to-earnings ratio is 173 ÷ 6.2 = 27.9 Specific behaviours ✓ correct ratio Solution Marjoke: $0.26 × 1860 = $483.60 Nemesis: 0.012 × $1.73 × 13 620 = $282.75 Total dividend: $483.60 + $282.75 = $766.35 Specific behaviours ✓ one correct dividend ✓ second correct dividend ✓ correct total dividend",
