    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (10 marks) A small supermarket sells several varieties of canned fish. The spreadsheet extract below shows how much they pay their supplier for packs of cans and their selling price for individual cans. For example, they sell a 95 gram can of tuna for $1.20 having paid their supplier $27 for a pack of 36 cans which equates to a cost of 75 cents per can. All prices include GST at 10%. Supplier Supermarket Item Pack cost ($) Cans per pack Unit cost ($) Selling price ($) Tuna 95 g 27.00 36 0.75 1.20 Tuna 185 g 30.00 24 1.25 1.70 Tuna 425 g 44.10 12 2.45 3.30 Sardines 110 g 93.60 48 𝐴 2.75 Mackerel 125 g 𝐵 28 2.80 3.50 Salmon 100 g 29.70 𝐶 1.65 2.45 (a) Determine the values of 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶 in the table above. (3 marks) (b) Determine the percentage profit the store makes when they sell a can of mackerel. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the amount of GST included in the selling price of a can of sardines. (1 mark)",
