    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-4 (d) The small supermarket is about to discount their selling price of a 95 gram can of tuna by 30%. (i) Calculate the discounted price. (1 mark) (ii) Use the unit cost method to determine which size of tuna offers the best and which offers the worst value for money for someone who shops at the supermarket while the discount is in place. (3 marks) Solution Discounted price: 1.20 × 0.70 = $0.84 Specific behaviours ✓ correct price Solution Unit cost for each size Tuna 95 g: 84 ÷ 95 = 0.88 cents per gram Tuna 185 g: 170 ÷ 185 = 0.92 cents per gram Tuna 425 g: 330 ÷ 425 = 0.78 cents per gram Best value is the 425 gram size and worst is the 185 gram size. Specific behaviours ✓ one correct unit price ✓ all correct unit prices ✓ correctly states best and worst sizes (Students may use different unit prices such as cents/100 gram or dollar/kg, no penalty given the calculation is correct.)",
