    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (10 marks) Five devices, numbered from 1 to 5, can all communicate with each other on a Wi-Fi network, but not always directly. The following list shows which devices each can communicate directly with: • device 1 can communicate directly with device 4 • device 2 can communicate directly with device 5 • device 3 can communicate directly with device 4 • device 4 can communicate directly with devices 1, 3 and 5 • device 5 can communicate directly with devices 2 and 4 No device can communicate directly with itself. (a) Construct matrix 𝑨 to represent this network, with element 𝑎𝑖,𝑗 equal to 1 if device 𝑖 can communicate directly with device 𝑗, and equal to 0 if not. (2 marks) (b) What information does the sum of the elements in the second column of matrix 𝑨 represent? (1 mark) Let matrix 𝑩= 𝑨2. (c) Determine matrix 𝑩. (2 marks)",
