    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (10 marks) The vertex of the right pyramid 𝑃 shown below lies 32 centimetres directly above the centre of its square base and 40 centimetres from the midpoint of each side of its base. The square base has sides of length 48 centimetres. (a) Determine the volume of the right pyramid 𝑃. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total surface area of the right pyramid 𝑃. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-253-4 Question 16 (10 marks) The vertex of the right pyramid 𝑃 shown below lies 32 centimetres directly above the centre of its square base and 40 centimetres from the midpoint of each side of its base. The square base has sides of length 48 centimetres. (a) Determine the volume of the right pyramid 𝑃. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total surface area of the right pyramid 𝑃. (3 marks) Solution Square base: 𝐴= 482 = 2304 One triangular face: 𝐴= 1 2 × 48 × 40 = 960 Total surface area: 𝐴= 2304 + 4 × 960 = 2304 + 3740 = 6144 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ area of base ✓ area of one triangular face ✓ correct total surface area Solution 𝑉= 1 3 × 482 × 32 = 24 576 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes into correct formula ✓ correct volume",
