    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-253-4 The composite solid shown below is formed by gluing the circular face of a hemisphere of radius 9.9 centimetres to each triangular face of the right pyramid 𝑃. (c) Determine the volume of the composite solid. (2 marks) (d) Determine the total surface area of the composite solid. (3 marks) Solution Surface area of one hemisphere: 𝐴= 1 2 × 4𝜋× 9.92 = 616 Area of circle lost: 𝐴= 𝜋× 9.92 = 308 Total surface area of composite solid: 𝐴= 6144 + 4 × 616 −4 × 308 = 6144 + 2464 −1232 = 7376 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates surface area of one hemisphere ✓ calculates area of one circle ✓ correct total surface area Solution Volume of one hemisphere: 𝑉= 1 2 × 4 3 × 𝜋× 9.93 = 2032 Volume of composite solid: 𝑉= 24 576 + 4 × 2032 = 24 576 + 8128 = 32 704 cm3 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates volume of one hemisphere ✓ correct composite volume",
