    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-253-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (10 marks) (a) A solid cone made from wood has a radius of 5.7 centimetres and a perpendicular height of 17.6 centimetres. (i) Determine the slant height of the cone. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the total surface area of the cone. (2 marks) (b) The volume of a cylinder of radius 4.5 centimetres is 250 cubic centimetres. Determine the volume of a similar cylinder whose radius is 15.3 centimetres. (3 marks) (c) The surface area of a prism of height 5.5 centimetres is 45 square centimetres. Determine the height of a similar prism whose surface area is 352.8 square centimetres. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-253-4 Question 17 (10 marks) (a) A solid cone made from wood has a radius of 5.7 centimetres and a perpendicular height of 17.6 centimetres. (i) Determine the slant height of the cone. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the total surface area of the cone. (2 marks) (b) The volume of a cylinder of radius 4.5 centimetres is 250 cubic centimetres. Determine the volume of a similar cylinder whose radius is 15.3 centimetres. (3 marks) (c) The surface area of a prism of height 5.5 centimetres is 45 square centimetres. Determine the height of a similar prism whose surface area is 352.8 square centimetres. (3 marks) Solution Area scale factor is 352.8 ÷ 45 = 7.84 Length scale factor is √7.84 = 2.8 Height of similar prism is 5.5 × 2.8 = 15.4 cm. Specific behaviours ✓ calculates area scale factor ✓ obtains length scale factor ✓ correct height (F/T) Solution 𝐴= 𝜋(5.7)(18.5) + 𝜋(5.7)2 = 331 + 102 = 433 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct area of curved side or base seen ✓ correct total surface area (F/T) Solution 𝑠= √5.72 + 17.62 = 18.5 cm Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct use of Pythagoras' Theorem ✓ correct slant height Solution Leng",
