    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 2 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 0.70 US dollars. (a) How many US dollars can be bought for (i) 500 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (ii) 280 Australian dollars? (1 mark) (b) How many Australian dollars are needed to buy 70 US dollars? (1 mark) One Australian dollar can buy 10 South African rand. (c) At an airport a traveller wants to buy 5 000 rand, but the exchange desk also charges them a commission of 3%. Determine the total cost, in Australian dollars, for the traveller to buy this amount of currency. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 2 (6 marks) One Australian dollar can buy 0.70 US dollars. (a) How many US dollars can be bought for (i) 500 Australian dollars? (1 mark) Solution 500 × 0.70 = 𝑈𝑆$350 Specific behaviours ✔ correct amount (ii) 280 Australian dollars? (1 mark) Solution 280 × 0.70 = 𝑈𝑆$196 Specific behaviours ✔ correct amount (b) How many Australian dollars are needed to buy 70 US dollars? (1 mark) Solution 70 ÷ 0.70 = 𝐴$100 Specific behaviours ✔ correct amount One Australian dollar can buy 10 South African rand. (c) At an airport a traveller wants to buy 5 000 rand, but the exchange desk also charges them a commission of 3%. Determine the total cost, in Australian dollars, for the traveller to buy this amount of currency. (3 marks) Solution 5000 ÷ 10 = 500",
