    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page Question 3 (9 marks) Four matrices are defined as 𝐴= [4 −1 6 ], 𝐵= [2 1 −1 7 −2 3 ], 𝐶= [1 3 −2 0 ] and 𝐷= [5 −4 ]. (a) State (i) which matrix has more rows than columns. (1 mark) (ii) the dimensions of the row matrix. (1 mark) (b) Calculate 5𝐶+ 3𝐼, where 𝐼 is the 2 × 2 identity matrix. (3 marks) (c) Calculate 𝐶2. (2 marks) (d) It is required to multiply all four matrices together so that the final product is a square matrix with the largest possible number of columns. State the order in which the matrices should be multiplied and state the number of columns in the final product. (2 marks)",
