    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 4 (6 marks) During the week, casual employees at a recycling plant are paid a wage of $15 per hour plus $1.50 for every kg of electronic waste they collect. Over the weekend, both rates are increased by 20%. A casual worked for 4 hours on Sunday, collecting 30 kg of electronic waste, and then a further 6 hours on Monday when they collected 50 kg of electronic waste. (a) Determine the hourly pay rate for weekends. (1 mark) (b) Calculate how much the casual earned on Monday. (2 marks) (c) Calculate the total earned by the casual over the two days. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 3 (9 marks) Four matrices are defined as 𝐴= [4 −1 6 ], 𝐵= [2 1 −1 7 −2 3 ], 𝐶= [1 3 −2 0 ] and 𝐷= [5 −4 ]. (a) State (i) which matrix has more rows than columns. (1 mark) Solution 𝑀𝑎𝑡𝑟𝑖𝑥 𝐴 Specific behaviours ✔ correct name (ii) the dimensions of the row matrix. (1 mark) Solution Size of matrix 𝐷 is 1 × 2 Specific behaviours ✔ correct size (b) Calculate 5𝐶+ 3𝐼, where 𝐼 is the 2 × 2 identity matrix. (3 marks) Solution 5 × [1 3 −2 0 ] = [5 15 −10 0 ] 3𝐼= [3 0 0 3 ] 5𝐶+ 3𝐼= [5 15 −10 0 ] + [3 0 0 3 ] = [8 15 −10 3 ] Specific behaviours ✔ correct multiple of 𝐶 ✔ correct multiple of 𝐼 ✔ correct sum",
    "questionImage": "apps year 11/generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-waep-2019-yr11-apps-u1-s1-74f6f0e60d-p007-question-dae48369b9.jpg",
