    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 5 (6 marks) Hockey teams A and B had each played 21 games in a league. Team A had won 11, lost 4 and drawn the remainder of its games. In total, the two teams had won 21 and drawn 14 games. (a) Show this information in a 2 × 3 matrix 𝐻, with columns ordered win, lose, draw and rows ordered team A and team B. (2 marks) Solution 𝐻= [11 4 6 10 3 8 ] Specific behaviours ✔ one row correct ✔ correct matrix (b) Each team gains 3 points for a win, 1 point for a draw and no points for a loss. Show this information in matrix 𝑃 that can be multiplied by matrix 𝐻. (1 mark) Solution 𝑃= [3 0 1 ] Specific behaviours ✔ correct matrix (c) Calculate 𝐻× 𝑃 and state which team is leading the other in the league. (3 marks) Solution [11 4 6 10 3 8 ] × [3 0 1 ] = [39 38 ] Team A is leading team B. Specific behaviours ✔ obtains a 2 × 1 product",
