    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Question 19 (8 marks) A right-triangular prism has dimensions shown in the diagram below. (a) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) (b) An eighth-size model is made of the prism, i.e. using a scale of 1: 8. Calculate the total surface area of this model. (2 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the original prism. (1 mark) (d) Another scale model is made of the prism, so that the dimensions of the sloping face are now 3.6 cm by 4 cm. Calculate the volume of this scale model. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page Solution 525 ÷ 100 × 116 = 609 𝑐 To be best value, price must be less, so $6.08. Specific behaviours ✔ calculates price to be equal best ✔ correct price (2 marks) (d) Suggest one reason that a shopper may prefer a size other than that which offers the best value in terms of unit price. (1 mark) Solution - avoid wastage - don't have enough money, etc, etc Specific behaviours ✔ sensible reason",
