    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN295-173-1 Question 2 (5 marks) (a) Describe the type (using row, column, square, zero or identity) of each of the following matrices: (i) [0 1]. (1 mark) (ii) [1 0 1 0 1 0]. (1 mark) (iii) [ 1 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 1 ]. (1 mark) (b) The size of matrix [ 0 1 0 0 1 0 ] is 𝑚× 𝑛. State the value of 𝑚. (1 mark) (c) Write the 4 × 2 zero matrix 𝑂. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN295-173-3 Question 2 (5 marks) (a) Describe the type (using row, column, square, zero or identity) of each of the following matrices: (i) [0 1]. (1 mark) (ii) [1 0 1 0 1 0]. (1 mark) (iii) [ 1 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 1 ]. (1 mark) (b) The size of matrix [ 0 1 0 0 1 0 ] is 𝑚× 𝑛. State the value of 𝑚. (1 mark) (c) Write the 4 × 2 zero matrix 𝑂. (1 mark) Solution Square Specific behaviours  correct type Solution 𝑂= [ 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 ] Specific behaviours  correct matrix Solution 𝑚= 3 Specific behaviours  correct size Solution Row Specific behaviours  correct type Solution Column Specific behaviours  correct type",
