    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-1 Question 3 (5 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar right triangles. (a) Calculate the scale factor for the larger triangle relative to the smaller. (1 mark) (b) Determine the length of side 𝐴𝐶, the length of side 𝐷𝐹 and the length of side 𝐸𝐹. (3 marks) (c) Calculate how many times greater the area of the large triangle is compared to the area of the small triangle. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-3 Question 3 (5 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows two similar right triangles. (a) Calculate the scale factor for the larger triangle relative to the smaller. (1 mark) (b) Determine the length of side 𝐴𝐶, the length of side 𝐷𝐹 and the length of side 𝐸𝐹. (3 marks) (c) Calculate how many times greater the area of the large triangle is compared to the area of the small triangle. (1 mark) Solution 32 = 9 The area is 9 times larger. Specific behaviours  squares linear scale factor Solution 𝐴𝐶= √32 + 42 = 5 cm 𝐷𝐹= 3 × 5 = 15 cm 𝐸𝐹= 3 × 3 = 9 cm Specific behaviours  calculates 𝐴𝐶  uses scale factor to calculate 𝐷𝐹  uses scale factor to calculate 𝐸𝐹 Solution 12 ÷ 4 = 3 The scale factor is 3. Specific behaviours  correct scale factor",
