    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-1 Question 5 (5 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑎+ 𝑏× 𝑐 when 𝑎= 5, 𝑏= 5 and 𝑐= 6. (1 mark) (b) Use the formula 𝑦= (𝑥−1)(𝑥+ 4) to calculate 𝑦 when 𝑥= 0.5. (2 marks) (c) Use the formula 𝑠= 𝑢𝑡+ 1 2 𝑎𝑡2 to calculate 𝑠 when 𝑢= 4.5, 𝑡= 10 and 𝑎= 3.8. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-3 Question 5 (5 marks) (a) Calculate the value of 𝑎+ 𝑏× 𝑐 when 𝑎= 5, 𝑏= 5 and 𝑐= 6. (1 mark) (b) Use the formula 𝑦= (𝑥−1)(𝑥+ 4) to calculate 𝑦 when 𝑥= 0.5. (2 marks) (c) Use the formula 𝑠= 𝑢𝑡+ 1 2 𝑎𝑡2 to calculate 𝑠 when 𝑢= 4.5, 𝑡= 10 and 𝑎= 3.8. (2 marks) Solution 5 + 5 × 6 = 5 + 30 = 35 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 𝑦= (−0.5)(4.5) = −2.25 Specific behaviours  evaluates terms in brackets  correct value Solution 𝑠= 4.5 × 10 + 1 2 × 3.8 × 102 = 45 + 1.9 × 100 = 45 + 190 = 235 Specific behaviours  substitutes and starts to simplify  correct value",
