    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN295-173-1 (c) Calculate matrix 𝑇, where 𝑇= 𝑋+ 𝑌 and explain what information it represents. (2 marks) The price per trip was $10 per adult and $5 per child. (d) Represent the price information in matrix 𝑃 that can be meaningfully multiplied by matrix 𝑇, calculate 𝑃𝑇 and explain what information it represents. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN295-173-3 (c) Calculate matrix 𝑇, where 𝑇= 𝑋+ 𝑌 and explain what information it represents. (2 marks) The price per trip was $10 per adult and $5 per child. (d) Represent the price information in matrix 𝑃 that can be meaningfully multiplied by matrix 𝑇, calculate 𝑃𝑇 and explain what information it represents. (4 marks) Solution 𝑇= [48 65 42 24 44 25] + [52 25 43 26 26 35] = [100 90 85 50 70 60] 𝑇 shows the number of adults and children carried by boats 𝐷, 𝐸 and 𝐹 over the weekend. Specific behaviours  correct matrix 𝑇  correct explanation Solution 𝑃= [10 5] 𝑃𝑇= [10 5] [100 90 85 50 70 60] = [1250 1250 1150] Matrix 𝑃𝑇 shows the total passenger fares collected over the weekend by boats 𝐷, 𝐸 and 𝐹. Specific behaviours  correct matrix 𝑃  at least one correct entry in 𝑃𝑇  correct product  correct explanation",
