    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN295-173-1 Question 8 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows a prism with trapezoidal cross-section 𝑂𝑃𝑄𝑅, where 𝑂𝑃= 8 cm, 𝑃𝑄= 15 cm, 𝑄𝑅= 17 cm, 𝑂𝑅= 30 cm and 𝑅𝑆= 10 cm. (a) Calculate the area of the cross-section 𝑂𝑃𝑄𝑅. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the volume of the prism. (2 marks) (c) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN295-173-3 Question 8 (7 marks) The diagram below, not drawn to scale, shows a prism with trapezoidal cross-section 𝑂𝑃𝑄𝑅, where 𝑂𝑃= 8 cm, 𝑃𝑄= 15 cm, 𝑄𝑅= 17 cm, 𝑂𝑅= 30 cm and 𝑅𝑆= 10 cm. (a) Calculate the area of the cross-section 𝑂𝑃𝑄𝑅. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the volume of the prism. (2 marks) (c) Determine the total surface area of the prism. (3 marks) Solution 𝑉= 180 × 10 = 1800 cm3 Specific behaviours  correctly uses answer from (a)  calculates volume Solution Top, bottom, back and sloping face: 𝐴= 10 × (8 + 15 + 17 + 30) = 10 × 70 = 700 Two ends: 𝐴= 2 × 180 = 360 Total: 𝐴= 700 + 360 = 1060 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates appropriate method for four rectangles  includes both trapezoidal faces  calculates total surface area Solution 𝐴= 15 × 8 + 1 2 × 15 × 8 = 120 + 60 = 180 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates appropriate method  calculates area",
