    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-2 Question 10 (8 marks) (a) A design for a button consists of a circle of radius 17 mm with four circles of radius 5 mm removed, as shown below. Determine the area of the shaded region. (3 marks) (b) Another design consists of a sector of a circle of diameter 16 mm, as shown below. (i) Determine the area of the sector. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the sector. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-4 Question 10 (8 marks) (a) A design for a button consists of a circle of radius 17 mm with four circles of radius 5 mm removed, as shown below. Determine the area of the shaded region. (3 marks) (b) Another design consists of a sector of a circle of diameter 16 mm, as shown below. (i) Determine the area of the sector. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the sector. (2 marks) Solution 𝜃= 360 −75 = 285, 𝑟= 16 ÷ 2 = 8 𝐴= 285 360 × 𝜋(8)2 = 159 mm2 Specific behaviours  calculates internal sector angle  calculates radius  calculates area Solution Arc length: 𝐿= 285 360 × 2𝜋(8) = 39.8 Perimeter: 𝑃= 39.8 + 2(8) = 55.8 mm Specific behaviours  calculates arc length  calculates perimeter Solution 𝐴𝐿= 𝜋(17)2 = 908 𝐴𝑆= 𝜋(5)2 = 78.5 4𝐴𝑆= 314 Shaded area: 𝐴= 908 −314 = 594 mm2 Specific behaviours  area of large circle  area of 4 small circles  calculates shaded area",
