    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-2 Question 13 (8 marks) A solid object takes the form shown. ABCDEFGH is a square prism with sides AB = BC = 48 cm and height 𝐴𝐸= 13 m. The apex T of pyramid EFGHT lies 45 cm directly above the centre of square EFGH. The four sloping faces of the pyramid are congruent isosceles triangles, so that the length from 𝑇 to 𝑀, the midpoint of edge EF is 51 cm. (a) Determine the area of one of the triangular faces of the pyramid. (2 marks) (b) Determine the surface area of the object. (3 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the object. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-4 Question 13 (8 marks) A solid object takes the form shown. ABCDEFGH is a square prism with sides AB = BC = 48 cm and height 𝐴𝐸= 13 m. The apex T of pyramid EFGHT lies 45 cm directly above the centre of square EFGH. The four sloping faces of the pyramid are congruent isosceles triangles, so that the length from 𝑇 to 𝑀, the midpoint of edge EF is 51 cm. (a) Determine the area of one of the triangular faces of the pyramid. (2 marks) (b) Determine the surface area of the object. (3 marks) (c) Determine the volume of the object. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴= 1 2 × 48 × 51 = 1224 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct choice and use of formula  calculates area Solution One rectangular face: 48 × 13 = 624 Square base: 48 × 48 = 2304 Total surface area: 𝐴= 2304 + 4 × 624 + 4 × 1224 = 9696 cm2 Specific behaviours  correctly calculates one relevant area  clearly indicates correct method to obtain total area  correct surface area Solution Pyramid: 𝑉= 1 3 (2304)(45) = 34 560 Square prism: 𝑉= 2304 × 13 = 29 952 Hence total volume: 𝑉= 34 560 + 29 952 = 64 512 cm3 Specific behaviours  volume of pyramid  volume of prism  correc",
