    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-2 Question 18 (8 marks) The following spreadsheet was used to calculate the weekly pay of four office assistants. In this pay period, Friday was a public holiday, and the assistants were paid time-and-a-half that day. A B C D E F G H 1 Employee Base pay rate ($ per hour) Daily hours worked Weekly pay ($) 2 Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri 3 Ian 24.75 8 0 8 7 4 717.75 4 Jem 26.50 5 ? 0 6 0 450.50 5 Kai 33.50 0 8 5 8 5 954.75 6 Liam 30.25 6 4 6 0 0 ? (a) Show that the total pay for hours worked on Friday by the assistants came to $399.75. (2 marks) (b) Determine the missing value in cell H6 and the missing value in cell D4. (3 marks) (c) By referring to the value in a spreadsheet cell using its column letter followed by its row number (e.g., B4 refers to the value 26.50 in that cell) write a formula to (i) recalculate the value in cell H3 when any cell value in the spreadsheet is changed. (1 mark) (ii) place in cell H7 that will calculate the total weekly pay for the assistants, and state what this total is. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-4 Question 18 (8 marks) The following spreadsheet was used to calculate the weekly pay of four office assistants. In this pay period, Friday was a public holiday, and the assistants were paid time-and-a-half that day. A B C D E F G H 1 Employee Base pay rate ($ per hour) Daily hours worked Weekly pay ($) 2 Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri 3 Ian 24.75 8 0 8 7 4 717.75 4 Jem 26.50 5 ? 0 6 0 450.50 5 Kai 33.50 0 8 5 8 5 954.75 6 Liam 30.25 6 4 6 0 0 ? (a) Show that the total pay for hours worked on Friday by the assistants came to $399.75. (2 marks) (b) Determine the missing value in cell H6 and the missing value in cell D4. (3 marks) (c) By referring to the value in a spreadsheet cell using its column letter followed by its row number (e.g., B4 refers to the value 26.50 in that cell) write a formula to (i) recalculate the value in cell H3 when any cell value in the spreadsheet is changed. (1 mark) (ii) place in cell H7 that will calculate the total weekly pay for the assistants, and state what this total is. (2 marks) Solution 𝐻6 = (6 + 4 + 6) × 30.25 = 484.00 (5 + 𝑥+ 6) × 26.50 = 450.50 →𝑥= 𝐷4 = 6 Specific behaviours  value of H6",
