    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-2 Question 19 (8 marks) The following diagram, drawn to scale, shows the plan for a new rectangular lawn on a plot of level ground. The lawn is 6 metres wide. (a) Determine, to the nearest metre, the length of the lawn. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total cost of turf to cover the lawn, given that suitable turf costs $16.25 per square metre. (2 marks) (c) Express the scale factor of the drawing in the form 1: 𝑛. (2 marks) (d) The turf will be laid on top of a layer of special soil that has a uniform depth of 75 mm. Determine the volume of soil that is required. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 See next page SN295-173-4 Question 19 (8 marks) The following diagram, drawn to scale, shows the plan for a new rectangular lawn on a plot of level ground. The lawn is 6 metres wide. (a) Determine, to the nearest metre, the length of the lawn. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total cost of turf to cover the lawn, given that suitable turf costs $16.25 per square metre. (2 marks) (c) Express the scale factor of the drawing in the form 1: 𝑛. (2 marks) (d) The turf will be laid on top of a layer of special soil that has a uniform depth of 75 mm. Determine the volume of soil that is required. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴= 6 × 18 = 108 m2 Cost = 108 × 16.25 = $1755 Specific behaviours  indicates area of lawn  correct cost Solution 30 mm ∶6 m →30 ∶6000 →1: 200 Specific behaviours  correctly eliminates units  correct scale factor Solution 𝑉= 108 × 0.075 𝑉= 8.1 m3 Specific behaviours  converts soil thickness to metres  correct volume of soil with units Solution On diagram, width is 30 mm and length is 90 mm. 𝐿= 90 30 × 6 = 18 m Specific behaviours  indicates use of appropriate method  correct length",
