    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-2 Question 20 (8 marks) A company makes spherical floats with an external radius of 30 cm for use in boat harbours. (a) The external surface of a float is coated with a special epoxy paint that costs $95 per square metre. Determine the cost of this paint for one float. (3 marks) (b) Each float is made from an inner solid steel sphere of radius 12 cm surrounded by a thick layer of polystyrene, as shown in the cutaway diagram. Given that the weights of one cubic centimetre of steel and polystyrene are 6.2 and 0.025 grams respectively, determine the total weight of materials in one float. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN295-173-4 Question 20 (8 marks) A company makes spherical floats with an external radius of 30 cm for use in boat harbours. (a) The external surface of a float is coated with a special epoxy paint that costs $95 per square metre. Determine the cost of this paint for one float. (3 marks) (b) Each float is made from an inner solid steel sphere of radius 12 cm surrounded by a thick layer of polystyrene, as shown in the cutaway diagram. Given that the weights of one cubic centimetre of steel and polystyrene are 6.2 and 0.025 grams respectively, determine the total weight of materials in one float. (5 marks) Solution Whole volume: 𝑉= 4 3 𝜋(30)3 = 113 097 cm3 Steel volume: 𝑉𝑆= 4 3 𝜋(12)3 = 7238 cm3 Polystyrene volume: 𝑉𝑃= 113 097 −7238 = 105 859 cm3 Steel weight: 𝑊𝑆= 7238 × 6.2 = 44 877 g Polystyrene weight: 𝑊𝑃= 105 859 × 0.025 = 2646 g Total weight: 𝑊= 44 877 + 2646 = 47 523 g Specific behaviours  calculates volume of whole sphere  calculates volume of inner sphere  calculates volume of polystyrene  calculates weight of at least one material  calculates total weight and states units Solution 𝑟= 0.30 m Surface area: 𝐴= 4𝜋(0.3",
