    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN295-173-2 Question 21 (8 marks) When a sum of $1400 is invested at a rate of 𝑅 percent per annum, compounded every two months, the total interest 𝐼 accumulated after 𝑇 years is given by the formula 𝐼= 1400 ((1 + 𝑅 600) 6𝑇 −1) This formula has been used to create the spreadsheet below. A B C D E F G 1 Interest, 𝐼 Rate, 𝑅 2 1 2 3 4 5 3 Time, 𝑇 1 14.06 28.23 42.53 56.94 71.47 4 2 28.26 57.04 86.35 116.20 146.60 5 3 42.60 86.42 131.50 177.87 225.56 6 4 57.09 116.4 178.02 242.04 ? (a) When the rate is 3% per annum, determine (i) the total interest accumulated after 3 years. (1 mark) (ii) the interest accumulated during the fourth year. (2 marks) (b) Determine, to the nearest cent, the total interest after 4 years at a rate of 5% per annum. (2 marks) (c) If the spreadsheet was extended, determine the value that would appear in cell K8. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 APPLICATIONS UNIT 1 End of questions SN295-173-4 Question 21 (8 marks) When a sum of $1400 is invested at a rate of 𝑅 percent per annum, compounded every two months, the total interest 𝐼 accumulated after 𝑇 years is given by the formula 𝐼= 1400 ((1 + 𝑅 600) 6𝑇 −1) This formula has been used to create the spreadsheet below. A B C D E F G 1 Interest, 𝐼 Rate, 𝑅 2 1 2 3 4 5 3 Time, 𝑇 1 14.06 28.23 42.53 56.94 71.47 4 2 28.26 57.04 86.35 116.20 146.60 5 3 42.60 86.42 131.50 177.87 225.56 6 4 57.09 116.4 178.02 242.04 ? (a) When the rate is 3% per annum, determine (i) the total interest accumulated after 3 years. (1 mark) (ii) the interest accumulated during the fourth year. (2 marks) (b) Determine, to the nearest cent, the total interest after 4 years at a rate of 5% per annum. (2 marks) (c) If the spreadsheet was extended, determine the value that would appear in cell K8. (3 marks) Solution $131.50 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 178.02 −131.50 = $46.52 Specific behaviours  uses difference of years  correct value Solution In cell K8, 𝑅= 9 and 𝑇= 6 𝐼= 1400 ((1 + 9 600) 6×6 −1) = $992.80 Specific behaviours  indicates correct values for 𝑅 and 𝑇  sub",
