    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-1 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight (8) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) (a) Solve the equation 4(5 −2𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥−7 for 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (b) Ash, Billie and Chris collected a total of 160 cans to recycle. Ash collected twice as many cans as Chris, Chris collected 12 more cans than Billie and Billie collected 𝑥𝑥 cans. Determine how many cans Billie collected. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-2 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight (8) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) (a) Solve the equation 4(5 −2𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥−7 for 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (b) Ash, Billie and Chris collected a total of 160 cans to recycle. Ash collected twice as many cans as Chris, Chris collected 12 more cans than Billie and Billie collected 𝑥𝑥 cans. Determine how many cans Billie collected. (3 marks) Solution 20 −8𝑥𝑥= 𝑥𝑥−7 27 = 9𝑥𝑥 𝑥𝑥= 3 Specific behaviours  expands LHS  collects like terms and solves Solution 𝑥𝑥+ (𝑥𝑥+ 12) + 2(𝑥𝑥+ 12) = 160 4𝑥𝑥+ 36 = 160 4𝑥𝑥= 124 𝑥𝑥= Billie's cans = 31 Specific behaviours  indicates number of cans each has  forms and simplifies equation  correct number",
