    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-123-1 Question 4 (8 marks) (a) The power 𝑃𝑃 consumed by a device can be calculated using the formula 𝑃𝑃= 𝐼𝐼2𝑅𝑅+ √2𝑅𝑅. Calculate the value of 𝑃𝑃 when (i) 𝐼𝐼= 5 and 𝑅𝑅= 8. (2 marks) (ii) 𝐼𝐼= 0.5 and 𝑅𝑅= 50. (2 marks) (b) The variable 𝐷𝐷 is related to diameters 𝑑𝑑1, 𝑑𝑑2 and 𝑑𝑑3 by the formula 𝐷𝐷= 𝑑𝑑1 4 + 2 𝑑𝑑2 −𝑑𝑑3 . Calculate the value of 𝐷𝐷 when (i) 𝑑𝑑1 = 2, 𝑑𝑑2 = 9 and 𝑑𝑑3 = 1. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑑𝑑1 = 18, 𝑑𝑑2 = 3.5 and 𝑑𝑑3 = 4. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-123-2 Question 4 (8 marks) (a) The power 𝑃𝑃 consumed by a device can be calculated using the formula 𝑃𝑃= 𝐼𝐼2𝑅𝑅+ √2𝑅𝑅. Calculate the value of 𝑃𝑃 when (i) 𝐼𝐼= 5 and 𝑅𝑅= 8. (2 marks) (ii) 𝐼𝐼= 0.5 and 𝑅𝑅= 50. (2 marks) (b) The variable 𝐷𝐷 is related to diameters 𝑑𝑑1, 𝑑𝑑2 and 𝑑𝑑3 by the formula 𝐷𝐷= 𝑑𝑑1 4 + 2 𝑑𝑑2 −𝑑𝑑3 . Calculate the value of 𝐷𝐷 when (i) 𝑑𝑑1 = 2, 𝑑𝑑2 = 9 and 𝑑𝑑3 = 1. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑑𝑑1 = 18, 𝑑𝑑2 = 3.5 and 𝑑𝑑3 = 4. (2 marks) Solution 𝐷𝐷= 2 4 + 2 9 −1 = 2 4 + 2 8 𝐷𝐷= 2 4 + 1 4 = 3 4 Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly, simplifying 𝑑𝑑2 −𝑑𝑑3  evaluates correctly Solution 𝑃𝑃= 52 × 8 + √2 × 8 𝑃𝑃= 25 × 8 + √16 𝑃𝑃= 200 + 4 = 204 Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly, simplifying 𝐼𝐼2 and 2𝑅𝑅  evaluates correctly Solution 𝑃𝑃= 0.52 × 50 + √2 × 50 𝑃𝑃= 0.25 × 50 + √100 𝑃𝑃= 12.5 + 10 = 22.5 Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly, simplifying 𝐼𝐼2 and 2𝑅𝑅  evaluates correctly Solution 𝐷𝐷= 18 4 + 2 3.5 −4 = 18 4 + 2 −0.5 𝐷𝐷= 4.5 −4 = 0.5 Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly, simplifying 𝑑𝑑2 −𝑑𝑑3  evaluates correctly",
