    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-1 Question 7 (7 marks) (a) The lines with equations 2𝑦𝑦+ 2 = 𝑥𝑥 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 𝑥𝑥= −6 are shown on the axes below. (i) Draw the line 𝑦𝑦= 𝑥𝑥−6 on the axes above. (2 marks) (ii) Solve the simultaneous equations 𝑦𝑦= 𝑥𝑥−6 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 2 = 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (b) Solve the simultaneous equations 𝑥𝑥+ 𝑦𝑦= 7 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 𝑥𝑥= −6. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-2 Question 7 (7 marks) (a) The lines with equations 2𝑦𝑦+ 2 = 𝑥𝑥 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 𝑥𝑥= −6 are shown on the axes below. (i) Draw the line 𝑦𝑦= 𝑥𝑥−6 on the axes above. (2 marks) (ii) Solve the simultaneous equations 𝑦𝑦= 𝑥𝑥−6 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 2 = 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (b) Solve the simultaneous equations 𝑥𝑥+ 𝑦𝑦= 7 and 2𝑦𝑦+ 𝑥𝑥= −6. (3 marks) Solution (2𝑦𝑦+ 𝑥𝑥= −6) −(𝑥𝑥+ 𝑦𝑦= 7) 𝑦𝑦= −13 𝑥𝑥−13 = 7 𝑥𝑥= 20 Specific behaviours  indicates use of substitution or elimination  solves for 𝑦𝑦  solves for 𝑥𝑥 Solution See graph Specific behaviours  𝑦𝑦-intercept  𝑥𝑥-intercept Solution From graph, 𝑥𝑥= 10, 𝑦𝑦= 4 Specific behaviours  indicates appropriate method  correct values of 𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦",
