    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-123-4 Question 10 (5 marks) (a) Show use of trigonometry to determine the length of side 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 in the triangle below, where ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 122°, 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 58 cm and 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 71 cm. (2 marks) (b) Show use of trigonometry to determine the size of angle ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃 in the triangle below, where ∠𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 105°, 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃= 45 cm and 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄= 65 cm. (3 marks) Solution If 𝑥𝑥= ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃 then sin 𝑥𝑥 45 = sin105 65 𝑥𝑥= 42° ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃= 180 −105 −42 = 33° Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly into sine rule  correct value for ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃  size of required angle Solution 𝐵𝐵𝐶𝐶2 = 582 + 712 −2(58)(71) cos122 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 113 cm Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly into cosine rule  correct length",
