    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-123-3 Question 12 (7 marks) Soup is sold in cylindrical tins that have an internal diameter of 7.6 cm and a height of 13.6 cm. (a) Calculate the internal surface area of the can. (3 marks) (b) Calculate the capacity of the can in millilitres. (1 mL = 1 cm3) (2 marks) (c) Before the cans are sealed, they are stood on their circular end and filled with 540 mL of soup. Determine the depth of soup in the can. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-123-4 Question 12 (7 marks) Soup is sold in cylindrical tins that have an internal diameter of 7.6 cm and a height of 13.6 cm. (a) Calculate the internal surface area of the can. (3 marks) (b) Calculate the capacity of the can in millilitres. (1 mL = 1 cm3) (2 marks) (c) Before the cans are sealed, they are stood on their circular end and filled with 540 mL of soup. Determine the depth of soup in the can. (2 marks) Solution 540 = 𝜋𝜋× 3.82 × ℎ ℎ= 11.9 cm Specific behaviours  substitutes into formula  solves for ℎ Solution 𝑉𝑉= 𝜋𝜋× 3.82 × 13.6 = 617 mL Specific behaviours  substitutes into formula  evaluates Solution 𝑟𝑟= 7.6 ÷ 2 = 3.8 𝐴𝐴= 2𝜋𝜋× 3.82 + 2𝜋𝜋× 13.6 = 415 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct radius  substitutes into formula  evaluates",
