    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-3 Question 18 (8 marks) The top of a vertical pole 𝑇𝑇 stands 6.4 m above a surrounding level playing field. The angle of depression from 𝑇𝑇 to a small animal at 𝐴𝐴 is 32°. The animal leaves 𝐴𝐴, moves directly towards the base of the pole 𝐵𝐵 and stops at 𝐶𝐶 (before reaching 𝐵𝐵). The distance 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is 5.5 m. (a) Sketch a diagram to show the above information. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the line of sight distance from the top of the pole to 𝐴𝐴. (2 marks) (c) Determine the angle of depression from 𝑇𝑇 to 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks) (d) Calculate the distance travelled by the animal from 𝐴𝐴 to 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-123-4 Question 18 (8 marks) The top of a vertical pole 𝑇𝑇 stands 6.4 m above a surrounding level playing field. The angle of depression from 𝑇𝑇 to a small animal at 𝐴𝐴 is 32°. The animal leaves 𝐴𝐴, moves directly towards the base of the pole 𝐵𝐵 and stops at 𝐶𝐶 (before reaching 𝐵𝐵). The distance 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is 5.5 m. (a) Sketch a diagram to show the above information. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the line of sight distance from the top of the pole to 𝐴𝐴. (2 marks) (c) Determine the angle of depression from 𝑇𝑇 to 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks) (d) Calculate the distance travelled by the animal from 𝐴𝐴 to 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 6.4 ÷ tan 32 = 10.2 m 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 10.2 −5.5 = 4.7 m Specific behaviours  calculates 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴  calculates 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 Solution ∠𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇= tan−1 6.4 5.5 = 49.3° Specific behaviours  uses tangent ratio  correct angle (to nearest degree) Solution Specific behaviours  vertical 𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇 with angle of depression to 𝐴𝐴  lengths 𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇 and 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵, making a right-angle Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 6.4 ÷ sin32 = 12.1 m Specific behaviours  uses sine ratio  correct distance",
