    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-123-3 Question 19 (7 marks) The wind chill index 𝐼𝐼 is a measure of how quickly a person exposed to a wind will lose heat. It is calculated using the formula below, where 𝑣𝑣 is the speed of the wind in metres per second and 𝑇𝑇 is the air temperature in degrees Celsius. 𝐼𝐼= ൫10√𝑣𝑣−𝑣𝑣+ 10.2൯(34 −𝑇𝑇) (a) Determine 𝐼𝐼 when the air temperature is −3°𝐶𝐶 and there is a wind of 12 m/s blowing. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the change in the wind chill index when the air temperature is −8°𝐶𝐶 and the strength of the wind decreases from 22 m/s to 8 m/s. (3 marks) (c) A person is likely to suffer from frostbite when the wind chill index reaches 1 500. At what temperature will this happen, on a day when the wind has a speed of 25 m/s? (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-123-4 Question 19 (7 marks) The wind chill index 𝐼𝐼 is a measure of how quickly a person exposed to a wind will lose heat. It is calculated using the formula below, where 𝑣𝑣 is the speed of the wind in metres per second and 𝑇𝑇 is the air temperature in degrees Celsius. 𝐼𝐼= ൫10√𝑣𝑣−𝑣𝑣+ 10.2൯(34 −𝑇𝑇) (a) Determine 𝐼𝐼 when the air temperature is −3°𝐶𝐶 and there is a wind of 12 m/s blowing. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the change in the wind chill index when the air temperature is −8°𝐶𝐶 and the strength of the wind decreases from 22 m/s to 8 m/s. (3 marks) (c) A person is likely to suffer from frostbite when the wind chill index reaches 1 500. At what temperature will this happen, on a day when the wind has a speed of 25 m/s? (2 marks) Solution 𝐼𝐼= (10√12 −12 + 10.2)(34 −−3) = 1215 Specific behaviours  correct substitution  evaluates Solution 1500 = (10√25 −25 + 10.2)(34 −𝑇𝑇) 1500 = 35.2(34 −𝑇𝑇) 𝑇𝑇= 34 −1500 35.2 = −8.6°𝐶𝐶 Specific behaviours  substitutes and simplifies  solves for temperature Solution 𝐼𝐼= (10√22 −22 + 10.2)(34 −−8) = 1474 𝐼𝐼= (10√8 −8 + 10.2)(34 −−8) = 1280 Decrease = 1474 −1280 = 194 Specific behaviou",
