    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN104-123-3 Question 21 (8 marks) When working out the cost of building an in-ground swimming pool, a contractor calculates a shape factor 𝑘𝑘 to use in a spreadsheet, where 𝑘𝑘= 𝑃𝑃2 4𝐴𝐴 . 𝑃𝑃 is the perimeter of the pool in metres and 𝐴𝐴 is the area of the pool in square metres. Pool 1 is rectangular with a semi-circular end and pool 2 is rectangular with a cut-out as shown. Determine, with justification, which of the pools shown has the larger shape factor 𝑘𝑘.",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN104-123-4 Question 21 (8 marks) When working out the cost of building an in-ground swimming pool, a contractor calculates a shape factor 𝑘𝑘 to use in a spreadsheet, where 𝑘𝑘= 𝑃𝑃2 4𝐴𝐴 . 𝑃𝑃 is the perimeter of the pool in metres and 𝐴𝐴 is the area of the pool in square metres. Pool 1 is rectangular with a semi-circular end and pool 2 is rectangular with a cut-out as shown. Determine, with justification, which of the pools shown has the larger shape factor 𝑘𝑘. Solution Pool 1 𝐴𝐴1 = 6 × 8 + 1 2 × 𝜋𝜋× 32 = 62.14 𝑃𝑃1 = 8 + 6 + 8 + 1 2 × 2 × 𝜋𝜋× 3 = 31.42 𝑘𝑘1 = 31.422 4 × 62.14 = 3.97 Pool 2 𝐴𝐴2 = 8 × 10 −2 × 4 −1 2 × 4 × 3 = 66 𝑃𝑃2 = 3 + 10 + 8 + 6 + 2 + 𝑥𝑥= 29 + 𝑥𝑥 𝑥𝑥= ඥ42 + 32 = 5 𝑃𝑃2 = 34 𝑘𝑘2 = 342 4 × 66 = 4.38 Pool 2 has the larger shape factor. Specific behaviours  area of pool 1  perimeter of pool 1  𝑘𝑘 for pool 1  area of pool 2  indicates missing length in pool 2  perimeter of pool 2  𝑘𝑘 for pool 2  identifies pool with larger 𝑘𝑘",
