    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-143-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 3 (7 marks) The graph of line 𝐿𝐿1 with equation 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏 is shown below. (a) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (2 marks) (b) Straight-line 𝐿𝐿2 has equation 𝑥𝑥+ 2𝑦𝑦= 8. (i) Draw 𝐿𝐿2 on the axes above. (2 marks) (ii) State the gradient of 𝐿𝐿2. (1 mark) (c) Determine the equation of the straight-line 𝐿𝐿3 that passes through the origin and the point of intersection of lines 𝐿𝐿1 and 𝐿𝐿2. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-143-2 Question 3 (7 marks) The graph of line 𝐿𝐿1 with equation 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏 is shown below. (a) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (2 marks) (b) Straight-line 𝐿𝐿2 has equation 𝑥𝑥+ 2𝑦𝑦= 8. (i) Draw 𝐿𝐿2 on the axes above. (2 marks) (ii) State the gradient of 𝐿𝐿2. (1 mark) (c) Determine the equation of the straight-line 𝐿𝐿3 that passes through the origin and the point of intersection of lines 𝐿𝐿1 and 𝐿𝐿2. (2 marks) Solution 𝑚𝑚= −1 2 = −0.5 Specific behaviours  correct gradient Solution 𝑚𝑚= 2 4 = 1 2 ⇒𝑦𝑦= 1 2 𝑥𝑥 Specific behaviours  indicates correct gradient  correct equation Solution Gradient = 𝑎𝑎= 2. 𝑦𝑦-intercept = 𝑏𝑏= −6. Specific behaviours  value of 𝑎𝑎  value of 𝑏𝑏 Solution (b)(i) See graph Specific behaviours  𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦 intercepts  ruled straight line",
