    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-143-2 Question 4 (9 marks) The dot plot below shows the goal difference between each pair of teams playing in a weekend round of a soccer league. (a) State the number of games that did not end in a draw. (1 mark) (b) Classify the type of variable that goal difference is by circling two of the following words: (1 mark) Categorical. Continuous. Discrete. Nominal. Numerical. Ordinal. (c) Determine (i) the median goal difference. (1 mark) (ii) the mean goal difference. (2 marks) Solution 25 −5 = 20 games Specific behaviours  correct number Solution Median is 13th score = 1 Specific behaviours  correct median Solution 0 + 9 + 6 + 12 + 12 + 6 25 = 45 25 = 9 5 = 1.8 Specific behaviours  indicates correct method  correct mean (as fraction or decimal) Solution Discrete and Numerical Specific behaviours  clearly circles both",
