    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-143-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (7 marks) The number of minutes that a group of students took to complete a task are listed below: 29, 26, 17, 29, 18, 26, 31, 25, 26, 35, 33, 28 (a) Construct an ordered stem-and-leaf plot to display this data. (3 marks) (b) Identify, with justification, any outliers that may be present in the times. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-143-2 Question 5 (7 marks) The number of minutes that a group of students took to complete a task are listed below: 29, 26, 17, 29, 18, 26, 31, 25, 26, 35, 33, 28 (a) Construct an ordered stem-and-leaf plot to display this data. (3 marks) (b) Identify, with justification, any outliers that may be present in the times. (4 marks) Solution 𝑄𝑄1 = 25.5, 𝑄𝑄3 = 30 1.5 × 𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼= 1.5 × 4.5 = 6.75 𝑄𝑄1 −6.75 = 25.5 −6.75 = 18.75 Any times less than 18.75 minutes are outliers. Hence the times of 17 and 18 minutes are both outliers. Specific behaviours  identifies quartiles  calculates 1.5𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼𝐼  calculates lower bound  identifies both outliers Solution Specific behaviours  stems and leaves aligned in columns  two correct set of leaves  all sets of leaves, correctly ordered",
