    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-143-2 Question 6 (5 marks) (a) Solve the equation 3(𝑥𝑥+ 5) −1 = 𝑥𝑥−2(𝑥𝑥−3). (2 marks) (b) Use the formula 𝐴𝐴= 1 2 (𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏)ℎ to determine (i) 𝐴𝐴 when 𝑎𝑎= 5.6, 𝑏𝑏= 8.4 and ℎ= 20. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑏𝑏 when 𝐴𝐴= 33, 𝑎𝑎= 4 and ℎ= 6. (2 marks) Solution 3𝑥𝑥+ 15 −1 = 𝑥𝑥−2𝑥𝑥+ 6 4𝑥𝑥= −8 𝑥𝑥= −2 Specific behaviours  correctly expands  correct solution Solution 𝐴𝐴= 1 2 (5.6 + 8.4) × 20 = 10 × 14 = 140 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 33 = 1 2 (4 + 𝑏𝑏) × 6 33 = 3(4 + 𝑏𝑏) 11 = 4 + 𝑏𝑏 𝑏𝑏= 7 Specific behaviours  substitutes and simplifies  correct value of 𝑏𝑏",
