    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 End of questions SN104-143-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (6 marks) At the start of the year 2002, the difference in the ages of a mother and her child was 24. Let the age of the mother be 𝑥𝑥 and the age of her child be 𝑦𝑦 at the start of 2002. (a) Use the above information to write an equation relating 𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦. (1 mark) Three years later, the mother was 5 times as old as her child. (b) Use this additional information to write another equation relating 𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦. (2 marks) (c) Determine the age of the child at the start of the year 2019. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 End of questions SN104-143-2 Question 8 (6 marks) At the start of the year 2002, the difference in the ages of a mother and her child was 24. Let the age of the mother be 𝑥𝑥 and the age of her child be 𝑦𝑦 at the start of 2002. (a) Use the above information to write an equation relating 𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦. (1 mark) Three years later, the mother was 5 times as old as her child. (b) Use this additional information to write another equation relating 𝑥𝑥 and 𝑦𝑦. (2 marks) (c) Determine the age of the child at the start of the year 2019. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥𝑥−𝑦𝑦= 24 Specific behaviours  correct equation Solution In 3 years, mother will be 𝑥𝑥+ 3 and child will be 𝑦𝑦+ 3. 𝑥𝑥+ 3 = 5(𝑦𝑦+ 3) Specific behaviours  expressions for ages of mother and child in 3 years  correct equation Solution Substitute 𝑥𝑥= 𝑦𝑦+ 24 into second equation: 𝑦𝑦+ 24 + 3 = 5𝑦𝑦+ 15 4𝑦𝑦= 12 ⇒𝑦𝑦= 3 In 2019 child will be 𝑦𝑦+ 17 and so child will be 20 years old. Specific behaviours  substitutes and expands  solves for 𝑦𝑦  correct age of child",
