    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-143-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (8 marks) The shaded areas in the diagram below form a logo for a business. 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 is a semicircle with radius 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 30 cm and ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= ∠𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶. The inner semicircle has radius 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 14 cm. (a) Determine the area of the sector 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total shaded area. (3 marks) (c) Determine the shaded area in a copy of the logo that is enlarged by a scale factor of 5 for use on a flag, giving your answer in square metres. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-143-4 Question 15 (8 marks) The shaded areas in the diagram below form a logo for a business. 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 is a semicircle with radius 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 30 cm and ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= ∠𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶. The inner semicircle has radius 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 14 cm. (a) Determine the area of the sector 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (2 marks) (b) Determine the total shaded area. (3 marks) (c) Determine the shaded area in a copy of the logo that is enlarged by a scale factor of 5 for use on a flag, giving your answer in square metres. (3 marks) Solution Area of inner semicircle = 1 2 𝜋𝜋× 142 = 307.9 Area of sector = 307.9 ÷ 3 = 102.6 cm2 Specific behaviours  area of semicircle  area of sector Solution Area of sector 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 1 2 𝜋𝜋× 302 ÷ 3 = 471.2 Area of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 471.2 −102.6 = 368.6 Total shaded area = 2 × 368.6 + 102.6 = 839.8 cm2 Specific behaviours  sector area  area of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴  total area Solution New area = 52 × 839.8 = 20995 cm2 20995 ÷ 10 000 ≈2.1 m2 Specific behaviours  indicates area scale factor  area in sq cm  area in sq m",
