    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-143-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (7 marks) The lifetimes of a type of heating element are normally distributed with a mean of 455 hours and a standard deviation of 32 hours. (a) State the percentage of elements that are expected to have a lifetime within two standard deviations of the mean. (1 mark) (b) Determine the standard score for an element that lasts for 433 hours. (2 marks) (c) Determine the probability that a randomly selected element will have a lifetime (i) of less than 433 hours. (1 mark) (ii) of more than 510 hours. (1 mark) (iii) within 25 hours of the mean lifetime. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN104-143-4 Question 16 (7 marks) The lifetimes of a type of heating element are normally distributed with a mean of 455 hours and a standard deviation of 32 hours. (a) State the percentage of elements that are expected to have a lifetime within two standard deviations of the mean. (1 mark) (b) Determine the standard score for an element that lasts for 433 hours. (2 marks) (c) Determine the probability that a randomly selected element will have a lifetime (i) of less than 433 hours. (1 mark) (ii) of more than 510 hours. (1 mark) (iii) within 25 hours of the mean lifetime. (2 marks) Solution 95% Specific behaviours  correct percentage Solution 𝑧𝑧= 433 −455 32 = −0.6875 Specific behaviours  correct method  correct score Solution 𝑃𝑃= 0.246 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃𝑃= 0.043 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 455 ± 25 = [430, 480] 𝑃𝑃= 0.565 Specific behaviours  correct bounds  correct probability",
