    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-143-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (8 marks) Three small huts lie on level ground. Hut 𝐵𝐵 lies 450 m due north of hut 𝐴𝐴 and hut 𝐶𝐶 lies 570 m from hut 𝐴𝐴 on a bearing of 125°. (a) Sketch a diagram to show this information. (2 marks) (b) The huts are equipped with radios that have a range of 800 m. Showing use of trigonometry, determine whether huts 𝐵𝐵 and 𝐶𝐶 can communicate by radio. (3 marks) (c) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the bearing of hut 𝐶𝐶 from hut 𝐵𝐵. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1 AND 2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-143-4 Question 17 (8 marks) Three small huts lie on level ground. Hut 𝐵𝐵 lies 450 m due north of hut 𝐴𝐴 and hut 𝐶𝐶 lies 570 m from hut 𝐴𝐴 on a bearing of 125°. (a) Sketch a diagram to show this information. (2 marks) (b) The huts are equipped with radios that have a range of 800 m. Showing use of trigonometry, determine whether huts 𝐵𝐵 and 𝐶𝐶 can communicate by radio. (3 marks) (c) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the bearing of hut 𝐶𝐶 from hut 𝐵𝐵. (3 marks) Solution 𝐵𝐵𝐶𝐶2 = 4502 + 5702 −2(450)(570) cos 125° 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 906 m No, cannot communicate as huts are more than 800 m apart. Specific behaviours  substitutes into cosine rule  calculates distance apart  states huts cannot communicate Solution 906 sin 125° = 570 sin𝐵𝐵 ∠𝐵𝐵= 31° Bearing is 180 −31 = 149° Specific behaviours  substitutes into sine rule  calculates angle  correct bearing Solution Specific behaviours  triangle roughly to scale  correct measurements",
