    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 3 (7 marks) (a) Construct the graph of 𝑥𝑥+ 2𝑦𝑦= 4 on the axes below. (3 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏 is shown at right. (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (2 marks) (ii) State with justification whether the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏 passes through the point with coordinates (30, 16). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-3 Question 3 (7 marks) (a) Construct the graph of 𝑥𝑥+ 2𝑦𝑦= 4 on the axes below. (3 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏 is shown at right. (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (2 marks) (ii) State with justification whether the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏 passes through the point with coordinates (30, 16). (2 marks) Solution 𝑦𝑦= −1 + 1 2 (30) = 14 No, does not pass through the point as when 𝑥𝑥= 30, 𝑦𝑦 should be 14, not 16, to lie on the line. Specific behaviours  states no  justifies using coordinates Solution See graph Specific behaviours  𝑥𝑥-intercept  𝑦𝑦-intercept  straight-line Solution 𝑎𝑎= −1, 𝑏𝑏= 1 2 = 0.5 Specific behaviours  correct value of 𝑎𝑎  correct value of 𝑏𝑏",
