    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN104-163-3 Question 4 (8 marks) (a) A mixture of linear and non-linear equations are shown below. Using a pencil, draw a circle around each linear equation. (2 marks) 2𝑥𝑥= 9, 𝑥𝑥2 = 9, 2(𝑥𝑥+ 1) = 3𝑥𝑥, 3𝑥𝑥= 2(𝑥𝑥+ 1), 𝑥𝑥−2 = 5𝑥𝑥. (b) Solve the equation 2(2𝑥𝑥+ 3) −5 = 3 −3(3 −𝑥𝑥) for 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (c) Ana, Bo and Cole are reading the same book. Ana has read 𝑥𝑥 pages, Bo has read 30 more pages than Ana and Cole has read twice as many pages as Bo. The mean number of pages read by the three friends is 42. (i) Use the above information to write an equation in terms of 𝑥𝑥. (2 marks) (ii) Determine how many pages of the book Ana has read. (2 marks) Solution Circles around equations 1, 4, 5. Specific behaviours  - subtract one  each error or omission Solution 4𝑥𝑥+ 6 −5 = 3 −9 + 3𝑥𝑥 𝑥𝑥= −7 Specific behaviours  correctly expands both sides  correct solution Solution Bo has read 𝑥𝑥+ 30 pages and Cole has read 2(𝑥𝑥+ 30) pages. Hence: 𝑥𝑥+ 𝑥𝑥+ 30 + 2(𝑥𝑥+ 30) 3 = 42 Specific behaviours  expressions for Bo and Cole in terms of 𝑥𝑥  equation using mean Solution 2𝑥𝑥+ 30 + 2𝑥𝑥+ 60 = 3 × 42 = 126 4𝑥𝑥= 36 𝑥𝑥= 9 Ana has read 9 pages. Specific be",
