    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN104-163-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (6 marks) (a) A formula used to estimate the speed, 𝑆𝑆 km per hour, of a car that skids to a halt is shown below. It uses the length of the skid 𝑑𝑑 m and the friction coefficient 𝑓𝑓 that varies with the type of road and weather. 𝑆𝑆= 3.5ඥ10𝑓𝑓𝑓𝑓 𝑓𝑓 Road Type Wet Dry Bitumen 0.50 0.90 Concrete 0.45 0.85 Unsealed 0.35 0.60 Estimate the speed of a car that skidded to a halt over a distance of 13.5 m on a dry unsealed road. (3 marks) (b) In baseball statistics, slugging average 𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆 is a measure of the batting productivity of a hitter. It is calculated from the number of singles 𝑆𝑆, doubles 𝐷𝐷, triples 𝑇𝑇, home runs 𝐻𝐻 and at bats 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 using the formula 𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆= 𝑆𝑆+ 2𝐷𝐷+ 3𝑇𝑇+ 4𝐻𝐻 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 A hitter who had been at bat 40 times had a slugging average of 0.4. Given that they had hit one home run, one triple, and five singles, determine their number of doubles. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN104-163-3 Question 8 (6 marks) (a) A formula used to estimate the speed, 𝑆𝑆 km per hour, of a car that skids to a halt is shown below. It uses the length of the skid 𝑑𝑑 m and the friction coefficient 𝑓𝑓 that varies with the type of road and weather. 𝑆𝑆= 3.5ඥ10𝑓𝑓𝑓𝑓 𝑓𝑓 Road Type Wet Dry Bitumen 0.50 0.90 Concrete 0.45 0.85 Unsealed 0.35 0.60 Estimate the speed of a car that skidded to a halt over a distance of 13.5 m on a dry unsealed road. (3 marks) (b) In baseball statistics, slugging average 𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆 is a measure of the batting productivity of a hitter. It is calculated from the number of singles 𝑆𝑆, doubles 𝐷𝐷, triples 𝑇𝑇, home runs 𝐻𝐻 and at bats 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 using the formula 𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆= 𝑆𝑆+ 2𝐷𝐷+ 3𝑇𝑇+ 4𝐻𝐻 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 A hitter who had been at bat 40 times had a slugging average of 0.4. Given that they had hit one home run, one triple, and five singles, determine their number of doubles. (3 marks) Solution 0.4 = 5 + 2𝑥𝑥+ 3(1) + 4(1) 40 0.4 × 40 = 2𝑥𝑥+ 12 2𝑥𝑥= 16 −12 𝑥𝑥= 2 They hit 2 doubles. Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly  shows at least two correct steps to simplify  correct number Solution 𝑆𝑆= 3.5√10 × 0.60 × 13.5 = 3.5√81 ",
