    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-163-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (8 marks) The plan shown below on 2 mm grid paper is a 1: 50 scale drawing of a concrete slab. (a) Show that the length of the slab edge 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is 6 m and calculate the length of the slab edge 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (2 marks) (b) When marking out the slab, a builder measures some of the diagonals to check that the corners are square. Determine the length that diagonal 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 should measure. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-163-4 Question 12 (8 marks) The plan shown below on 2 mm grid paper is a 1: 50 scale drawing of a concrete slab. (a) Show that the length of the slab edge 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is 6 m and calculate the length of the slab edge 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (2 marks) (b) When marking out the slab, a builder measures some of the diagonals to check that the corners are square. Determine the length that diagonal 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 should measure. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐶𝐶2 = 62 + 2.22 = 40.84 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 6.39 m Specific behaviours  indicates use of Pythagoras' Theorem  correct length, with units Solution Plan length 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 12 cm and so actual length is 0.12 × 50 = 6 m. Plan length 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 4.4 cm and so actual length is 0.044 × 50 = 2.2 m. Specific behaviours  indicates use of plan length and scale for 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴  correct length 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵",
