    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (7 marks) A water trough can be made from half of a cylindrical oil drum, as shown. Oil drum 𝑃𝑃 has a radius of 18 cm and a height of 55 cm. (a) The interior of the trough made from the oil drum 𝑃𝑃 is to be painted with a waterproofing paint. Calculate the area to be painted, rounded to the nearest 10 square centimetres. (3 marks) Oil drum 𝑄𝑄 is a similar figure to oil drum 𝑃𝑃 but with a height of 77 cm. (b) Obtain a scale factor for the size of the drum 𝑄𝑄 relative to the drum 𝑃𝑃. (2 marks) (c) Determine the capacity of a water trough made from drum 𝑄𝑄, given that the capacity of the trough made from the drum 𝑃𝑃 is 28 L. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-4 Question 15 (7 marks) A water trough can be made from half of a cylindrical oil drum, as shown. Oil drum 𝑃𝑃 has a radius of 18 cm and a height of 55 cm. (a) The interior of the trough made from the oil drum 𝑃𝑃 is to be painted with a waterproofing paint. Calculate the area to be painted, rounded to the nearest 10 square centimetres. (3 marks) Oil drum 𝑄𝑄 is a similar figure to oil drum 𝑃𝑃 but with a height of 77 cm. (b) Obtain a scale factor for the size of the drum 𝑄𝑄 relative to the drum 𝑃𝑃. (2 marks) (c) Determine the capacity of a water trough made from drum 𝑄𝑄, given that the capacity of the trough made from the drum 𝑃𝑃 is 28 L. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶= 2𝜋𝜋(18)(55) + 2𝜋𝜋(18)2 = 8256.1 cm2 𝐴𝐴Paint = 8256.1 ÷ 2 = 4128 ≈4130 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct use of cylinder SA formula  correct area of cylinder  correct area to be painted, rounded as required Solution 𝑆𝑆𝑆𝑆= 77 ÷ 55 = 1.4 Specific behaviours  uses heights  correct scale factor Solution 𝐶𝐶𝑄𝑄= 28 × 1.43 ≈76.8 L Specific behaviours  uses cube of scale factor  correct capacity",
