    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-163-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (8 marks) (a) A borrower secures a short term loan for an amount of $2 350 for 28 days at a simple interest rate of 12.97% pa. Determine the amount that must be repaid. (3 marks) (b) Another borrower is considering a loan of $18 500 for 3 years to use as part payment for a car. The car dealership offer the borrower a loan at 7.94% pa compounded monthly. The borrowers bank offer a loan at 8.19% pa compounded annually. Determine which loan will be cheaper for borrower to repay at the end of the 3 year period and state how much they save compared to the other loan. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-163-4 Question 16 (8 marks) (a) A borrower secures a short term loan for an amount of $2 350 for 28 days at a simple interest rate of 12.97% pa. Determine the amount that must be repaid. (3 marks) (b) Another borrower is considering a loan of $18 500 for 3 years to use as part payment for a car. The car dealership offer the borrower a loan at 7.94% pa compounded monthly. The borrowers bank offer a loan at 8.19% pa compounded annually. Determine which loan will be cheaper for borrower to repay at the end of the 3 year period and state how much they save compared to the other loan. (5 marks) Solution Car dealer: 𝐴𝐴= 18500 ൬1 + 7.94 12 × 100൰ 12×3 = $23 457.40 Bank: 𝐴𝐴= 18500 ൬1 + 8.19 100൰ 3 = $23 427.89 Difference: 23457.40 −23427.89 = $29.51 The bank loan will be cheaper by $29.51. Specific behaviours  uses compound interest formula for dealer, adjusted for monthly  correct amount to repay to dealer  uses compound interest formula for bank  correct amount to repay to bank  states cheaper loan and saving Solution 𝐼𝐼= 2350 × 12.97 100 × 28 365 = $23.38 Repayment = 2350 + 23.38 = $2373.38 Specific behaviours  uses ",
