    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (7 marks) Police in a city have detected that a mobile phone lies within a triangle bounded by three phone towers 𝑃𝑃, 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑅𝑅 where tower 𝑅𝑅 lies due east of tower 𝑃𝑃 and tower 𝑄𝑄 is the most northerly tower. The distances 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃, 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄 and 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃 are 650, 540 and 810 metres respectively. (a) Use Heron's rule to determine the area of the triangle within which the phone has been located. (3 marks) (b) Determine the bearing of tower 𝑄𝑄 from tower 𝑃𝑃 to the nearest degree. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN104-163-4 Question 17 (7 marks) Police in a city have detected that a mobile phone lies within a triangle bounded by three phone towers 𝑃𝑃, 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑅𝑅 where tower 𝑅𝑅 lies due east of tower 𝑃𝑃 and tower 𝑄𝑄 is the most northerly tower. The distances 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃, 𝑄𝑄𝑄𝑄 and 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃 are 650, 540 and 810 metres respectively. (a) Use Heron's rule to determine the area of the triangle within which the phone has been located. (3 marks) (b) Determine the bearing of tower 𝑄𝑄 from tower 𝑃𝑃 to the nearest degree. (4 marks) Solution cos 𝑃𝑃= 6502 + 8102 −5402 2(650)(810) 𝑃𝑃≈42° Bearing = 90° −42° = 048° Specific behaviours  diagram, roughly to scale, 𝑅𝑅 east of 𝑃𝑃  correct use of cosine rule  angle 𝑃𝑃  correct bearing Solution 𝑠𝑠= 650 + 540 + 810 2 = 1000 𝐴𝐴= ඥ10002 + (1000 −650)2 + (1000 −540)2 + (1000 −810)2 = ඥ10002 + 3502 + 4602 + 1902 ≈174900 m2 Specific behaviours  semi-perimeter  substitutes correctly  correct area",
