    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN104-163-4 Question 20 (9 marks) A company fabricates cylindrical storage tanks. A thin rectangular sheet of steel 𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹 with 𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹= 4.97 m and 𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹= 2.40 m is cut into two rectangles along 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, where 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 1 2 𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹. Two circles of radius 1 2 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 and with centres 𝐺𝐺 and 𝐻𝐻 are cut out of the smaller rectangle for the ends of the cylinder. The remaining rectangle 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is then rolled up and edge 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is welded to edge 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 to form the wall of the cylinder. Finally, the circular ends are welded in place. (a) Determine the area of the sheet 𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹𝐹 that is not used in the fabrication of a tank. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 1.2 × 2.4 = 2.88 m2 𝐴𝐴𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶𝐶= 𝜋𝜋(0.6)2 = 1.131 m2 𝐴𝐴𝑁𝑁𝑁𝑁𝑁𝑁 𝑈𝑈𝑈𝑈𝑈𝑈𝑈𝑈= 2.88 −2(1.131) = 0.618 m2 Specific behaviours  area of rectangle  area of circle  area not used",
