    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN104-163-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 21 (8 marks) A triangular logo 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is to be mounted at the entrance to a company. Δ𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is split into two smaller triangles by line 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 that bisects ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, as shown in the sketch. Δ𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is coloured red and Δ𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is grey. The length of 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is 44 cm, ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 33° and ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 51°. (a) Determine the length of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (3 marks) (c) Determine what percentage of the logo is coloured red. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN104-163-4 Question 21 (8 marks) A triangular logo 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is to be mounted at the entrance to a company. Δ𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is split into two smaller triangles by line 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 that bisects ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, as shown in the sketch. Δ𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is coloured red and Δ𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is grey. The length of 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is 44 cm, ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 33° and ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 51°. (a) Determine the length of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (3 marks) (c) Determine what percentage of the logo is coloured red. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 sin51° = 44 sin 33° 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 62.8 cm Specific behaviours  correct use of sin rule  correct length Solution 2𝜃𝜃= 180° −33° −51° = 96° ⇒𝜃𝜃= 48° ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 180° −51° −48° = 81° 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 sin51° = 44 sin81° 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 34.6 cm Specific behaviours  calculates 𝜃𝜃  correct use of sin rule  correct length Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 0.5(62.8)(44) sin 96° = 1374 cm2 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 0.5(62.8)(34.6) sin48° = 808 cm2 % red = 808 1374 × 100 ≈59% Specific behaviours  area of whole  area of smaller triangle  correct percentage",
