    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) A fruit picker is paid 60 cents for each kilogram of cherries they pick, and a box of cherries contains 9 kg of the fruit. (a) Determine, in dollars, how much a picker is paid to pick one box of cherries. (2 marks) (b) Determine how much a picker earns in a day when they pick 40 boxes of cherries. (1 mark) (c) A picker worked for four days and earned a total of $660. Calculate how many kilograms of cherries they picked in this time. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-3 Section One: Calculator-free 35% (52 Marks) This section has eight questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 50 minutes. Question 1 (5 marks) A fruit picker is paid 60 cents for each kilogram of cherries they pick, and a box of cherries contains 9 kg of the fruit. (a) Determine, in dollars, how much a picker is paid to pick one box of cherries. (2 marks) (b) Determine how much a picker earns in a day when they pick 40 boxes of cherries. (1 mark) (c) A picker worked for four days and earned a total of $660. Calculate how many kilograms of cherries they picked in this time. (2 marks) Solution 60 ÷ 100 = $0.60 0.60 × 9 = $5.40 Specific behaviours  indicates correct calculation(s)  correctly evaluates Solution 5.40 × 40 = 5 × 40 + 0.4 × 40 = 200 + 16 = $216 Specific behaviours  correctly evaluates Solution 660 ÷ 0.6 = 6600 6 = 1100 kg Specific behaviours  indicates correct calculation  correct number of kilograms",
