    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 2 (6 marks) (a) The surface area 𝑆 of an object is given by 𝑆= 2(𝑤ℎ+ 𝑙ℎ+ 𝑤𝑙). Calculate the value of 𝑆 when ℎ= 8 cm, 𝑙= 4 cm and 𝑤= 0.5 cm. (2 marks) (b) The quantity Δ is calculated using the formula Δ = √𝑏2 −4𝑎𝑐. Calculate the value of Δ when 𝑎= 2, 𝑏= 7 and 𝑐= 3. (2 marks) (c) Given that 𝑎2 −𝑏2 = (𝑎+ 𝑏)(𝑎−𝑏), evaluate 422 −322. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-3 Question 2 (6 marks) (a) The surface area 𝑆 of an object is given by 𝑆= 2(𝑤ℎ+ 𝑙ℎ+ 𝑤𝑙). Calculate the value of 𝑆 when ℎ= 8 cm, 𝑙= 4 cm and 𝑤= 0.5 cm. (2 marks) (b) The quantity Δ is calculated using the formula Δ = √𝑏2 −4𝑎𝑐. Calculate the value of Δ when 𝑎= 2, 𝑏= 7 and 𝑐= 3. (2 marks) (c) Given that 𝑎2 −𝑏2 = (𝑎+ 𝑏)(𝑎−𝑏), evaluate 422 −322. (2 marks) Solution 422 −322 = (42 + 32)(42 −32) = (74)(10) = 740 Specific behaviours  expresses as sum and difference  correct value Solution 𝑆= 2(0.5 × 8 + 4 × 8 + 0.5 × 4) = 2(4 + 32 + 2) = 2 × 38 = 76 cm2 Specific behaviours  simplifies three terms in brackets  sums terms and doubles Solution Δ = √72 −4 × 2 × 3 = √49 −24 = √25 = 5 Specific behaviours  simplifies two terms in roots  calculates difference and takes root",
