    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 3 (6 marks) The weights in kilograms of the 10 members of basketball squad P are shown below. The standard deviation of these weights is 6.3 kg. 79, 81, 73, 67, 62, 78, 73, 68, 77, 82. (a) Determine the mean weight of the members of squad P. (2 marks) Basketball squad Q also has 10 members. The mean and standard deviation of the weights of the members of this squad are 77 and 7.9 kg respectively. (b) Write a statement, with reasoning, that compares the variation in weights of the members of the two squads. (2 marks) (c) Write a statement, with reasoning, that compares the weights of the members of the two squads. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 5 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-3 Question 3 (6 marks) The weights in kilograms of the 10 members of basketball squad P are shown below. The standard deviation of these weights is 6.3 kg. 79, 81, 73, 67, 62, 78, 73, 68, 77, 82. (a) Determine the mean weight of the members of squad P. (2 marks) Basketball squad Q also has 10 members. The mean and standard deviation of the weights of the members of this squad are 77 and 7.9 kg respectively. (b) Write a statement, with reasoning, that compares the variation in weights of the members of the two squads. (2 marks) (c) Write a statement, with reasoning, that compares the weights of the members of the two squads. (2 marks) Solution Σ𝑥= 740 𝑥̅ = 740 ÷ 10 = 74 kg Specific behaviours  correctly adds the weights  calculates mean Solution The standard deviation for squad P is lower than for squad Q, since 6.3 < 7.9. Hence there is less variation in weight amongst the members of squad P compared to squad Q. Specific behaviours  compares standard deviations  indicates lower sd means less variation Solution The mean of squad P is lower than squad Q, since 74 < 77. Hence the members of squad P tend to be lighter",
