    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 4 (6 marks) The annual cost of water, $𝐶, varies with 𝑥, the total number of kilolitres of water used by a household in a year, as shown in the graph below. (a) Determine the cost of water for a household that used 275 kL in a year. (1 mark) (b) Calculate the slope of the line between (145, 250) and (245, 600) and interpret, in context, this slope. (3 marks) (c) Describe how the slope of the piecewise graph changes as the yearly household water use increases and suggest, in context, a reason for this change. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-3 Question 4 (6 marks) The annual cost of water, $𝐶, varies with 𝑥, the total number of kilolitres of water used by a household in a year, as shown in the graph below. (a) Determine the cost of water for a household that used 275 kL in a year. (1 mark) (b) Calculate the slope of the line between (145, 250) and (245, 600) and interpret, in context, this slope. (3 marks) (c) Describe how the slope of the piecewise graph changes as the yearly household water use increases and suggest, in context, a reason for this change. (2 marks) Solution Any cost between $740 and $760 Specific behaviours  cost within given range Solution 𝑚= 600 −250 245 −145 = 350 100 = 3.5 Each kilolitre of water in this interval costs $3.50. Specific behaviours  appropriate use of slope formula  correct slope  reasonable interpretation Solution As water use increases, so the slope of each part of the graph increases. Reason: To discourage excessive use, households that use the most water will pay more per kL than households who use less water. Specific behaviours  describes change  any plausible reason",
