    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 5 (7 marks) Let 𝑷= [ 1 2 −3 −2] and 𝑸= [ 2 1 −4 3]. (a) Express 𝑷+ 2𝑸 as a single matrix. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the matrix 𝑷× 𝑸. (2 marks) (c) Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐 given the matrix equation 𝑎[2 5 −3 3 1 𝑏] + [1 −1 4 3 5 3] = [−1 𝑐 7 0 4 1]. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 7 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-3 Question 5 (7 marks) Let 𝑷= [ 1 2 −3 −2] and 𝑸= [ 2 1 −4 3]. (a) Express 𝑷+ 2𝑸 as a single matrix. (2 marks) (b) Calculate the matrix 𝑷× 𝑸. (2 marks) (c) Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐 given the matrix equation 𝑎[2 5 −3 3 1 𝑏] + [1 −1 4 3 5 3] = [−1 𝑐 7 0 4 1]. (3 marks) Solution 𝑷+ 2𝑸= [ 1 2 −3 −2] + 2 [ 2 1 −4 3] = [ 1 2 −3 −2] + [ 4 2 −8 6] = [ 5 4 −11 4] Specific behaviours  correct multiple  correct sum Solution Using top left elements: 2𝑎+ 1 = −1 →2𝑎= −2 →𝑎= −1 Using bottom right elements: −𝑏+ 3 = 1 →𝑏= 2 Using top centre elements: −5 −1 = 𝑐→𝑐= −6 𝑎= −1, 𝑏= 2, 𝑐= −6 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑎  value of 𝑏  value of 𝑐 Solution 𝑷× 𝑸= [ 1 2 −3 −2] × [ 2 1 −4 3] = [−6 7 2 −9] Specific behaviours  at least two elements correct  correct result",
