    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 6 (7 marks) (a) The area of a trapezium can be calculated using the formula shown below. 𝐴= ℎ 2 (𝑎+ 𝑏) Determine the value of 𝑎 when 𝐴= 75, ℎ= 5 and 𝑏= 17. (3 marks) (b) To hire a scooter from company A, a customer is charged a fee of $8 plus $5 per hour, but to hire one from company B, they are charged a fee of $10.50 plus $3 per hour. Ben hires four scooters from company B and Aida hires three scooters from company A. If they both hire the scooters for the same length of time, 𝑥 hours, and their bills are the same, use the above information to write an equation and hence determine the value of 𝑥. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 8 CALCULATOR-FREE See next page SN153-183-3 Question 6 (7 marks) (a) The area of a trapezium can be calculated using the formula shown below. 𝐴= ℎ 2 (𝑎+ 𝑏) Determine the value of 𝑎 when 𝐴= 75, ℎ= 5 and 𝑏= 17. (3 marks) (b) To hire a scooter from company A, a customer is charged a fee of $8 plus $5 per hour, but to hire one from company B, they are charged a fee of $10.50 plus $3 per hour. Ben hires four scooters from company B and Aida hires three scooters from company A. If they both hire the scooters for the same length of time, 𝑥 hours, and their bills are the same, use the above information to write an equation and hence determine the value of 𝑥. (4 marks) Solution 4(10.50 + 3𝑥) = 3(8 + 5𝑥) 42 + 12𝑥= 24 + 15𝑥 18 = 3𝑥 𝑥= 6 Specific behaviours  one correct expression for cost  equates both cost expressions  expands at least one side correctly  correct value of 𝑥 Solution 75 = 5 2 (𝑎+ 17) 150 = 5(𝑎+ 17) 30 = 𝑎+ 17 𝑎= 13 Specific behaviours  substitutes  one correct step to simplify  correct value",
