    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 7 (7 marks) Water is pumped into a storage tank. The table below shows the depth of water, 𝑦 cm, in the tank after the pump has been running for 𝑥 minutes. 𝑥 1 2 3 4 𝑦 7 11 15 19 (a) Plot these points on the axes below. (1 mark) (b) What feature of the graph in part (a) suggests a linear formula relates 𝑥 and 𝑦? (1 mark) (c) The formula 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥+ 𝑏 relates the depth of water to the time. Determine the value of the constant 𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏. (2 marks) (d) Determine the depth of water in the tank after 15 minutes. (1 mark) (e) Determine the time required for the depth of water in the tank to reach 91 cm. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-FREE 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-3 Question 7 (7 marks) Water is pumped into a storage tank. The table below shows the depth of water, 𝑦 cm, in the tank after the pump has been running for 𝑥 minutes. 𝑥 1 2 3 4 𝑦 7 11 15 19 (a) Plot these points on the axes below. (1 mark) (b) What feature of the graph in part (a) suggests a linear formula relates 𝑥 and 𝑦? (1 mark) (c) The formula 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥+ 𝑏 relates the depth of water to the time. Determine the value of the constant 𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏. (2 marks) (d) Determine the depth of water in the tank after 15 minutes. (1 mark) (e) Determine the time required for the depth of water in the tank to reach 91 cm. (2 marks) Solution All points on the graph lie in a straight line. Specific behaviours  identifies feature of graph Solution 𝑦= 4(15) + 3 = 60 + 3 = 63 cm Specific behaviours  correct depth using values from (c) Solution 91 = 4𝑥+ 3 88 = 4𝑥 𝑥= 88 4 = 22 min Specific behaviours  substitutes into relation  solves for 𝑥 Solution Gradient: 𝑎= 4 Axis-intercept: 𝑏= 3 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑎  value of 𝑏 Solution See graph Specific behaviours  plots all points (Ignore any line)",
