    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) An isosceles triangle has two sides of length 6.8 cm and a base of length 11 cm. Sketch this triangle and hence determine the angle between the base and one of the sides. (3 marks) (b) Clearly show use of Heron's rule to determine the area of a triangle that has sides of length 16 cm, 23.1 cm and 28.1 cm. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-4 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) An isosceles triangle has two sides of length 6.8 cm and a base of length 11 cm. Sketch this triangle and hence determine the angle between the base and one of the sides. (3 marks) (b) Clearly show use of Heron's rule to determine the area of a triangle that has sides of length 16 cm, 23.1 cm and 28.1 cm. (3 marks) Solution 𝑠= 14 + 17.1 + 22.1 2 = 33.6 𝐴= √33.6(26.6 −14)(33.6 −17.1)(33.6 −22.1) = √33.6 × 17.6 × 10.5 × 5.5 = 184.8 cm2 Specific behaviours  calculates semi-perimeter  substitutes correctly  calculates area Solution cos 𝑥= 5.5 6.8 OR cos 𝑥= 6.82 + 112 −6.82 2(6.8)(11) 𝑥= 36.0° Specific behaviours  sketch, indicates required angle  indicates expression for cosine of angle  correct angle",
