    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (5 marks) (a) The length of a hallway in an office is 8.4 metres. On a scale drawing of the office, the hallway has a length of 70 mm. Determine the scale used to make the drawing. Give your answer in the form 1: 𝑛, where 𝑛 is a whole number. (2 marks) (b) A plan for an area outside the office is drawn to a scale of 1: 200, and on this plan, a rectangular courtyard is 4.8 cm wide and 11.4 cm long. If this courtyard is paved with square pavers measuring 30 × 30 cm, determine how many pavers it contains. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-4 Question 10 (5 marks) (a) The length of a hallway in an office is 8.4 metres. On a scale drawing of the office, the hallway has a length of 70 mm. Determine the scale used to make the drawing. Give your answer in the form 1: 𝑛, where 𝑛 is a whole number. (2 marks) (b) A plan for an area outside the office is drawn to a scale of 1: 200, and on this plan, a rectangular courtyard is 4.8 cm wide and 11.4 cm long. If this courtyard is paved with square pavers measuring 30 × 30 cm, determine how many pavers it contains. (3 marks) Solution 𝑤= 4.8 × 200 = 960 cm 𝑙= 11.4 × 200 = 2280 cm 960 ÷ 30 = 32 pavers wide 2280 ÷ 30 = 76 pavers long 32 × 76 = 2432 pavers were used. Specific behaviours  uses scale correctly  indicates appropriate method  correct number of pavers Solution 70 mm: 8.4 m 70: 8400 1: 120 Specific behaviours  ratio, using same units  ratio in required form",
