    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (10 marks) A class of students sat a general knowledge quiz that had 25 multiple choice questions, each with one correct answer. The score of each student in the quiz is shown in the dot plot below. (a) State the number of students in the class. (1 mark) (b) Name the statistical variable shown in the dot plot and classify this variable as ordinal, nominal, discrete or continuous. (2 marks) (c) Represent the data from the dot plot as a box plot on the axes below. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-4 Question 12 (10 marks) A class of students sat a general knowledge quiz that had 25 multiple choice questions, each with one correct answer. The score of each student in the quiz is shown in the dot plot below. (a) State the number of students in the class. (1 mark) (b) Name the statistical variable shown in the dot plot and classify this variable as ordinal, nominal, discrete or continuous. (2 marks) (c) Represent the data from the dot plot as a box plot on the axes below. (4 marks) Solution 20 students. Specific behaviours  correct number Solution Variable is score. Classification is discrete. Specific behaviours  correct variable  correct classification Solution Minimum is 4 and maximum is 24. Median is 10. 𝑄1 is is 7.5 and 𝑄3 is 14. Specific behaviours  indicates correct minimum and maximum  indicates correct median  indicates correct quartiles  uses values to draw box plot neatly",
