    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (d) State the interquartile range for this data and use it in a calculation to determine whether the highest score can be classified as an outlier. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-4 (d) State the interquartile range for this data and use it in a calculation to determine whether the highest score can be classified as an outlier. (3 marks) Solution 𝐼𝑄𝑅= 14 −7.5 = 6.5 𝑄3 + 1.5 × 𝐼𝑄𝑅= 14 + 1.5 × 6.5 = 14 + 9.75 = 23.75 Hence any score above 23.75 is an outlier, and so the highest score in the dataset of 24 is an outlier. Specific behaviours  correct IQR  calculates 𝑄3 + 1.5 × 𝐼𝑄𝑅  reasons that highest score is an outlier",
