    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 14 (7 marks) The shape of a metal reinforcing plate is a parallelogram with a sector of a circle removed, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). The acute angle between the sides of 75 cm and 58 cm is 45°, and the radius of the sector removed is 32 cm. (a) Show that the perpendicular distance ℎ between the two long sides is 41 cm. (1 mark) (b) Determine the area of the sector removed from the parallelogram. (2 marks) (c) Determine the area of the metal plate. (2 marks) (d) Every edge of the plate is welded to the main structure. Determine the total length of the five edges of the plate. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN153-183-4 Question 14 (7 marks) The shape of a metal reinforcing plate is a parallelogram with a sector of a circle removed, as shown in the diagram (not to scale). The acute angle between the sides of 75 cm and 58 cm is 45°, and the radius of the sector removed is 32 cm. (a) Show that the perpendicular distance ℎ between the two long sides is 41 cm. (1 mark) (b) Determine the area of the sector removed from the parallelogram. (2 marks) (c) Determine the area of the metal plate. (2 marks) (d) Every edge of the plate is welded to the main structure. Determine the total length of the five edges of the plate. (2 marks) Solution ℎ= 58 × sin(45°) = 41.0 cm Specific behaviours  shows correct trig expression Solution Parallelogram area: 𝐴= 75 × 41 = 3075 Area of plate: 𝐴= 3075 −402 = 2673 cm2 Specific behaviours  area of parallelogram  area of plate Solution 𝐴= 45 360 × 𝜋× 322 = 402 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct fraction of circle  calculates area Solution Curved edge: 𝐿= 45 360 × 2𝜋× 32 = 25.1 Total length: 𝐿= 25 + 2 × 75 + 2 × 58 −2 × 32 = 227 cm Specific behaviours  length of curved edge  calculates total l",
