    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-4 Question 17 (10 marks) The retirement ages of a group of 80 people is summarised in the following table. (a) A student looked at the above data and stated that the oldest person of the group who retired was aged 72. Comment on the validity of this statement. (2 marks) (b) Use the mid-point of each class interval to determine the mean and standard deviation of the retirement ages. (2 marks) (c) Construct a histogram of the retirement ages on the axes below. (2 marks) Age (𝑡 years) Frequency 𝑓 48 < 𝑡≤51 1 51 < 𝑡≤54 0 54 < 𝑡≤57 2 57 < 𝑡≤60 5 60 < 𝑡≤63 16 63 < 𝑡≤66 28 66 < 𝑡≤69 23 69 < 𝑡≤72 5 Solution Statement is not valid. The summary shows that 5 people aged from 69 to 72 retired and it is quite possible that none of these were actually aged 72. Specific behaviours  states not a valid statement  reasonable explanation Solution 𝑡̅ = 64.35 y sd = 3.70 y Specific behaviours  mean  standard deviation Solution See graph Specific behaviours  all frequencies correct  all edges straight and neat",
