    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 18 (8 marks) A solid cone has a radius of 9.1 cm and a perpendicular height of 6 cm. (a) Determine the slant height of the cone and hence its total surface area. (3 marks) The cone is placed inside a hollow cylinder of radius 9.1 cm and height 8.8 cm as shown in the diagram (not to scale), and the remaining space inside the cylinder filled with liquid. (b) Determine the volume of liquid that is required, rounding your answer to the nearest 10 cm3. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-4 Question 18 (8 marks) A solid cone has a radius of 9.1 cm and a perpendicular height of 6 cm. (a) Determine the slant height of the cone and hence its total surface area. (3 marks) The cone is placed inside a hollow cylinder of radius 9.1 cm and height 8.8 cm as shown in the diagram (not to scale), and the remaining space inside the cylinder filled with liquid. (b) Determine the volume of liquid that is required, rounding your answer to the nearest 10 cm3. (5 marks) Solution 𝑉𝐶𝑂𝑁𝐸= 1 3 𝜋(9.1)2(6) = 520 𝑉𝐶𝑌𝐿= 𝜋(9.1)2(8.8) = 2289 𝑉𝐿= 2289 −520 = 1769 ≈1770 cm3 Specific behaviours  substitutes into expressions for cone and cylinder volume  evaluates cone volume  evaluates cylinder volume  evaluates volume of liquid  rounds as required, stating units Solution 𝑠= √9.12 + 62 = 10.9 cm 𝐴= 𝜋(9.1)(10.9) + 𝜋(9.1)2 = 311.6 + 260.2 = 572 cm2 Specific behaviours  calculates slant height  calculates curved surface area  calculates total surface area",
