    "questionText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 20 (8 marks) The temperatures of component A and component B in a heat exchanger vary in a linear fashion as shown in the graph below, where 𝑦 is the temperature in °𝐶, after 𝑥 minutes. (a) Determine a rule for the temperature of component A in terms of 𝑥. (3 marks) (b) Explaining your method, determine when both components are at the same temperature, and state what this temperature is. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "APPLICATIONS UNITS 1&2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN153-183-4 Question 20 (8 marks) The temperatures of component A and component B in a heat exchanger vary in a linear fashion as shown in the graph below, where 𝑦 is the temperature in °𝐶, after 𝑥 minutes. (a) Determine a rule for the temperature of component A in terms of 𝑥. (3 marks) (b) Explaining your method, determine when both components are at the same temperature, and state what this temperature is. (5 marks) Solution Require equation for component B: 𝑚= 30 ÷ 10 = 3 𝑐= −30 𝑦= 3𝑥−30 Now use calculator to graph both lines and find point of intersection at (16.4, 19.2). Hence components reach the same temperature of 19.2 °𝐶 after 16.4 minutes. Specific behaviours  correct gradient for line B  writes rule for B  states time  states temperature  explains method throughout Solution 𝑚= −52 ÷ 26 = −2 𝑐= 52 𝑦= −2𝑥+ 52 Specific behaviours  correct gradient  correct intercept  writes rule for 𝑦",
